window.CARDS=window.CARDS||{};CARDS["people-horikita-suzune"]=[{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v1-p16-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"action spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune classroom coercion  ch 2 opening  present late may  class 1 d classroom after final bell  ayanokoji is feigning sleep  sleeping strategy  pondering society  horikita approaches his desk and stands over him like an intimidating presence  described as a  devil  to shostakovich s symphony no  11   ayanokouji kun  do you have a moment   if you do not awaken within three seconds  i will bestow additional punishment upon you   see  you are awake after all  aren t you   glad to hear it  well then  may i have a little of your time   well  even though you have no right to veto such a decision  i suppose i would be exceptionally displeased   and when i am displeased  then i will prove a major obstacle to your school life  ayanokouji kun  for example  i might set a great number of thumbtacks on your chair  or  when you go to the toilet  i might splash water on you from above  or stab you with the needle of my mathematical compass  those kinds of obstacles  i suppose   don t worry  that was only a joke  i wouldn t splash water on you from above   after his harassment protest   evidence   she asked   what about the evidence  did you decide i m the culprit without evidence   demands proof when accused of previously stabbing his arm with a drawing compass   ayanokouji kun  would you prefer to regret while you suffer or regret while you despair  which would you like more  because if you refuse me and force my hand  it will be your responsibility   all right  then  what am i supposed to do   agrees under duress  filled with trepidation  the narrative then flashes back two months to the entrance ceremony   the favor itself is named only later  at p 150   i need your help  ayanokouji kun  physical intimidation  stands directly over him  uses cold countdowns  completely denies physical violence  compass stab  on strict legalistic grounds  lack of evidence  dominant  uncompromising  highly articulate  ruthlessly practical  utilizes psychological pressure and legalistic deflection  formal  polite yet chillingly authoritative diction  keigo combined with overt threats   bestow additional punishment   prove a major obstacle to your school life   regret while you suffer  master slave   coerced partner dynamic  views him as someone she can leverage for assistance through relentless pressure  already comfortable threatening physical harm","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v1-p16-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Classroom coercion (Ch.2 opening, present late May)<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.16–18<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Class 1-D classroom after final bell. Ayanokōji is feigning sleep (&quot;Sleeping Strategy&quot;) pondering society. Horikita approaches his desk and stands over him like an intimidating presence (described as a &quot;devil&quot; to Shostakovich&#x27;s Symphony No. 11).<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Ayanokouji-kun, do you have a moment?”<span class=\"pg\">p.16<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“If you do not awaken within three seconds, I will bestow additional punishment upon you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.16<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“See, you are awake after all, aren’t you?”<span class=\"pg\">p.16<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>12 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Glad to hear it. Well then, may I have a little of your time?”<span class=\"pg\">p.16<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, even though you have no right to veto such a decision, I suppose I would be exceptionally displeased.”<span class=\"pg\">p.17<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “And when I am displeased, then I will prove a major obstacle to your school life, Ayanokouji-kun. For example, I might set a great number of thumbtacks on your chair. Or, when you go to the toilet, I might splash water on you from above. Or stab you with the needle of my mathematical compass. Those kinds of obstacles, I suppose.”<span class=\"pg\">p.17<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Don’t worry. That was only a joke. I wouldn’t splash water on you from above.” (after his harassment protest)<span class=\"pg\">p.17<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Evidence?” (she asked)<span class=\"pg\">p.17<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What about the evidence? Did you decide I’m the culprit without evidence?” (demands proof when accused of previously stabbing his arm with a drawing compass)<span class=\"pg\">p.17<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ayanokouji-kun. Would you prefer to regret while you suffer or regret while you despair? Which would you like more? Because if you refuse me and force my hand, it will be your responsibility.”<span class=\"pg\">p.17–18<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “All right, then. What am I supposed to do?” (agrees under duress, filled with trepidation; the narrative then flashes back two months to the entrance ceremony — the favor itself is named only later, at p.150: “I need your help, Ayanokouji-kun.”)<span class=\"pg\">p.18<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Physical intimidation; stands directly over him; uses cold countdowns; completely denies physical violence (compass stab) on strict legalistic grounds (lack of evidence).<span class=\"pg\">p.16–17<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Dominant, uncompromising, highly articulate, ruthlessly practical, utilizes psychological pressure and legalistic deflection.<span class=\"pg\">p.16–18<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Voice<\/span> Formal, polite yet chillingly authoritative diction (keigo combined with overt threats: &quot;bestow additional punishment&quot;, &quot;prove a major obstacle to your school life&quot;, &quot;regret while you suffer&quot;).<span class=\"pg\">p.16–18<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Master-slave / coerced partner dynamic; views him as someone she can leverage for assistance through relentless pressure; already comfortable threatening physical harm.<span class=\"pg\">p.16–18<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v1-p20-1\">→ After: Entrance ceremony bus &amp; rock gate confrontation (Ch.2 flashback, April)<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v1-p20-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"action spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune entrance ceremony bus   rock gate confrontation  ch 2 flashback  april  crowded city bus heading to anhs on entrance ceremony day  an elderly woman stands shaking in the aisle  kushida appeals to passengers  koenji haughtily refuses to yield his priority seat  sits beside ayanokoji near the elderly woman  unlike the hesitant or ignoring passengers  she remains completely stone faced and expressionless  completely immune to the surrounding emotional pressure  eyes lock with ayanokoji across the aisle for an instant  shared silent mutual recognition that neither sees any reason to sacrifice their seat  natural rock school gate outside anhs  as students disembark  horikita immediately intercepts ayanokoji before he enters  confronts him directly  narrows her sharp eyes in suspicion   wait   calls out to him as he approaches the gate   you were looking at me  why   she asked  narrowing her eyes   that s right  i didn t consider giving it up  is there something wrong with that   you dislike trouble  then i don t think you and i are anything alike  i didn t give up my seat because i thought it would be pointless  that s all   perhaps  i m simply acting according to my own beliefs  that s different from someone who just dislikes trouble  like you  i don t want to spend any time around people like you  principle driven individualism  fierce distinction between her rational convictions  pointless  and mere apathy  disliking trouble  openly hostile to people she deems weak willed or apathetic  mutual dismissal  establishes deep boundary  don t want to spend any time around people like you  walks off with identical mutual sigh","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v1-p20-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Entrance ceremony bus &amp; rock gate confrontation (Ch.2 flashback, April)<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.20–25<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Crowded city bus heading to ANHS on entrance ceremony day. An elderly woman stands shaking in the aisle. Kushida appeals to passengers; Kōenji haughtily refuses to yield his priority seat. Natural rock school gate outside ANHS. As students disembark, Horikita immediately intercepts Ayanokōji before he enters.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Wait!” (calls out to him as he approaches the gate)<span class=\"pg\">p.25<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“You were looking at me. Why?” (she asked, narrowing her eyes)<span class=\"pg\">p.25<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“That’s right. I didn’t consider giving it up. Is there something wrong with that?”<span class=\"pg\">p.25<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>7 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Sits beside Ayanokōji near the elderly woman. Unlike the hesitant or ignoring passengers, she remains completely stone-faced and expressionless, completely immune to the surrounding emotional pressure.<span class=\"pg\">p.24<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Eyes lock with Ayanokōji across the aisle for an instant; shared silent mutual recognition that neither sees any reason to sacrifice their seat.<span class=\"pg\">p.24<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Confronts him directly; narrows her sharp eyes in suspicion.<span class=\"pg\">p.25<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You dislike trouble? Then I don’t think you and I are anything alike. I didn’t give up my seat because I thought it would be pointless. That’s all.”<span class=\"pg\">p.25<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Perhaps. I’m simply acting according to my own beliefs. That’s different from someone who just dislikes trouble, like you. I don’t want to spend any time around people like you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.25<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Principle-driven individualism; fierce distinction between her rational convictions (&quot;pointless&quot;) and mere apathy (disliking trouble); openly hostile to people she deems weak-willed or apathetic.<span class=\"pg\">p.25<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Mutual dismissal; establishes deep boundary (&quot;don&#x27;t want to spend any time around people like you&quot;); walks off with identical mutual sigh.<span class=\"pg\">p.25<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v1-p16-1\">← Before: Classroom coercion (Ch.2 opening, present late May)<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v1-p27-1\">→ After: Classroom Day 1: assigned neighbors &amp; favor exchange<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v1-p27-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune classroom day 1  assigned neighbors   favor exchange class 1 d classroom before ceremony  horikita sits down at the desk directly to ayanokoji s left  window column  rear   that s quite a heavy sigh  considering the school year has only begun  meeting you again makes me want to sigh   you just went ahead and introduced yourself   do you mind if i refuse   she asked  when he introduces himself   you re a curious one  aren t you  you won t find talking to me very interesting  though   replies when ak asks if she has friends in another class or enrolled alone   i m horikita suzune   introduces herself only after sighing and changing her mind   spoken just like someone who avoids trouble  i don t think i could ever like such a person   her verdict on ak s self description  adds  i pray this will be my only upset  deeply guarded and transactional  refuses engagement outright  do you mind if i refuse  performs self introduction only under social pressure  and delivers a cutting verdict on ak s  avoids trouble  persona  openly states she doesn t want to spend time around people like him  clinical  dismissive boundary setting  wraps rejection in pseudo clinical judgments  spoken just like someone who avoids trouble  formally exchanges full names after visible reluctance  ends the exchange with mutual disdain  i don t want to spend any time around people like you     i feel the same way","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v1-p27-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Classroom Day 1: assigned neighbors &amp; favor exchange<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.27–29<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Class 1-D classroom before ceremony. Horikita sits down at the desk directly to Ayanokōji&#x27;s left (window column, rear).<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“That’s quite a heavy sigh, considering the school year has only begun. Meeting you again makes me want to sigh.”<span class=\"pg\">p.27<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“You just went ahead and introduced yourself?”<span class=\"pg\">p.28<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Do you mind if I refuse?” (she asked, when he introduces himself)<span class=\"pg\">p.28<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You’re a curious one, aren’t you? You won’t find talking to me very interesting, though.” (replies when AK asks if she has friends in another class or enrolled alone)<span class=\"pg\">p.28<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m Horikita Suzune.” (introduces herself only after sighing and changing her mind)<span class=\"pg\">p.28<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Spoken just like someone who avoids trouble. I don’t think I could ever like such a person,” (her verdict on AK’s self-description; adds “I pray this will be my only upset.”)<span class=\"pg\">p.29<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Deeply guarded and transactional; refuses engagement outright (“Do you mind if I refuse?”), performs self-introduction only under social pressure, and delivers a cutting verdict on AK’s “avoids trouble” persona; openly states she doesn’t want to spend time around people like him.<span class=\"pg\">p.28–29<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Voice<\/span> Clinical, dismissive boundary-setting; wraps rejection in pseudo-clinical judgments (“Spoken just like someone who avoids trouble”).<span class=\"pg\">p.29<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Formally exchanges full names after visible reluctance; ends the exchange with mutual disdain (“I don’t want to spend any time around people like you” / “I feel the same way”).<span class=\"pg\">p.28–29<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v1-p20-1\">← Before: Entrance ceremony bus &amp; rock gate confrontation (Ch.2 flashback, April)<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v1-p37-1\">→ After: Rejection of Hirata&#x27;s introductions<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v1-p37-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"action","w":"horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune rejection of hirata s introductions class 1 d classroom after chiyabashira leaves  hirata attempts class wide self introductions  when sudo and others rebel and storm out  horikita stands up from her desk without speaking a single word of introduction  she glances briefly at ayanokoji  sees he isn t moving  and walks straight out the classroom door  completely unbothered by collective class harmony  utter disregard for peer pressure  social cohesion  or performative harmony","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v1-p37-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Rejection of Hirata&#x27;s introductions<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.37<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Class 1-D classroom after Chiyabashira leaves. Hirata attempts class-wide self-introductions.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q action\">When Sudō and others rebel and storm out, Horikita stands up from her desk without speaking a single word of introduction. She glances briefly at Ayanokōji, sees he isn&#x27;t moving, and walks straight out the classroom door…<span class=\"pg\">p.37<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> When Sudō and others rebel and storm out, Horikita stands up from her desk without speaking a single word of introduction. She glances briefly at Ayanokōji, sees he isn&#x27;t moving, and walks straight out the classroom door, completely unbothered by collective class harmony.<span class=\"pg\">p.37<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Utter disregard for peer pressure, social cohesion, or performative harmony.<span class=\"pg\">p.37<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v1-p27-1\">← Before: Classroom Day 1: assigned neighbors &amp; favor exchange<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v1-p41-1\">→ After: Convenience store observation &amp; pushover lecture<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v1-p41-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"action spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune convenience store observation   pushover lecture campus convenience store on entrance afternoon  horikita stands reading a book in the aisle  dryly critiques ayanokoji s botched class introduction  notes his self introduction was painful to watch and achieved the exact opposite of making friends  stays quiet during sudo s altercation with the two mocking second years  observes ayanokoji stoop down and clean up sudo s spilled instant ramen cup from the floor outside the store  berates ayanokoji for his submissive nature  tells him cleaning up another student s mess makes him look like a hopeless pushover and doormat  critical of passivity  views unrewarded  self effacing kindness as weak and illogical  continued observation of his contradictory behavior  disdainful of his conflict averse actions while remaining tethered to his vicinity","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v1-p41-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Convenience store observation &amp; pushover lecture<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.41–45<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Campus convenience store on entrance afternoon. Horikita stands reading a book in the aisle.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">Dryly critiques Ayanokōji&#x27;s botched class introduction: notes his self-introduction was painful to watch and achieved the exact opposite of making friends.<span class=\"pg\">p.42–43<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">Berates Ayanokōji for his submissive nature; tells him cleaning up another student&#x27;s mess makes him look like a hopeless pushover and doormat.<span class=\"pg\">p.52<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Stays quiet during Sudō&#x27;s altercation with the two mocking second-years.<span class=\"pg\">p.46–51<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Observes Ayanokōji stoop down and clean up Sudō&#x27;s spilled instant ramen cup from the floor outside the store.<span class=\"pg\">p.51–52<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Critical of passivity; views unrewarded, self-effacing kindness as weak and illogical.<span class=\"pg\">p.52<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Continued observation of his contradictory behavior; disdainful of his conflict-averse actions while remaining tethered to his vicinity.<span class=\"pg\">p.42–52<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v1-p37-1\">← Before: Rejection of Hirata&#x27;s introductions<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v1-p54-1\">→ After: Lunchtime mockery of Ayanokōji&#x27;s isolation<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v1-p54-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"action spoken","w":"horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune lunchtime mockery of ayanokoji s isolation class 1 d classroom at lunch on day 2  ayanokoji is sitting alone  wishing someone would invite him to eat  laughs derisively at ayanokoji from the adjacent desk   how pathetic   i want someone to invite me along  i want to eat with someone  your thoughts are like an open book   that s right  i prefer to be alone  why don t you stop worrying about me and instead think about yourself  watches hirata invite the class to the cafeteria and get swarmed by girls  including karuizawa kei  horikita scoffs at ayanokoji s outstretched  unreciprocated hand   how tragic  gives ayanokoji one final pitying look before departing the classroom alone to eat in private  fiercely defends solitude as a deliberate preference rather than a social defeat  observant of others  insecurities  uses sharp mockery as a defense mechanism","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v1-p54-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Lunchtime mockery of Ayanokōji&#x27;s isolation<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.54–56<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Class 1-D classroom at lunch on Day 2. Ayanokōji is sitting alone, wishing someone would invite him to eat.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“How pathetic.”<span class=\"pg\">p.54<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“‘I want someone to invite me along. I want to eat with someone!’ Your thoughts are like an open book.”<span class=\"pg\">p.54<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“That’s right. I prefer to be alone... Why don’t you stop worrying about me and instead think about yourself?”<span class=\"pg\">p.54<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Laughs derisively at Ayanokōji from the adjacent desk.<span class=\"pg\">p.54–55<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Watches Hirata invite the class to the cafeteria and get swarmed by girls (including Karuizawa Kei). Horikita scoffs at Ayanokōji&#x27;s outstretched, unreciprocated hand.<span class=\"pg\">p.55<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “How tragic.”<span class=\"pg\">p.55<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Gives Ayanokōji one final pitying look before departing the classroom alone to eat in private.<span class=\"pg\">p.56<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Fiercely defends solitude as a deliberate preference rather than a social defeat; observant of others&#x27; insecurities, uses sharp mockery as a defense mechanism.<span class=\"pg\">p.54–55<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v1-p41-1\">← Before: Convenience store observation &amp; pushover lecture<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v1-p59-1\">→ After: The club-fair invitation &amp; the violence justification<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v1-p59-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"action spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune the club fair invitation   the violence justification classroom 1 d afternoon lunch  ak returns with convenience store bread  later  walking to the gymnasium   i m not interested in joining a club   cuts ak off before he can even ask   ayanokouji kun  do you have dementia  or are you just an idiot  didn t i just tell you that i m not interested   you don t really have any friends  do you   she asked   listen  don t count me as one of your friends   you don t plan to join a club  but you want to go to the club fair  how odd  do you plan to use this as a pretext for talking to people and making friends  karate chops ayanokoji in the side when he presses her with a  mean spirited  question  then delivers a grand speech justifying it  violence is the human race s most effective means of resolution  older than recorded history  wielded even by police   ayanokouji kun  i ve warned you thoroughly  but it would appear that you haven t been listening  i think i may have to dole out rather merciless punishment to you later   oh  really  violence has existed since the dawn of time  violence has historically proven to be the human race s most effective means of achieving resolution  violence is the most reliable method to make others listen  or safely deny their demands  not to mention that  in many countries  the police who enforce the law use handguns and batons  wielding violence as a tool to make arrests   well  if it s only for a little while after school  i ll go with you  she said   concedes to accompany him to the club fair strictly as an observer   watching you flail about as you fail to make friends sounds somewhat interesting  sharp tongued and combative  justifies physical aggression with cold rationalization  concedes ground only when logic permits  framing every concession as her own limited choice  despite constant rejection  she repeatedly ends up accompanying him when reasoned with   on her terms only","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v1-p59-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">The club-fair invitation &amp; the violence justification<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.59–62<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Classroom 1-D afternoon lunch (AK returns with convenience-store bread); later, walking to the gymnasium.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“I’m not interested in joining a club.” (cuts AK off before he can even ask)<span class=\"pg\">p.59<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Ayanokouji-kun, do you have dementia, or are you just an idiot? Didn’t I just tell you that I’m not interested?”<span class=\"pg\">p.59<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“You don’t really have any friends, do you?” (she asked)<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>9 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Listen, don’t count me as one of your friends.”<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You don’t plan to join a club, but you want to go to the club fair? How odd. Do you plan to use this as a pretext for talking to people and making friends?”<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Karate-chops Ayanokōji in the side when he presses her with a “mean-spirited” question, then delivers a grand speech justifying it: violence is the human race’s most effective means of resolution, older than recorded history, wielded even by police.<span class=\"pg\">p.61<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ayanokouji-kun. I’ve warned you thoroughly, but it would appear that you haven’t been listening. I think I may have to dole out rather merciless punishment to you later.”<span class=\"pg\">p.61<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Oh, really? Violence has existed since the dawn of time. Violence has historically proven to be the human race’s most effective means of achieving resolution. Violence is the most reliable method to make others listen, or safely deny their demands. Not to mention that, in many countries, the police who enforce the law use handguns and batons, wielding violence as a tool to make arrests.”<span class=\"pg\">p.61<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, if it’s only for a little while after school, I’ll go with you,” she said. (concedes to accompany him to the club fair strictly as an observer)<span class=\"pg\">p.62<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Watching you flail about as you fail to make friends sounds somewhat interesting.”<span class=\"pg\">p.62<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Sharp-tongued and combative; justifies physical aggression with cold rationalization; concedes ground only when logic permits, framing every concession as her own limited choice.<span class=\"pg\">p.59–62<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Despite constant rejection, she repeatedly ends up accompanying him when reasoned with — on her terms only.<span class=\"pg\">p.59–62<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v1-p54-1\">← Before: Lunchtime mockery of Ayanokōji&#x27;s isolation<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v1-p67-1\">→ After: The Student Council President&#x27;s speech: frozen shock<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v1-p67-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"action","w":"horikita-manabu horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune the student council president s speech  frozen shock gymnasium club fair  student council president horikita manabu takes the stage  as manabu commands absolute silence across hundreds of students and delivers his stern manifesto against naive candidates  suzune freezes completely  remains  still as a statue  completely paralyzed  her eyes stay locked forward  and she gives no sign of hearing ayanokoji speaking right next to her  while ayanokoji is distracted exchanging contact info with sudo  ike  and yamauchi  suzune slips silently into the departing crowd and disappears alone  visceral  overwhelming psychological reaction to her brother s presence  completely immobilizes her razor sharp composure  reducing her to silence and flight","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v1-p67-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">The Student Council President&#x27;s speech: frozen shock<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.67–71<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Gymnasium club fair. Student council president Horikita Manabu takes the stage.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-manabu.html\">Horikita Manabu<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q action\">As Manabu commands absolute silence across hundreds of students and delivers his stern manifesto against naive candidates, Suzune freezes completely.<span class=\"pg\">p.67–68<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q action\">Remains “still as a statue”, completely paralyzed; her eyes stay locked forward, and she gives no sign of hearing Ayanokōji speaking right next to her.<span class=\"pg\">p.68<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> While Ayanokōji is distracted exchanging contact info with Sudō, Ike, and Yamauchi, Suzune slips silently into the departing crowd and disappears alone.<span class=\"pg\">p.71<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Manabu<\/b> Visceral, overwhelming psychological reaction to her brother&#x27;s presence; completely immobilizes her razor-sharp composure, reducing her to silence and flight.<span class=\"pg\">p.67–68<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v1-p59-1\">← Before: The club-fair invitation &amp; the violence justification<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v1-p73-1\">→ After: Friendship boundary &amp; swimming performance<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v1-p73-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"action spoken","w":"horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune friendship boundary   swimming performance classroom 1 d  morning before pe  then indoor swimming pool  arrives at class and catches ayanokoji eyeing the boys  group conversation  scorns his hesitation  pathetic   from what i ve seen  you don t seem to be unsociable or lacking in communication skills  though   wait just a minute  i already warned you not to  but you wouldn t be thinking of me as your friend  would you  steps backward in visible disgust when asking if he considers her a friend  when ayanokoji replies that no matter how low he sinks he d never dream of being her friend  she visibly relaxes   i see  i feel a little relieved  competes in the first girls  heat of 50m swimming  finishes in  approximately 28 seconds  with sharp  disciplined form  strong athletic competence  steadfast commitment to solitary status  deeply relieved when social boundaries are affirmed","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v1-p73-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Friendship boundary &amp; swimming performance<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.73–74, 78<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Classroom 1-D (morning before PE); then indoor swimming pool.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“From what I’ve seen, you don’t seem to be unsociable or lacking in communication skills, though.”<span class=\"pg\">p.73<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Wait just a minute. I already warned you not to, but you wouldn’t be thinking of me as your friend, would you?”<span class=\"pg\">p.73<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I see. I feel a little relieved.”<span class=\"pg\">p.73<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Arrives at class and catches Ayanokōji eyeing the boys&#x27; group conversation. Scorns his hesitation (*&quot;Pathetic&quot;*).<span class=\"pg\">p.73<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Steps backward in visible disgust when asking if he considers her a friend. When Ayanokōji replies that no matter how low he sinks he&#x27;d never dream of being her friend, she visibly relaxes.<span class=\"pg\">p.73<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Competes in the first girls&#x27; heat of 50m swimming; finishes in **approximately 28 seconds** with sharp, disciplined form.<span class=\"pg\">p.78<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Strong athletic competence; steadfast commitment to solitary status; deeply relieved when social boundaries are affirmed.<span class=\"pg\">p.73, 78<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v1-p67-1\">← Before: The Student Council President&#x27;s speech: frozen shock<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v1-p89-1\">→ After: Café trap unmasked &amp; the ninth year alone<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v1-p89-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"action spoken","w":"kushida-kikyou ayanokouji-kiyotaka horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune cafe trap unmasked   the ninth year alone classroom 1 d  then palate cafe in keyaki mall  packing textbook into her bag at the end of class  when kushida approaches with a bright smile to invite her to a cafe  horikita rejects her flatly without hesitation   not interested   don t invite me again  it s a bother  overhears other girls in the doorway whispering they hate her  remains completely indifferent  palate cafe  ayanokoji invites her under the guise of thanking her for advice  seating them at a four person table and ordering a caramel latte  when kushida suddenly arrives pretending it is a coincidence  horikita dismantles the scheme instantly  glares with razor sharp deduction  exposes the setup before kushida can even sit down   i don t like this  what are you plotting   icy look  the moment she sits down   i thought as much  i thought this whole thing was a little suspicious right from the start   also  we came straight here after classes ended  no matter how much those girls rushed  they could only have been here for about one to two minutes at the most  it was far too early for them to get up and leave  am i wrong   dismantles the timing of the  coincidental  encounter   i ve already said this many times  i want you to leave me alone  i have no intention of becoming friends with anyone in class  can you not understand that   to kushida  after  please be my friend   i wouldn t deny you your wish  but it s wrong to try forcing people into something against their will  being alone doesn t make me sad   besides  do you think that i would be happy if you forced me to become your friend  do you think that feelings of trust would arise out of something forced   it s my fault for not being clear enough with you  so i don t blame you this time  but if you try this again  please keep in mind that i will not forgive you  takes her untouched latte and stands up to leave  when kushida murmurs that she feels they have met before  horikita brutally cuts her off   this is a waste of time  i find everything you re saying unpleasant  ayanokoji tries to mediate  warning her that spending three years without friends will be painful  horikita nonchalantly drops a staggering revelation about her past   it will be my ninth year in a row of being alone  so i ll be fine  oh  and if you include kindergarten  it would actually be slightly longer   kushida san  if you don t try to force me into anything  i won t be rude  i promise  you re not stupid  so you understand what i m telling you  right  gives a cold  final parting and walks out into keyaki mall alone  total lifelong isolation  has lived without a single friend for over nine consecutive years  since elementary and kindergarten  solitary existence is her normal state  keen deductive perception  catches subtle environmental tells  table sizing  eye movements  instantly  utter refusal to entertain her overtures  finds her performative cheerfulness unpleasant  warns her against forced familiarity  catches him conspiring with kushida  issues a firm  chilling warning that she will not forgive a second deception","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v1-p89-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Café trap unmasked &amp; the ninth year alone<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.89–90, 94–100<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Classroom 1-D; then Palate Café in Keyaki Mall. Palate Café. Ayanokōji invites her under the guise of thanking her for advice, seating them at a four-person table and ordering a caramel latte. When Kushida suddenly arrives pretending it is a coincidence, Horikita dismantles the scheme instantly.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a> · <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Not interested.”<span class=\"pg\">p.89<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Don’t invite me again. It’s a bother.”<span class=\"pg\">p.89<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I don’t like this. What are you plotting?” (icy look, the moment she sits down)<span class=\"pg\">p.98<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>20 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Packing textbook into her bag at the end of class. When Kushida approaches with a bright smile to invite her to a café, Horikita rejects her flatly without hesitation.<span class=\"pg\">p.89<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Overhears other girls in the doorway whispering they hate her; remains completely indifferent.<span class=\"pg\">p.89–90<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Glares with razor-sharp deduction; exposes the setup before Kushida can even sit down.<span class=\"pg\">p.98<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I thought as much. I thought this whole thing was a little suspicious right from the start.”<span class=\"pg\">p.98<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Also, we came straight here after classes ended. No matter how much those girls rushed, they could only have been here for about one to two minutes at the most. It was far too early for them to get up and leave. Am I wrong?” (dismantles the timing of the “coincidental” encounter)<span class=\"pg\">p.98<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’ve already said this many times. I want you to leave me alone. I have no intention of becoming friends with anyone in class. Can you not understand that?” (to Kushida, after “Please be my friend!”)<span class=\"pg\">p.98<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I wouldn’t deny you your wish, but it’s wrong to try forcing people into something against their will. Being alone doesn’t make me sad.”<span class=\"pg\">p.99<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Besides, do you think that I would be happy if you forced me to become your friend? Do you think that feelings of trust would arise out of something forced?”<span class=\"pg\">p.99<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It’s my fault for not being clear enough with you, so I don’t blame you this time. But if you try this again, please keep in mind that I will not forgive you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.98–99<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Takes her untouched latte and stands up to leave.<span class=\"pg\">p.99<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> When Kushida murmurs that she feels they have met before, Horikita brutally cuts her off.<span class=\"pg\">p.99<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “This is a waste of time. I find everything you’re saying unpleasant.”<span class=\"pg\">p.99<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Ayanokōji tries to mediate, warning her that spending three years without friends will be painful. Horikita nonchalantly drops a staggering revelation about her past.<span class=\"pg\">p.99–100<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It will be my ninth year in a row of being alone, so I’ll be fine. Oh, and if you include kindergarten, it would actually be slightly longer.”<span class=\"pg\">p.100<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Kushida-san, if you don’t try to force me into anything, I won’t be rude. I promise. You’re not stupid, so you understand what I’m telling you, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.100<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Gives a cold, final parting and walks out into Keyaki Mall alone.<span class=\"pg\">p.100<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Backstory<\/span> Total lifelong isolation: has lived without a single friend for over nine consecutive years (since elementary and kindergarten); solitary existence is her normal state.<span class=\"pg\">p.100<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Keen deductive perception: catches subtle environmental tells (table sizing, eye movements) instantly.<span class=\"pg\">p.98<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> Utter refusal to entertain her overtures; finds her performative cheerfulness unpleasant; warns her against forced familiarity.<span class=\"pg\">p.89, 99–100<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Catches him conspiring with Kushida; issues a firm, chilling warning that she will not forgive a second deception.<span class=\"pg\">p.98–99<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v1-p73-1\">← Before: Friendship boundary &amp; swimming performance<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v1-p124-1\">→ After: The S-System shock &amp; rejection of class cooperation<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v1-p124-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"action spoken","w":"hirata-yousuke horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune the s system shock   rejection of class cooperation classroom 1 d  morning homeroom on may 1st  quietly tallies up the 98 absences lates and 391 talking infractions in her notebook as chabashira announces class d s conduct breakdown  correctly deduces the newly posted poster displays the evaluation results and point rankings across all four classes  a  940  b  650  c  490  d  0  face stiffens in sheer disbelief and revolt when chabashira announces class d is sorted by incompetence and branded  defective   corpus   you re defective  this is just the result of you being defective  scores near the top of class d on the diagnostic short test  held the 3rd highest entrance exam score among the entire first year grade  notices ayanokoji photographing the class point totals board with his phone and questions what he is doing  impatiently points out investigating infractions cannot undo the class s established habit of talking and tardiness   wouldn t it be difficult to figure out those details at this stage  besides  i don t think you can resolve this simply by investigating  everyone in our class arrived late and talked too often   points are just a byproduct of our performance  though  not having points won t hinder our lives here at school  we have free options at almost every turn  right   while unfortunate  they ve simply reaped what they ve sown  when hirata steps down from the podium and invites her and ayanokoji to join a class cooperation discussion to raise points  horikita shuts him down with icy disdain   i m sorry  can you ask someone else  i m not particularly good at discussing things with others   her first refusal   i m sorry  but i have no interest in something meaningless   i refuse  i won t participate   her words were stern  yet composed   final rejection   that s one perspective  yes  if we could easily solve this by talking  then that d be fine  however  if an unintelligent student tries to lead the discussion  the group will fall further into chaos  to the point where there s no hope of salvaging anything  besides  i can t meekly accept my current situation   post rejection rationale to ayanokoji  absolute meritocratic elitism  total contempt for collective failure  views social compromise as a toxic liability  rebuffs his leadership outright  views his idealistic consensus building as weak and futile","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v1-p124-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">The S-System shock &amp; rejection of class cooperation<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.124–126, 132–136<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Classroom 1-D. Morning homeroom on May 1st.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Wouldn’t it be difficult to figure out those details at this stage? Besides, I don’t think you can resolve this simply by investigating. Everyone in our class arrived late and talked too often.”<span class=\"pg\">p.132<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Points are just a byproduct of our performance, though. Not having points won’t hinder our lives here at school. We have free options at almost every turn, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.133<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“While unfortunate, they’ve simply reaped what they’ve sown.”<span class=\"pg\">p.133<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>12 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Quietly tallies up the 98 absences/lates and 391 talking infractions in her notebook as Chabashira announces Class D&#x27;s conduct breakdown.<span class=\"pg\">p.124<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Correctly deduces the newly posted poster displays the evaluation results and point rankings across all four classes (A: 940, B: 650, C: 490, D: 0).<span class=\"pg\">p.125<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Face stiffens in sheer disbelief and revolt when Chabashira announces Class D is sorted by incompetence and branded &quot;defective&quot; (corpus: &quot;You&#x27;re defective. This is just the result of you being defective.&quot;)<span class=\"pg\">p.126<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Scores near the top of Class D on the diagnostic short test; held the 3rd highest entrance exam score among the entire first-year grade.<span class=\"pg\">p.128, 143<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Notices Ayanokōji photographing the class point totals board with his phone and questions what he is doing; impatiently points out investigating infractions cannot undo the class&#x27;s established habit of talking and tardiness.<span class=\"pg\">p.132<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> When Hirata steps down from the podium and invites her and Ayanokōji to join a class cooperation discussion to raise points, Horikita shuts him down with icy disdain.<span class=\"pg\">p.135–136<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m sorry, can you ask someone else? I’m not particularly good at discussing things with others,” (her first refusal)<span class=\"pg\">p.135<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m sorry, but I have no interest in something meaningless.”<span class=\"pg\">p.135<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I refuse. I won’t participate.” (her words were stern, yet composed — final rejection)<span class=\"pg\">p.135<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s one perspective, yes. If we could easily solve this by talking, then that’d be fine. However, if an unintelligent student tries to lead the discussion, the group will fall further into chaos, to the point where there’s no hope of salvaging anything. Besides, I can’t meekly accept my current situation.” (post-rejection rationale to Ayanokōji)<span class=\"pg\">p.136<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Absolute meritocratic elitism; total contempt for collective failure; views social compromise as a toxic liability.<span class=\"pg\">p.133, 136<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Rebuffs his leadership outright; views his idealistic consensus-building as weak and futile.<span class=\"pg\">p.135–136<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v1-p89-1\">← Before: Café trap unmasked &amp; the ninth year alone<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v1-p142-1\">→ After: Faculty office protest &amp; the all-50s revelation<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v1-p142-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"action spoken","w":"horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune faculty office protest   the all 50s revelation marches into the faculty office over her placement in class d  guidance office adjacent to faculty staff room  marches into the faculty guidance office to directly confront chabashira over her placement in class d   i will be frank  why was i sorted into class d   i solved nearly every problem on the entrance examination  i made no substantial mistakes on the interview  either  at the very least  i shouldn t have been sorted into class d   who could be happy with an incorrect evaluation  furthermore  the class rankings greatly impact our future prospects  of course i m dissatisfied  when chabashira counters that common sense created japan s flawed hereditary succession and that academic ability alone does not define superiority  horikita falters but refuses to concede   you still haven t given me an explanation  was i honestly sorted into class d  did anything go wrong with the grading  please double check   is that so  then i will ask the school again  at another time   i can t imagine it will be easy  though  forget overtaking class a  how in the world could those immature class d misfits gain more points  i can t see how it s possible  gasps as chabashira reveals ayanokoji hiding in the kitchenette and produces his entrance examination answer sheets  showing exactly 50 out of 100 in japanese  math  english  social studies  and science  plus 50 on the short test   this is a rather frightening coincidence  flinches visibly when chabashira points out ak solved a 3 success rate math problem with an advanced formula while botching a 76 success problem  and warns her that ak may be more intelligent than she is   why do you pretend not to know   what other reasons do you have  extreme academic pride  shaken to her core when confronted with an enigmatic peer who can manipulate test outcomes at will","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v1-p142-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Faculty office protest &amp; the all-50s revelation<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.142–148<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Guidance office adjacent to faculty staff room.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“I will be frank. Why was I sorted into Class D?”<span class=\"pg\">p.142<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I solved nearly every problem on the entrance examination. I made no substantial mistakes on the interview, either. At the very least, I shouldn’t have been sorted into Class D.”<span class=\"pg\">p.143<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Who could be happy with an incorrect evaluation? Furthermore, the class rankings greatly impact our future prospects. Of course I’m dissatisfied.”<span class=\"pg\">p.143<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>12 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Post<\/span> Marches into the faculty office over her placement in Class D.<span class=\"pg\">p.142–143<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Marches into the faculty guidance office to directly confront Chabashira over her placement in Class D.<span class=\"pg\">p.142–143<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> When Chabashira counters that common sense created Japan&#x27;s flawed hereditary succession and that academic ability alone does not define superiority, Horikita falters but refuses to concede.<span class=\"pg\">p.144<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You still haven’t given me an explanation. Was I honestly sorted into Class D? Did anything go wrong with the grading? Please double-check.”<span class=\"pg\">p.144<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Is that so? Then I will ask the school again, at another time.”<span class=\"pg\">p.145<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I can’t imagine it will be easy, though. Forget overtaking Class A; how in the world could those immature Class D misfits gain more points? I can’t see how it’s possible.”<span class=\"pg\">p.145<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Gasps as Chabashira reveals Ayanokōji hiding in the kitchenette and produces his entrance examination answer sheets, showing exactly 50 out of 100 in Japanese, Math, English, Social Studies, and Science, plus 50 on the short test.<span class=\"pg\">p.146<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “This is a rather frightening coincidence.”<span class=\"pg\">p.146<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Flinches visibly when Chabashira points out AK solved a 3%-success-rate math problem with an advanced formula while botching a 76%-success problem, and warns her that AK may be more intelligent than she is.<span class=\"pg\">p.147<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Why do you pretend not to know?”<span class=\"pg\">p.147<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What other reasons do you have?”<span class=\"pg\">p.147<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Extreme academic pride; shaken to her core when confronted with an enigmatic peer who can manipulate test outcomes at will.<span class=\"pg\">p.143, 147<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v1-p124-1\">← Before: The S-System shock &amp; rejection of class cooperation<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v1-p148-1\">→ After: Stairwell confrontation &amp; the pawn offer<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v1-p148-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"action spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune stairwell confrontation   the pawn offer school corridor stairs  follows ayanokoji out of the office and confronts him on the stairs  grilling him about his true motives   was your score really just a coincidence   i don t  but i also don t understand  ayanokouji kun  you said that you like to avoid trouble  but you don t seem to be interested in class a   when i entered this school  i thought graduation was my only goal  but the reality is different  i m not even at the starting line  delivers a sharp karate chop to ayanokoji s ribs when he tells her not to act so proud   no  you re right that no lone individual can solve this problem  we won t even make it to the starting line without everyone s help   we have three major  immediate issues  tardiness and talking during class are the first two  third  we must make sure no one fails the midterm exam   i need your help  ayanokouji kun  when ayanokoji flatly refuses  i refuse  she completely ignores him with unnerving composure   i always knew you d help  ayanokouji kun  i m grateful   no  i heard the voice inside your head  you said you d help   don t worry  i don t require your brain power  ayanokouji kun  leave the planning to me  and act as i tell you   unfortunately  no one else in class d is nearly as easy to manipulate as you  when ayanokoji suggests she recruit hirata instead  horikita drops her iconic shogi metaphor  exposing her ruthless utilitarian mindset   he s no good  even if he has some talent and ability  i can t use him  to use an analogy  think about the pieces in shogi  right now  i don t need a gold or silver general  i want a pawn   an interesting answer  but you don t seem like the type to make that effort  ayanokouji kun  besides  haven t you been thinking   i ve always been a pawn  i don t want to advance  all along   well  contact me once you ve given it some thought  i look forward to hearing from you  discovers his deliberate 50 point sandbagging  views him not as an equal partner or strategist  but as an easily disposable  obedient  pawn  to execute her directives while keeping his abilities hidden","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v1-p148-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Stairwell confrontation &amp; the pawn offer<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.148–151<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">School corridor stairs.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Was your score…really just a coincidence?”<span class=\"pg\">p.148<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I don’t, but…I also don’t understand, Ayanokouji-kun. You said that you like to avoid trouble, but you don’t seem to be interested in Class A.”<span class=\"pg\">p.148<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“When I entered this school, I thought graduation was my only goal. But the reality is different. I’m not even at the starting line.”<span class=\"pg\">p.148<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>15 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Follows Ayanokōji out of the office and confronts him on the stairs, grilling him about his true motives.<span class=\"pg\">p.148<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Delivers a sharp karate chop to Ayanokōji&#x27;s ribs when he tells her not to act so proud.<span class=\"pg\">p.149<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “No. You’re right that no lone individual can solve this problem. We won’t even make it to the starting line without everyone’s help.”<span class=\"pg\">p.149<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “We have three major, immediate issues. Tardiness and talking during class are the first two. Third, we must make sure no one fails the midterm exam.”<span class=\"pg\">p.150<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I need your help, Ayanokouji-kun.”<span class=\"pg\">p.150<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> When Ayanokōji flatly refuses (&quot;I refuse&quot;), she completely ignores him with unnerving composure.<span class=\"pg\">p.150<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I always knew you’d help, Ayanokouji-kun. I’m grateful.”<span class=\"pg\">p.150<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “No, I heard the voice inside your head. You said you’d help.”<span class=\"pg\">p.150<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Don’t worry. I don’t require your brain power, Ayanokouji-kun. Leave the planning to me, and act as I tell you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.151<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Unfortunately, no one else in Class D is nearly as easy to manipulate as you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.151<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> When Ayanokōji suggests she recruit Hirata instead, Horikita drops her iconic shogi metaphor, exposing her ruthless utilitarian mindset.<span class=\"pg\">p.151<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “He’s no good. Even if he has some talent and ability, I can’t use him. To use an analogy, think about the pieces in shogi. Right now, I don’t need a gold or silver general. I want a pawn.”<span class=\"pg\">p.151<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “An interesting answer, but you don’t seem like the type to make that effort, Ayanokouji-kun. Besides, haven’t you been thinking, ‘I’ve always been a pawn, I don’t want to advance,’ all along?”<span class=\"pg\">p.151<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, contact me once you’ve given it some thought. I look forward to hearing from you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.151<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Discovers his deliberate 50-point sandbagging; views him not as an equal partner or strategist, but as an easily disposable, obedient &quot;pawn&quot; to execute her directives while keeping his abilities hidden.<span class=\"pg\">p.146–151<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v1-p142-1\">← Before: Faculty office protest &amp; the all-50s revelation<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v1-p152-1\">→ After: Compass stabbing, cafeteria recruitment, &amp; Kushida veto<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v1-p152-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"action spoken","w":"horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune compass stabbing  cafeteria recruitment    kushida veto classroom 1 d  school cafeteria  dorm phone call  when ayanokoji begins nodding off in class before lunch  drives the sharp metal needle of her drawing compass directly into his right arm to wake him   are you angry with me   what  when did i stab with you a compass needle  ayanokouji kun   so  just because i m holding something means i stabbed you   be careful  if you get caught sleeping  that would undoubtedly lead to a loss in points  invites ayanokoji to lunch and treats him to an expensive cafeteria meal set to negotiate his assistance in gathering the failing students  sudo  ike  yamauchi  for a midterm study group  calls ayanokoji late at night  furious upon learning he enlisted kushida kikyo to assemble the boys   i don t quite understand the message you just sent me  not that part  the part about kushida  i didn t know about that   i don t remember giving you permission to do that  her grades aren t even failing   i don t like it  shouldn t you have sought my approval first   i understand  i suppose anything worth doing requires sacrifice  however  kushida may only help gather the students  she s not allowed to join the study group   i will not allow her into our study group  i refuse to budge on this   this has nothing to do with that  she didn t fail the test  inviting extra people will only mean more time spent and greater confusion   don t you feel uncomfortable sitting next to someone you hate  abruptly hangs up the phone on ayanokoji to avoid further compromise","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v1-p152-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Compass stabbing, cafeteria recruitment, &amp; Kushida veto<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.152–157, 167–169<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Classroom 1-D; school cafeteria; dorm phone call.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Are you angry with me?”<span class=\"pg\">p.152<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“What? When did I stab with you a compass needle, Ayanokouji-kun?”<span class=\"pg\">p.152<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“So, just because I’m holding something means I stabbed you?”<span class=\"pg\">p.152<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>12 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> When Ayanokōji begins nodding off in class before lunch, drives the sharp metal needle of her drawing compass directly into his right arm to wake him.<span class=\"pg\">p.152<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Be careful. If you get caught sleeping, that would undoubtedly lead to a loss in points.”<span class=\"pg\">p.153<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Invites Ayanokōji to lunch and treats him to an expensive cafeteria meal set to negotiate his assistance in gathering the failing students (Sudō, Ike, Yamauchi) for a midterm study group.<span class=\"pg\">p.154–157<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Calls Ayanokōji late at night, furious upon learning he enlisted Kushida Kikyō to assemble the boys.<span class=\"pg\">p.167–169<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I don’t quite understand the message you just sent me… Not that part. The part about Kushida. I didn’t know about that.”<span class=\"pg\">p.167<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I don’t remember giving you permission to do that. Her grades aren’t even failing.”<span class=\"pg\">p.167<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I don’t like it. Shouldn’t you have sought my approval first?”<span class=\"pg\">p.168<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I understand. I suppose anything worth doing requires sacrifice. However, Kushida may only help gather the students. She’s not allowed to join the study group.”<span class=\"pg\">p.168<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I will not allow her into our study group. I refuse to budge on this.”<span class=\"pg\">p.168<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “This has nothing to do with that. She didn’t fail the test. Inviting extra people will only mean more time spent and greater confusion.”<span class=\"pg\">p.168<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Don’t you feel uncomfortable sitting next to someone you hate?”<span class=\"pg\">p.168<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Abruptly hangs up the phone on Ayanokōji to avoid further compromise.<span class=\"pg\">p.168–169<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v1-p148-1\">← Before: Stairwell confrontation &amp; the pawn offer<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v1-p173-1\">→ After: Library collapse &amp; &quot;getting rid of dead weight&quot;<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v1-p173-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"action spoken","w":"horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune library collapse    getting rid of dead weight  school library  after school  arrives at the library with immaculate  meticulously organized study materials  but rigidly demands absolute silence  instantly suffocating the study group  mercilessly ridicules sudo when he struggles with elementary fraction arithmetic   i m sorry  you re far too ignorant and incompetent   said by horikita  who d been silent until now   if you can t solve this problem  i seriously shiver at the thought of what the future will bring   you re right  this has nothing to do with me  your suffering won t influence me at all  i just pity you  you must have spent your whole life running from anything that presented a challenge   after sudo slams the desk  when sudo slams the desk and threatens violence  she challenges him with unflinching  cold mockery   so  you lack the courage to hit me  don t use my gender as an excuse  when ike quits in protest against her condescension  horikita shoots back with venomous indifference   i don t care if you get expelled  do what you want   interesting  didn t you come here because you can t study  formulates her cold  elitist conclusion as the boys walk out   i was certainly mistaken  even if i d helped them avoid failure this time  we would ve faced a similar dilemma soon after  we d have to go through this irritation all over again  eventually  they ll fail  i finally understand how unproductive this was  i don t have the time for it   i mean that it s better to get rid of the dead weight  directly antagonizes kushida  accusing her of faking her sympathy for the failing boys   even if that was how you truly felt  i wouldn t particularly care  but i don t think that you actually want to save them  offers to tutor ayanokoji alone in the empty library  calling him  somewhat better than those worthless idiots  and calls ak cruel for passively watching his friends get expelled   i suppose you were the only one who understood me  ayanokouji kun  you re at least somewhat better than those worthless idiots  if there s some subject you re struggling with  i could teach you   there s nothing to be gained from associating with people who ll likely be expelled soon   how incredibly selfish  you call them your friends  yet you simply stand by and watch as they re expelled  from my point of view  you re cruel","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v1-p173-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Library collapse &amp; &quot;getting rid of dead weight&quot;<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.173–180<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">School library, after school.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“I’m sorry, you’re far too ignorant and incompetent,” (said by Horikita, who’d been silent until now)<span class=\"pg\">p.176<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“If you can’t solve this problem, I seriously shiver at the thought of what the future will bring.”<span class=\"pg\">p.176<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“You’re right. This has nothing to do with me. Your suffering won’t influence me at all. I just pity you. You must have spent your whole life running from anything that presented a challenge,” (after Sudō slams the desk)<span class=\"pg\">p.176<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>16 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Arrives at the library with immaculate, meticulously organized study materials, but rigidly demands absolute silence, instantly suffocating the study group.<span class=\"pg\">p.173<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Mercilessly ridicules Sudō when he struggles with elementary fraction arithmetic.<span class=\"pg\">p.176<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> When Sudō slams the desk and threatens violence, she challenges him with unflinching, cold mockery.<span class=\"pg\">p.177<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “So, you lack the courage to hit me? Don’t use my gender as an excuse.”<span class=\"pg\">p.177<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> When Ike quits in protest against her condescension, Horikita shoots back with venomous indifference.<span class=\"pg\">p.178<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I don’t care if you get expelled. Do what you want.”<span class=\"pg\">p.178<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Interesting. Didn’t you come here because you can’t study?”<span class=\"pg\">p.178<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Formulates her cold, elitist conclusion as the boys walk out.<span class=\"pg\">p.178<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I was certainly mistaken. Even if I’d helped them avoid failure this time, we would’ve faced a similar dilemma soon after. We’d have to go through this irritation all over again. Eventually, they’ll fail. I finally understand how unproductive this was. I don’t have the time for it.”<span class=\"pg\">p.178<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I mean that it’s better to get rid of the dead weight.”<span class=\"pg\">p.178<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Directly antagonizes Kushida, accusing her of faking her sympathy for the failing boys.<span class=\"pg\">p.179<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Even if that was how you truly felt, I wouldn’t particularly care. But I don’t think that you actually want to save them.”<span class=\"pg\">p.179<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Offers to tutor Ayanokōji alone in the empty library, calling him &quot;somewhat better than those worthless idiots,&quot; and calls AK cruel for passively watching his friends get expelled.<span class=\"pg\">p.179–180<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I suppose you were the only one who understood me, Ayanokouji-kun. You’re at least somewhat better than those worthless idiots. If there’s some subject you’re struggling with, I could teach you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.179<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “There’s nothing to be gained from associating with people who’ll likely be expelled soon.”<span class=\"pg\">p.180<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “How incredibly selfish. You call them your friends, yet you simply stand by and watch as they’re expelled. From my point of view, you’re cruel.”<span class=\"pg\">p.180<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v1-p152-1\">← Before: Compass stabbing, cafeteria recruitment, &amp; Kushida veto<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v1-p192-1\">→ After: Night assault by Manabu, the equality debate, &amp; the devil&#x27;s handshake<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v1-p192-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"action spoken","w":"horikita-manabu ayanokouji-kiyotaka horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune night assault by manabu  the equality debate    the devil s handshake pathway outside dormitories  late night  follows her older brother horikita manabu into the darkness  completely paralyzed by fear and reverence  submits powerlessly when he grabs her wrist and pins her against the concrete wall   hmph  i m far different from the useless girl you once knew  niisan  i came here to catch you   that s  you re wrong about that  i ll show you  i ll reach class a right away  then   i i can t do that  i will definitely reach class a  i ll show you   niisan  i  gasps in strained shock as ayanokoji physically intercepts her brother s throw   a ayanokouji kun   stop it  ayanokouji kun  stunned by ayanokoji evading her brother s lethal strikes  denies to her brother that ak is her friend   he s not my friend  just my classmate   i m going to drag myself up to class a even if it kills me  sits slumped against the concrete wall in dejection  reveals manabu s formidable martial arts ranks   he s ranked fifth dan in karate and fourth dan in aikido   you also practice martial arts  don t you  ayanokouji kun  you must hold a dan rank   you purposefully get lower test scores  and you say that you studied piano and calligraphy  i really don t understand you  debates the nature of merit and human ability with ayanokoji under the night sky  defends absolute meritocracy   even if there are potential unknown negatives  it s better for the future of our class to abandon the failing students  wouldn t you regret not abandoning them when we do finally increase our points  right now  it s a risk that we should take   yes  really  i m at a complete loss as to why you re so desperate to save them   is that bad  people are calculating creatures  for the most part  if you sell goods  you receive money  if you do someone a favor  that debt of gratitude will be repaid  by giving up a seat  you gain the joy of contributing to society  am i wrong   who do you think you are  do you even have the ability to find fault with me  stumbles when ayanokoji diagnoses her fatal flaw  she isolates herself because she considers everyone else inferior baggage  blinding her to others  unique strengths  sudo s athletics  ike s communication  where she herself would drag down the class   it s almost as if you re saying i m the same as sudou kun and his group   this is all pure conjecture  it s nothing more than armchair speculation  forced to concede the argument  shaken by ayanokoji s logic   it s frustrating  but what you said was basically correct  you ve persuaded me  i have to concede that point  however  i still don t understand you  what do you want  what is this school to you  why did you work so hard to convince me   cut the crap  i want to know the real reason  is it for points  to rise up  even by one class level  or is it to save your friends  when ayanokoji answers that he wants to understand true merit and equality  she extends her arm to seal an alliance   there s no way that you could fool me into believing you  ayanokouji kun   i ll look after sudou kun and the others  but for my own sake  i ll make sure that they don t get left behind  but only as a strategic means of securing an advantage for our future  okay   we ve come to an arrangement  then  devastating inferiority complex regarding her brother manabu  fiercely stubborn yet fundamentally logical can be persuaded by undeniable rational evidence  formalizes an explicit utilitarian pact with ayanokoji  her primary psychological driver  desperate for his acknowledgment  but rendered completely docile and helpless in his presence  witnesses him deflect her brother s lethal strikes  accepts his philosophical critique of her arrogance  seals the alliance  his narration   made a deal with the devil","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v1-p192-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Night assault by Manabu, the equality debate, &amp; the devil&#x27;s handshake<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.192–202<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Pathway outside dormitories, late night.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-manabu.html\">Horikita Manabu<\/a> · <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Hmph. I’m far different from the useless girl you once knew, niisan. I came here to catch you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.192<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“That’s… You’re wrong about that. I’ll show you. I’ll reach Class A right away, then—”<span class=\"pg\">p.192<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I-I can’t do that… I will definitely reach Class A. I’ll show you!”<span class=\"pg\">p.193<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>30 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Follows her older brother Horikita Manabu into the darkness; completely paralyzed by fear and reverence. Submits powerlessly when he grabs her wrist and pins her against the concrete wall.<span class=\"pg\">p.192–193<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Niisan, I…”<span class=\"pg\">p.193<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Gasps in strained shock as Ayanokōji physically intercepts her brother&#x27;s throw.<span class=\"pg\">p.194<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “A-Ayanokouji-kun?!”<span class=\"pg\">p.194<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Stop it, Ayanokouji-kun.”<span class=\"pg\">p.194<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Stunned by Ayanokōji evading her brother’s lethal strikes; denies to her brother that AK is her friend.<span class=\"pg\">p.196<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “He’s…not my friend. Just my classmate.”<span class=\"pg\">p.196<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m going to drag myself up to Class A even if it kills me.”<span class=\"pg\">p.196<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Sits slumped against the concrete wall in dejection; reveals Manabu’s formidable martial arts ranks.<span class=\"pg\">p.196–197<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “He’s ranked fifth dan in karate and fourth dan in aikido.”<span class=\"pg\">p.196<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You also practice martial arts, don’t you, Ayanokouji-kun? You must hold a dan rank.”<span class=\"pg\">p.197<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You purposefully get lower test scores, and you say that you studied piano and calligraphy. I really don’t understand you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.197<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Debates the nature of merit and human ability with Ayanokōji under the night sky. Defends absolute meritocracy.<span class=\"pg\">p.199–201<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Even if there are potential unknown negatives, it’s better for the future of our class to abandon the failing students. Wouldn’t you regret not abandoning them when we do finally increase our points? Right now, it’s a risk that we should take.”<span class=\"pg\">p.199<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yes. Really. I’m at a complete loss as to why you’re so desperate to save them.”<span class=\"pg\">p.199<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Is that bad? People are calculating creatures, for the most part. If you sell goods, you receive money. If you do someone a favor, that debt of gratitude will be repaid. By giving up a seat, you gain the joy of contributing to society. Am I wrong?”<span class=\"pg\">p.200<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Who do you think you are? Do you even have the ability to find fault with me?”<span class=\"pg\">p.200<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Stumbles when Ayanokōji diagnoses her fatal flaw: she isolates herself because she considers everyone else inferior baggage, blinding her to others&#x27; unique strengths (Sudō&#x27;s athletics, Ike&#x27;s communication) where she herself would drag down the class.<span class=\"pg\">p.200–201<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It’s almost as if you’re saying I’m the same as Sudou-kun and his group.”<span class=\"pg\">p.200<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “This is all pure conjecture. It’s nothing more than armchair speculation.”<span class=\"pg\">p.201<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Forced to concede the argument; shaken by Ayanokōji’s logic.<span class=\"pg\">p.201<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It’s frustrating, but what you said was basically correct. You’ve persuaded me; I have to concede that point. However, I still don’t understand you. What do you want? What is this school to you? Why did you work so hard to convince me?”<span class=\"pg\">p.201<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Cut the crap. I want to know the real reason. Is it for points? To rise up, even by one class level? Or is it to save your friends?”<span class=\"pg\">p.202<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> When Ayanokōji answers that he wants to understand true merit and equality, she extends her arm to seal an alliance.<span class=\"pg\">p.202<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “There’s no way that you could fool me into believing you, Ayanokouji-kun.”<span class=\"pg\">p.202<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’ll look after Sudou-kun and the others, but for my own sake. I’ll make sure that they don’t get left behind, but only as a strategic means of securing an advantage for our future. Okay?”<span class=\"pg\">p.202<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “We’ve come to an arrangement, then.”<span class=\"pg\">p.202<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Devastating inferiority complex regarding her brother Manabu; fiercely stubborn yet fundamentally logical—can be persuaded by undeniable rational evidence; formalizes an explicit utilitarian pact with Ayanokōji.<span class=\"pg\">p.192–196, 202<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Manabu<\/b> Her primary psychological driver; desperate for his acknowledgment, but rendered completely docile and helpless in his presence.<span class=\"pg\">p.192–196<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Witnesses him deflect her brother’s lethal strikes; accepts his philosophical critique of her arrogance; seals the alliance (his narration: &quot;made a deal with the devil&quot;).<span class=\"pg\">p.194–202<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v1-p173-1\">← Before: Library collapse &amp; &quot;getting rid of dead weight&quot;<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v1-p203-1\">→ After: The reunion campaign: honesty, &quot;I hate you,&quot; and the in-class study plan<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v1-p203-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"action spoken","w":"kushida-kikyou horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune the reunion campaign  honesty   i hate you  and the in class study plan one and a half months in  smacks ayanokoji awake mid thought  checks him for fever  and dispatches him to re recruit the fallen study group   while grumbling that  sacrifices are inevitable  over needing kushida again   here  look at this written contract   produces a ludicrous written contract making ak her workhorse until class a  he tears it up  personally invites kushida to lunch at palate and treats her to a drink   the site of her earlier fury   then answers kushida s motive probe with total honesty   no  this is for me   i m going to do it  definitely   declaring class a within earshot of kushida s doubts   fine  if everything goes well with the study group  i ll accept your help moving forward   conditionally admitting kushida into the wider class a project  when sudou demands a sincere apology for the library insults  refuses point blank   then detonates the opposite move   i hate you  sudou kun   however  our mutual abhorrence is trivial right now  i will teach you for my own sake  you will do your best for your own sake  am i wrong   yes  exactly  otherwise  why would anyone willingly involve you  unveils her notebook schedule  exploit the six wasted hours of class time instead of scarce after school hours  ak kushida horikita each tutor one on one in ten minute breaks  memorize  don t take notes   there are no shortcuts or cheap tricks when it comes to studying  you just have to spend your time carefully   turns his own basketball logic against him   put in the effort so that you can continue to play basketball at this school  don t throw away your own potential  accepts ayanokoji s manufactured date stakes incentive as her own   boys are the simplest creatures on earth  practical honesty as a weapon  confesses selfish motives to win kushida  refuses performative apology  engineering instinct   restructures time itself rather than demanding willpower  major compromise  tolerates kushida s proximity for capability  granting conditional entry to the class a project","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v1-p203-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">The reunion campaign: honesty, &quot;I hate you,&quot; and the in-class study plan<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.203–211<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Here, look at this written contract.” (produces a ludicrous written contract making AK her workhorse until Class A; he tears it up)<span class=\"pg\">p.204<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“No. This is for me.”<span class=\"pg\">p.204<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I’m going to do it. Definitely,” (declaring Class A within earshot of Kushida&#x27;s doubts)<span class=\"pg\">p.205<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>13 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> One and a half months in: smacks Ayanokōji awake mid-thought, checks him for fever, and dispatches him to re-recruit the fallen study group — while grumbling that &quot;Sacrifices are inevitable&quot; over needing Kushida again.<span class=\"pg\">p.203<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Personally invites Kushida to lunch at Palate and treats her to a drink — the site of her earlier fury — then answers Kushida&#x27;s motive probe with total honesty.<span class=\"pg\">p.204<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Fine. If everything goes well with the study group, I’ll accept your help moving forward,” (conditionally admitting Kushida into the wider Class A project)<span class=\"pg\">p.205<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> When Sudou demands a sincere apology for the library insults, refuses point-blank — then detonates the opposite move.<span class=\"pg\">p.207<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I hate you, Sudou-kun.”<span class=\"pg\">p.207<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “However, our mutual abhorrence is trivial right now. I will teach you for my own sake. You will do your best for your own sake. Am I wrong?”<span class=\"pg\">p.207<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yes, exactly. Otherwise, why would anyone willingly involve you?”<span class=\"pg\">p.207<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Unveils her notebook schedule: exploit the six wasted hours of class time instead of scarce after-school hours; AK/Kushida/Horikita each tutor one-on-one in ten-minute breaks; memorize, don&#x27;t take notes.<span class=\"pg\">p.208–210<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “There are no shortcuts or cheap tricks when it comes to studying. You just have to spend your time carefully.” (turns his own basketball logic against him)<span class=\"pg\">p.210<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Put in the effort so that you can continue to play basketball at this school. Don’t throw away your own potential.”<span class=\"pg\">p.210<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Accepts Ayanokōji&#x27;s manufactured date-stakes incentive as her own: &quot;boys are the simplest creatures on earth.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.211<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Practical honesty as a weapon (confesses selfish motives to win Kushida); refuses performative apology; engineering instinct — restructures time itself rather than demanding willpower.<span class=\"pg\">p.203–211<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> Major compromise: tolerates Kushida&#x27;s proximity for capability, granting conditional entry to the Class A project.<span class=\"pg\">p.204–205<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v1-p192-1\">← Before: Night assault by Manabu, the equality debate, &amp; the devil&#x27;s handshake<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v1-p237-1\">→ After: The hate confirmation &amp; the basketball apology<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v1-p237-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"action spoken","w":"kushida-kikyou sudou-ken horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune the hate confirmation   the basketball apology gives kushida genuine  unprompted praise for the old test distribution   including precise analysis of why announcing it after class protected everyone s motivation   really  thank you for everything you ve done  if you weren t here  the study group would not have succeeded  stops kushida at the door for the one confirmation she needs before trusting the partnership   you hate me  don t you   you re not answering my question because it s true  right   no  that s unnecessary  knowing that is good enough  i can continue working with you without hesitation   hearing  i really hate you  changes nothing   pure utility logic  glances at ayanokoji and shuts down his swimsuit daydream with one word   pervert  during the break  leaps to sudou s side and triages his ten minute english crisis with tactical advice   sudou kun  memorize the problems that are worth a lot of points and those with the shortest answers  steps in front of sulking sudou after the exam and delivers her first genuine encouragement   it was certainly your fault for not reviewing the old test s final section  however  as you said  you did everything that you could with the time that you had  you didn t cut any corners or give up  considering how much effort you put in  i think you should hold your head high and feel proud   comfort  i m speaking the truth  when i look at how far you ve come  i understand how hard studying is for you  sudou  amends her earlier scorn for his professional basketball dream   having researched the actual career path   and bows her head in a formal apology   i never thought i needed to understand anyone except for myself  so when you first told me that you wanted to play basketball  i insulted you  however  i now regret that  someone who doesn t understand how difficult  how arduous basketball is has no right to dismiss that dream as foolish   sudou kun  don t forget the hard work and effort that you poured into studying  apply that diligence to basketball  if you do  you might be able to go pro  at least  that s how i feel   i m sorry for what i said back then  well  now that i ve said my piece  i ll be going  growth arc  converts hate into explicitly acknowledged working distrust  capable of researched  bow level apology when her earlier judgment is proven wrong   delivered in her usual aloof manner but unmistakable  trusts utility over affection  proceeds  without hesitation  on a confirmed mutual hatred  from library tormentor to coach and apologizer   the pivot that fully wins his loyalty","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v1-p237-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">The hate confirmation &amp; the basketball apology<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.237–245<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a> · <a href=\"sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Really, thank you for everything you’ve done. If you weren’t here, the study group would not have succeeded.”<span class=\"pg\">p.238<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“You hate me, don’t you?”<span class=\"pg\">p.238<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“You’re not answering my question because it’s true. Right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.238<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>17 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Gives Kushida genuine, unprompted praise for the old-test distribution — including precise analysis of why announcing it after class protected everyone&#x27;s motivation.<span class=\"pg\">p.237<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Stops Kushida at the door for the one confirmation she needs before trusting the partnership.<span class=\"pg\">p.238<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “No. That’s unnecessary. Knowing that is good enough. I can continue working with you without hesitation.” (hearing &quot;I really hate you&quot; changes nothing — pure utility logic)<span class=\"pg\">p.238<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Glances at Ayanokōji and shuts down his swimsuit-daydream with one word.<span class=\"pg\">p.240<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Pervert.”<span class=\"pg\">p.240<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> During the break, leaps to Sudou&#x27;s side and triages his ten-minute English crisis with tactical advice.<span class=\"pg\">p.241<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Sudou-kun, memorize the problems that are worth a lot of points and those with the shortest answers.”<span class=\"pg\">p.241<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Steps in front of sulking Sudou after the exam and delivers her first genuine encouragement.<span class=\"pg\">p.244<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It was certainly your fault for not reviewing the old test’s final section. However, as you said, you did everything that you could with the time that you had. You didn’t cut any corners or give up. Considering how much effort you put in, I think you should hold your head high and feel proud.”<span class=\"pg\">p.244<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Comfort? I’m speaking the truth. When I look at how far you’ve come, I understand how hard studying is for you, Sudou.”<span class=\"pg\">p.244<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Amends her earlier scorn for his professional-basketball dream — having researched the actual career path — and bows her head in a formal apology.<span class=\"pg\">p.244–245<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I never thought I needed to understand anyone except for myself. So when you first told me that you wanted to play basketball, I insulted you. However, I now regret that. Someone who doesn’t understand how difficult, how arduous basketball is has no right to dismiss that dream as foolish.”<span class=\"pg\">p.245<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Sudou-kun, don’t forget the hard work and effort that you poured into studying. Apply that diligence to basketball. If you do, you might be able to go pro. At least, that’s how I feel.”<span class=\"pg\">p.245<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m sorry for what I said back then. Well. Now that I’ve said my piece, I’ll be going.”<span class=\"pg\">p.245<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Growth arc: converts hate into explicitly acknowledged working distrust; capable of researched, bow-level apology when her earlier judgment is proven wrong — delivered in her usual aloof manner but unmistakable.<span class=\"pg\">p.238, 244–245<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> Trusts utility over affection: proceeds &quot;without hesitation&quot; on a confirmed mutual hatred.<span class=\"pg\">p.237–238<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> From library tormentor to coach and apologizer — the pivot that fully wins his loyalty.<span class=\"pg\">p.241, 244–245<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v1-p203-1\">← Before: The reunion campaign: honesty, &quot;I hate you,&quot; and the in-class study plan<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v1-p249-1\">→ After: The 51-point sacrifice &amp; &quot;defective, not trash&quot;<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v1-p249-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"action spoken","w":"sudou-ken chabashira-sae ayanokouji-kiyotaka horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune the 51 point sacrifice    defective  not trash  breaks her lifelong pattern  raises her hand and speaks voluntarily for the first time all year  shocking chabashira and the class   earlier  you said that the previous test had a passing grade of thirty two points  you arrived at that number by the same formula you showed us today  were there no mistakes in calculating the passing grade for the last test   avg 64 4   2   32 2   they set 32  decimal dropped   inconsistency trap  the class realizes the truth  she scored  perfect in four subjects but deliberately botched english to 51    dragging the english average down so sudou s 39 would clear the threshold  after chabashira s rounding kill destroys the counter argument  mutters her apology to sudou   i m sorry  i should have tried to lower my score just a little more   don t misunderstand  i did this for my own sake  it was all for nothing  though   to sudou s  you said that you hated me  appears behind ayanokoji in the faculty room hallway and backs the point buying play without a second s hesitation   i ll pay  too   joining her id card to ak s for the 100 000 point purchase   i wonder  when i look at him  all i see is a disagreeable student   answering chabashira s talent question   lists his deliberate low scores  stolen credit  and test point purchase   i don t know about him  but i most definitely will   on reaching higher classes  returns chabashira s gaze and delivers her transformed class philosophy   honestly  maybe the students in class d are defective  however  that doesn t mean they re trash   the difference is paper thin  however  with repairs  a defective product may become a superior article  chops ayanokoji in the side as they return    for whatever  willing to burn her own exam score for a student who hates her  utility framed as self interest  publicly redefines her class from baggage to repairable material   the transformation chabashira visibly registers  secretly gambles her english grade to save him  frames it as  for my own sake  bests her once  forcing the rounding confession  loses the round  then wins her approval with the trash repairs answer  wordlessly joins the 100 000 point risk   the pact operating in practice","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v1-p249-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">The 51-point sacrifice &amp; &quot;defective, not trash&quot;<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.249–255<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a> · <a href=\"chabashira-sae.html\">Chabashira Sae<\/a> · <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Earlier, you said that the previous test had a passing grade of thirty-two points. You arrived at that number by the same formula you showed us today. Were there no mistakes in calculating the passing grade for the last test?”…”<span class=\"pg\">p.249<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I’m sorry. I should have tried to lower my score just a little more,”<span class=\"pg\">p.250<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Don’t misunderstand. I did this for my own sake. It was all for nothing, though.” (to Sudou&#x27;s &quot;You said that you hated me&quot;)<span class=\"pg\">p.250<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>16 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Breaks her lifelong pattern: raises her hand and speaks voluntarily for the first time all year, shocking Chabashira and the class.<span class=\"pg\">p.249<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Earlier, you said that the previous test had a passing grade of thirty-two points. You arrived at that number by the same formula you showed us today. Were there no mistakes in calculating the passing grade for the last test?” (avg 64.4 ÷ 2 = 32.2 → they set 32: decimal dropped — inconsistency trap)<span class=\"pg\">p.249<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> The class realizes the truth: she scored **perfect in four subjects but deliberately botched English to 51** — dragging the English average down so Sudou&#x27;s 39 would clear the threshold.<span class=\"pg\">p.249<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> After Chabashira&#x27;s rounding kill destroys the counter-argument, mutters her apology to Sudou.<span class=\"pg\">p.250<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Appears behind Ayanokōji in the faculty-room hallway and backs the point-buying play without a second&#x27;s hesitation.<span class=\"pg\">p.253<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’ll pay, too,” (joining her ID card to AK&#x27;s for the 100,000-point purchase)<span class=\"pg\">p.253<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I wonder. When I look at him, all I see is a disagreeable student.” (answering Chabashira&#x27;s talent question — lists his deliberate low scores, stolen credit, and test-point purchase)<span class=\"pg\">p.254<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I don’t know about him, but I most definitely will.” (on reaching higher classes)<span class=\"pg\">p.254<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Returns Chabashira&#x27;s gaze and delivers her transformed class philosophy.<span class=\"pg\">p.254<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Honestly, maybe the students in Class D are defective. However, that doesn’t mean they’re trash.”<span class=\"pg\">p.254<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “The difference is paper thin. However, with repairs, a defective product may become a superior article.”<span class=\"pg\">p.254<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Chops Ayanokōji in the side as they return — &quot;For whatever.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.255<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Willing to burn her own exam score for a student who hates her (utility-framed as self-interest); publicly redefines her class from baggage to repairable material — the transformation Chabashira visibly registers.<span class=\"pg\">p.249–255<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> Secretly gambles her English grade to save him; frames it as &quot;for my own sake.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.249–250<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> Bests her once (forcing the rounding confession), loses the round, then wins her approval with the trash/repairs answer.<span class=\"pg\">p.249, 254<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Wordlessly joins the 100,000-point risk — the pact operating in practice.<span class=\"pg\">p.253<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v1-p237-1\">← Before: The hate confirmation &amp; the basketball apology<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v1-p256-1\">→ After: The victory party: attending, deflecting, enlisting<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v1-p256-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"action spoken","w":"horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune the victory party  attending  deflecting  enlisting attends the celebration in ayanokoji s dorm room   sitting outside the circle  quietly reading a novel  narration flags her mere presence as progress the old horikita would never have allowed   i did it for my own sake  if someone had been expelled  class d s evaluation would ve worsened   her answer to the party s thanks   it d be fine with me if you didn t   rejecting ike s plea to just pretend she cares  when the party asks how the expulsion was reversed  plays total ignorance   preserving the point purchase secret   hmm  i don t really remember   our next challenge is the final exam  we should expect those questions to be even more difficult than the ones today  in addition  we still need to find a way to increase our points   drags celebration back to strategy   did you not see class d s average score  we were the lowest of all of the classes by far  if you think that we ll get points for that  then i think you need to open your eyes   i think you should learn to live a more modest life and give up on points   studying isn t the sole factor in deciding who goes into what class  though  right   planting the non academic path   i guess if you combined all three of their test scores  you d get one normal person s grade   systematically knocking down every morale boost kushida builds   i never wanted your help  sudou kun  besides  i have a hard time imagining how you ll be useful in the first place   thank you  i appreciate your words of praise   to sudou s  you re a really annoying girl   in this school  ability is paramount  i m positive that our competition will grow even more severe moving forward  if you say you ll work with us  know that you can t do so half heartedly  otherwise you ll be a burden   i really can t expect anything from you at all   to sudou s physical ability volunteering  progress without softening  attends  jokes in her own way  guards the secret  and converts a party into a war council   her will to class a declared unshakeable","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v1-p256-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">The victory party: attending, deflecting, enlisting<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.256–262<\/span><\/h3><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“I did it for my own sake. If someone had been expelled, Class D’s evaluation would’ve worsened.” (her answer to the party&#x27;s thanks)<span class=\"pg\">p.257<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“It’d be fine with me if you didn’t.” (rejecting Ike&#x27;s plea to just pretend she cares)<span class=\"pg\">p.257<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Hmm, I don’t really remember.”<span class=\"pg\">p.257<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>12 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Attends the celebration in Ayanokōji&#x27;s dorm room — sitting outside the circle, quietly reading a novel; narration flags her mere presence as progress the old Horikita would never have allowed.<span class=\"pg\">p.256–257<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> When the party asks how the expulsion was reversed, plays total ignorance — preserving the point-purchase secret.<span class=\"pg\">p.257<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Our next challenge is the final exam. We should expect those questions to be even more difficult than the ones today. In addition, we still need to find a way to increase our points.” (drags celebration back to strategy)<span class=\"pg\">p.257<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Did you not see Class D’s average score? We were the lowest of all of the classes by far. If you think that we’ll get points for that, then I think you need to open your eyes.”<span class=\"pg\">p.258<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I think you should learn to live a more modest life and give up on points.”<span class=\"pg\">p.258<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Studying isn’t the sole factor in deciding who goes into what class, though. Right?” (planting the non-academic path)<span class=\"pg\">p.258<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I guess if you combined all three of their test scores, you’d get one normal person’s grade.” (systematically knocking down every morale boost Kushida builds)<span class=\"pg\">p.261<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I never wanted your help, Sudou-kun. Besides, I have a hard time imagining how you’ll be useful in the first place.”<span class=\"pg\">p.261<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Thank you. I appreciate your words of praise.” (to Sudou&#x27;s &quot;You&#x27;re a really annoying girl&quot;)<span class=\"pg\">p.261<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “In this school, ability is paramount. I’m positive that our competition will grow even more severe moving forward. If you say you’ll work with us, know that you can’t do so half-heartedly. Otherwise you’ll be a burden.”<span class=\"pg\">p.262<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I really can’t expect anything from you at all.” (to Sudou&#x27;s physical-ability volunteering)<span class=\"pg\">p.262<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Progress without softening: attends, jokes-in-her-own-way, guards the secret, and converts a party into a war council — her will to Class A declared unshakeable.<span class=\"pg\">p.256–262<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v1-p249-1\">← Before: The 51-point sacrifice &amp; &quot;defective, not trash&quot;<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p17-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune ch 2  2 1  july 1  reading the point board correctly  this isn t good  could they have figured out a way to increase their point total   it s too early to celebrate  all the other classes saw a similar increase in their points  we didn t close the distance at all  this might just be a reward first year students receive for getting through the midterm  every class seems to have gotten at least 100 points   so that s what happened  i thought it odd that we d been awarded points so quickly   no  that s not it  we managed to get something this time  after all   to ak s jab about the widening gap  then falls silent  refusing to explain  only student tracking other classes  totals  celebration proof   measures relative gap  not absolute gain","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p17-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2 §2.1 (July 1): reading the point board correctly<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.17–18<\/span><\/h3><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;This isn’t good. Could they have figured out a way to increase their point total?!&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.17<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;It’s too early to celebrate. All the other classes saw a similar increase in their points. We didn’t close the distance at all. This might just be a reward first-year students receive for getting through the midterm. Every class…<span class=\"pg\">p.17<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;So that’s what happened. I thought it odd that we’d been awarded points so quickly.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.17<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;It’s too early to celebrate. All the other classes saw a similar increase in their points. We didn’t close the distance at all. This might just be a reward first-year students receive for getting through the midterm. Every class seems to have gotten at least 100 points.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.17<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;No, that’s not it. We managed to get something this time, after all.&quot; (to AK&#x27;s jab about the widening gap; then falls silent, refusing to explain)<span class=\"pg\">p.17<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Only student tracking other classes&#x27; totals; celebration-proof — measures relative gap, not absolute gain.<span class=\"pg\">p.17<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p19-1\">→ After: Ch.2 §2.2 (lunch): the bento era<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p19-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune ch 2  2 2  lunch  the bento era  you re still not used to it  you re as pathetic as ever  ayanokouji kun   noticing him scanning for lunch invitations   i m quite fine  thank you   his sarcasm about her solitude taken literally   i m not sure about that  the school supermarket provides free ingredients  you know   anyone can cook by looking up a recipe in a book or on the internet  our dorms come equipped with all of the necessary tools  as well   the cafeteria is noisy  it s much more relaxing to eat here  wouldn t you say   you re always staring out at the ocean  but you don t have a surfboard  you lack even the determination to ride the wave  don t you  and you talk about missing it  you re awfully full of yourself  new budget coping routine  home made bento from free supermarket ingredients  refuses the free cafeteria subsidy optics  roasts ak with ocean surfboard metaphor unprompted","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p19-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2 §2.2 (lunch): the bento era<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.19–21<\/span><\/h3><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;You’re still not used to it. You’re as pathetic as ever, Ayanokouji-kun.&quot; (noticing him scanning for lunch invitations)<span class=\"pg\">p.19<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I’m quite fine, thank you.&quot; (his sarcasm about her solitude taken literally)<span class=\"pg\">p.20<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I’m not sure about that. The school supermarket provides free ingredients, you know.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.20<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Anyone can cook by looking up a recipe in a book or on the Internet. Our dorms come equipped with all of the necessary tools, as well.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.21<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;The cafeteria is noisy. It’s much more relaxing to eat here, wouldn’t you say?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.21<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;You’re always staring out at the ocean, but you don’t have a surfboard. You lack even the determination to ride the wave, don’t you? And you talk about missing it? You’re awfully full of yourself.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.21<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> New budget coping routine: home-made bento from free supermarket ingredients; refuses the free-cafeteria-subsidy optics; roasts AK with ocean/surfboard metaphor unprompted.<span class=\"pg\">p.19–21<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p17-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.1 (July 1): reading the point board correctly<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p22-1\">→ After: Ch.2 §2.3 (after school): points paranoia, chat refusal, oil and water<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p22-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka kushida-kikyou sudou-ken horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune ch 2  2 3  after school  points paranoia  chat refusal  oil and water  do you think so  too  that it would have been better if sudou kun were expelled   opening  while packing every textbook   hmm  well  we still don t know whether our points would go up as a class  really   on her own midterm rescue of sudou   feigned disinterest   i m a little worried about what chabashira sensei said this morning   yes  she said that there was trouble  but did she mean that it was a problem for the school  or a problem for us  the students  if it s the latter  then   i hope that s the case  trouble directly affects our points   i m not interested in the slightest  also  i keep my notifications turned off   class group chat  joined but zero participation  keeps the app so leaving won t notify kushida   you ve been quite talkative lately  ayanokouji kun   it s a slight difference  but you ve changed   did something make you change   you seem to be getting along quite well with kushida san  aren t you bothered  especially knowing about her other side   hmm  well  you may have a point there  it s true that i hate you  too  ayanokouji kun  yet i talk to you normally  i don t really mind  then   that s what i m getting at  if someone says that they hate another person  it s fine  but if someone says that they hate you  don t you feel a little bad   i don t have any intention of getting in her way  but kushida san and i are like oil and water  i think it s better not to associate with her   who knows  she probably doesn t know that much about me   if you re that curious  why don t you ask her yourself  directly   what you just said was really disgusting  you know that   reaction to  i m fine with the kushida we have now  runs the worst case simulation on every institutional signal  her hate lines are delivered analytically  then re used as a lesson about honesty  deliberate testing of ak  his   were you testing me  daily walk back ritual  she monitors his behavioral drift and says so  conversation register now includes open hostility as rapport  it s true that i hate you  too  ayanokouji kun  yet i talk to you normally  declares them  like oil and water  refuses any shared group engagement with her  genuinely does not know kushida s rooftop face  won t call for his expulsion yet discounts defending him publicly  frames everything through class point consequences","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p22-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2 §2.3 (after school): points paranoia, chat refusal, oil and water<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.22–26<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a> · <a href=\"sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Do you think so, too? That it would have been better if Sudou-kun were expelled?&quot; (opening, while packing every textbook)<span class=\"pg\">p.22<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Hmm. Well, we still don’t know whether our points would go up as a class, really,&quot; (on her own midterm rescue of Sudou — feigned disinterest)<span class=\"pg\">p.23<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I’m a little worried about what Chabashira-sensei said this morning,&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.22<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>17 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Yes. She said that there was trouble, but did she mean that it was a problem for the school, or a problem for us, the students? If it’s the latter, then…&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.22<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I hope that’s the case. Trouble directly affects our points.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.23<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I’m not interested in the slightest. Also, I keep my notifications turned off.&quot; (class group chat: joined but zero participation; keeps the app so leaving won&#x27;t notify Kushida)<span class=\"pg\">p.24<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;You’ve been quite talkative lately, Ayanokouji-kun.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.24<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;It’s a slight difference, but you’ve changed.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.24<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Did something make you change?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.25<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;You seem to be getting along quite well with Kushida-san. Aren’t you bothered, especially knowing about her other side?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.25<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Hmm. Well, you may have a point there. It’s true that I hate you, too, Ayanokouji-kun, yet I talk to you normally. I don’t really mind, then.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.25<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;That’s what I’m getting at. If someone says that they hate another person, it’s fine. But if someone says that they hate you, don’t you feel a little bad?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.25<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I don’t have any intention of getting in her way, but Kushida-san and I are like oil and water. I think it’s better not to associate with her.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.25<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Who knows? She probably doesn’t know that much about me.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.25<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;If you’re that curious, why don’t you ask her yourself? Directly?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.25<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;What you just said was really disgusting, you know that?&quot; (reaction to &quot;I&#x27;m fine with the Kushida we have now&quot;)<span class=\"pg\">p.26<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Runs the worst-case simulation on every institutional signal; her hate lines are delivered analytically, then re-used as a lesson about honesty; deliberate testing of AK (his: &quot;Were you testing me?&quot;).<span class=\"pg\">p.22–26<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Daily walk-back ritual; she monitors his behavioral drift and says so; conversation register now includes open hostility-as-rapport (&quot;It’s true that I hate you, too, Ayanokouji-kun, yet I talk to you normally&quot;).<span class=\"pg\">p.19–26<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> Declares them &quot;like oil and water&quot;; refuses any shared-group engagement with her; genuinely does not know Kushida&#x27;s rooftop face.<span class=\"pg\">p.25<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> Won&#x27;t call for his expulsion yet discounts defending him publicly; frames everything through class-point consequences.<span class=\"pg\">p.22–23<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p19-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.2 (lunch): the bento era<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p44-1\">→ After: Ch.3 §3.1 (cafeteria): refusing Sudou in front of the group<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p44-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune ch 3  3 1  cafeteria  refusing sudou in front of the group  you seem to get yourself into trouble time and time again  sudou kun   sorry  but i don t feel like helping you this time   for class d to rise through the ranks  it s important to recover the class points we lost as quickly as possible  however  we probably won t get any points now  thanks to you  you hindered those plans   you keep focusing on who started the fight  but that s a trivial detail  did you never consider that   is that so  well  best of luck to you   don t make me laugh  i ve never once considered you a friend  nothing makes me more uncomfortable than being around someone who doesn t recognize his own stupidity  goodbye  the refusal is delivered as arithmetic  not malice   horikita appeared more exasperated than angry  she let out a deep sigh  and left  she takes her tray and sits elsewhere in the cafeteria  ak watches her  looking slightly irritated  while the group tries to work out her reasons without her   what idea  to toss me out like the trash   sudou throwing her refusal back at ak","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p44-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3 §3.1 (cafeteria): refusing Sudou in front of the group<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.44–47<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">She takes her tray and sits elsewhere in the cafeteria; AK watches her &quot;looking slightly irritated&quot; while the group tries to work out her reasons without her.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“You seem to get yourself into trouble time and time again, Sudou-kun.”<span class=\"pg\">p.44<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Sorry, but I don’t feel like helping you this time.”<span class=\"pg\">p.44<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“For Class D to rise through the ranks, it’s important to recover the class points we lost as quickly as possible. However, we probably won’t get any points now, thanks to you. You hindered those plans.”<span class=\"pg\">p.44<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You keep focusing on who started the fight, but that’s a trivial detail. Did you never consider that?”<span class=\"pg\">p.44<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Is that so? Well, best of luck to you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.45<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Don’t make me laugh. I’ve never once considered you a friend. Nothing makes me more uncomfortable than being around someone who doesn’t recognize his own stupidity. Goodbye.”<span class=\"pg\">p.45<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The refusal is delivered as arithmetic, not malice: &quot;Horikita appeared more exasperated than angry. She let out a deep sigh, and left.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.45<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What idea? To toss me out like the trash?” (Sudou throwing her refusal back at AK)<span class=\"pg\">p.47<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p22-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.3 (after school): points paranoia, chat refusal, oil and water<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p54-1\">→ After: Ch.3 §3.2: walked out on, chased down, and still not moved<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p54-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune ch 3  3 2  walked out on  chased down  and still not moved announces  all right  i m going to the dorms  nods  without hesitation  and leaves  she  didn t quail under everyone s gazes  which all expressed variations on  you re leaving  ak s portrait of the manner   she would probably grow up to be a fierce woman  the type that leaves social outings without reading the room and concludes meetings exactly on time   what is it   i thought i already declined  a few minutes ago  no less   you re free to run about for sudou kun s sake  i ve no right to stop you  however  if you need help  try someone else  i m busy   i have an important daily routine  so i need my alone time  it s unpleasant to have that time stolen from me   even if i step in and save him now  he ll land himself in trouble again  it s a vicious cycle  isn t it  you seem to think that sudou kun is the victim here  but i think differently   maybe the class c students really did start this fight  but sudou kun was also one of the perpetrators   why was he dragged into the fight  this problem will persist until we understand that fundamental question  got it  i do not wish to help until that question is answered  since you weren t able to convince me  why don t you ask the guy standing next to you  even though he pretends not to understand what i m thinking  he probably does  kushida s  necessary to reach class a  argument bounces off her because she is not arguing about points  she sets a precondition  explain why the fight happened  that no one in the class is willing to meet  then walks  in front of kushida she claims ak reads her mind   the first time the private shorthand between them is asserted to a third party  ak s reaction is refusal   please stop saying that i understand you  ak s gloss on her motive  said only in his own head   horikita wasn t the type to teach through kindness  she didn t feel an obligation to others","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p54-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3 §3.2: walked out on, chased down, and still not moved<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.54–57<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Announces &quot;All right, I’m going to the dorms,&quot; nods &quot;without hesitation&quot; and leaves; she &quot;didn’t quail under everyone’s gazes, which all expressed variations on &#x27;You’re leaving?&#x27;&quot;<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“What is it?”<span class=\"pg\">p.56<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I thought I already declined? A few minutes ago, no less.”<span class=\"pg\">p.56<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“You’re free to run about for Sudou-kun’s sake. I’ve no right to stop you. However, if you need help, try someone else. I’m busy,”<span class=\"pg\">p.56<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>8 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> AK&#x27;s portrait of the manner: &quot;She would probably grow up to be a fierce woman, the type that leaves social outings without reading the room and concludes meetings exactly on time.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.54<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I have an important daily routine, so I need my alone time. It’s unpleasant to have that time stolen from me.”<span class=\"pg\">p.56<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Even if I step in and save him now, he’ll land himself in trouble again. It’s a vicious cycle, isn’t it? You seem to think that Sudou-kun is the victim here, but I think differently.”<span class=\"pg\">p.56<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Maybe the Class C students really did start this fight, but Sudou-kun was also one of the perpetrators.”<span class=\"pg\">p.56<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Why was he dragged into the fight? This problem will persist until we understand that fundamental question. Got it? I do not wish to help until that question is answered. Since you weren’t able to convince me, why don’t you ask the guy standing next to you? Even though he pretends not to understand what I’m thinking, he probably does.”<span class=\"pg\">p.57<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Kushida&#x27;s &quot;necessary to reach Class A&quot; argument bounces off her because she is not arguing about points: she sets a precondition (explain why the fight happened) that no one in the class is willing to meet, then walks.<span class=\"pg\">p.56–57<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> In front of Kushida she claims AK reads her mind — the first time the private shorthand between them is asserted to a third party. AK&#x27;s reaction is refusal: &quot;Please stop saying that I understand you.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.57<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Backstory<\/span> AK&#x27;s gloss on her motive, said only in his own head: &quot;Horikita wasn’t the type to teach through kindness. She didn’t feel an obligation to others.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p44-1\">← Before: Ch.3 §3.1 (cafeteria): refusing Sudou in front of the group<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p67-1\">→ After: Ch.4 §4.0: the class-change question, and a point-based reason to save Sudou<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p67-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune ch 4  4 0  the class change question  and a point based reason to save sudou she is the only student in the room who reacts to the class s griping with contempt  and ak is the only one who sees it   horikita spontaneously broke into derisive laughter in response to ike and karuizawa s delusions  as her neighbor  i was the only one who noticed  her reading material while the class argues about points   horikita immediately took out a library book and began reading  almost as if she was trying not to be distracted by the noise  at a glance  i saw she was reading dostoevsky s demons  chabashira s announcement of a paid class change lands on her first   horikita looked up from her book  probably trying to gauge whether chabashira sensei was lying   may i ask one question  please    ak   the watchful horikita raised her hand  she looked quite determined  considering this was a potential road to class a   what is the highest number of points that a student has saved since the opening of this school  i m just asking for the sake of reference   so  you re saying that even if we were to use criminal methods  12 million points is about the limit    ak s tag   horikita muttered  she drops the subject the moment the answer arrives   horikita returned to reading  likely feeling idiotic for bothering to raise her hand at all   we should save him because he s in a club    her first question back to ak s argument that sudou has point value   i have a hard time imagining that he d use his points altruistically  though   i won t say that i ll help  but i suppose i ought to acknowledge sudou s existence  at least a little    the movement ak gets out of her in this chapter  stated as little as possible   horikita s language was harsh  but she acknowledged the connection to her own interests  she asks the school for data  not for sympathy  the only two questions she volunteers in the chapter are about the maximum points ever saved and whether the rule is a lie   and she stops arguing the moment the arithmetic says no  chabashira s claim that a class can be bought is verified by exactly two people in the room  and the teacher s glance names them   chabashira sensei shot a quick glance over at horikita and me  we had tested out that very method ourselves by buying a test point from the school","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p67-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.4 §4.0: the class-change question, and a point-based reason to save Sudou<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.67–73<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Her reading material while the class argues about points: &quot;Horikita immediately took out a library book and began reading, almost as if she was trying not to be distracted by the noise. At a glance, I saw she was reading Dostoevsky’s Demons.&quot; Chabashira&#x27;s announcement of a paid class change lands on her first: &quot;Horikita looked up from her book, probably trying to gauge whether Chabashira-sensei was lying.&quot; She drops the subject the moment the answer arrives: &quot;Horikita returned to reading, likely feeling idiotic for bothering to raise her hand at all.&quot;<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;May I ask one question, please?&quot; — AK: &quot;The watchful Horikita raised her hand. She looked quite determined, considering this was a potential road to Class A.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.70<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;What is the highest number of points that a student has saved since the opening of this school? I’m just asking for the sake of reference.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.70<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;So, you’re saying that even if we were to use criminal methods, 12 million points is about the limit?&quot; — AK&#x27;s tag: &quot;Horikita muttered.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.70<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> She is the only student in the room who reacts to the class&#x27;s griping with contempt, and AK is the only one who sees it: &quot;Horikita spontaneously broke into derisive laughter in response to Ike and Karuizawa’s delusions. As her neighbor, I was the only one who noticed.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.67<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;We should save him because he’s in a club?&quot; — her first question back to AK&#x27;s argument that Sudou has point value.<span class=\"pg\">p.72<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I have a hard time imagining that he’d use his points altruistically, though.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.72<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I won’t say that I’ll help, but I suppose I ought to acknowledge Sudou’s existence, at least a little.&quot; — the movement AK gets out of her in this chapter, stated as little as possible: &quot;Horikita’s language was harsh, but she acknowledged the connection to her own interests.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.73<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> She asks the school for data, not for sympathy: the only two questions she volunteers in the chapter are about the maximum points ever saved and whether the rule is a lie — and she stops arguing the moment the arithmetic says no.<span class=\"pg\">p.67–73<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Chabashira&#x27;s claim that a class can be bought is verified by exactly two people in the room, and the teacher&#x27;s glance names them: &quot;Chabashira-sensei shot a quick glance over at Horikita and me. We had tested out that very method ourselves by buying a test point from the school.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.68<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p54-1\">← Before: Ch.3 §3.2: walked out on, chased down, and still not moved<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p75-1\">→ After: Ch.4 §4.1: she names the witness, and refuses the credit<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p75-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"kushida-kikyou sudou-ken horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune ch 4  4 1  she names the witness  and refuses the credit she appears at ak s door unannounced  the first time in the volume she seeks him out   just then  my doorbell rang and a visitor appeared  while i considered who this new visitor might be  she peered through the door   have you made any progress finding the witness    ak   asked horikita  looking as if she already knew the response   i m only telling you this because it s you  but i may have found out something    she stops mid sentence on seeing shoes at the door and turns to leave  kushida s wave forces her in   i didn t particularly plan on helping  you don t appear to have found the witness yet  right  her verdict on kushida s plan  given without being asked to join it   i wouldn t say it s a bad plan  provided you have sufficient time  your labors may actually bear fruit   i ll give you just one piece of advice  to help your pathetic odds    then the advice itself   it s hard to see what s right in front of you  if someone actually witnessed sudou s incident  then that person is close by   sakura san    then  on being pressed   she s the witness  she saw the incident  the whole method  in one answer   when kushida san said that she was looking for a witness in class  sakura looked down  a lot of students were staring at kushida san  sakura was the only one who didn t appear interested  she wouldn t have acted that way without some connection to the incident  ak s measure of what she did   i hadn t noticed that at all  i was genuinely impressed by horikita s observational prowess  she d noticed a classmate s very minor gesture    and his summary of the chapter s turn   while we d been paralyzed by uncertainty  horikita had stepped up and taken control   no  sakura san is undoubtedly the witness  her actions confirmed it  although she may not admit to it  she is definitely the one  she rejects the rescue narrative outright   don t misunderstand  i just didn t want to waste more time looking for the witness  and letting other classes see us in such a shameful light  that s all  and  you are free to interpret things however you wish  but i m telling you that you re wrong  she will move on reasons but never on appeal   the difference between ak s point argument  which lands  and ike s or sudou s gratitude  which she calls wrong  ike s playful shove on the shoulder ends with her tossing him to the ground and putting him in a headlock   don t touch me  this is your one warning  the next time you try it  i ll despise you all the way to graduation  ak s note on the technique   those weren t the defensive moves of a normal girl  since i knew that her older brother practiced karate and aikido  she might have learned something  too  she leaves the second the room turns to teasing her    goodbye    before anyone can convert her help into belonging  kushida is the one who physically keeps her in the room and then the one who asks for her advice  she answers kushida s plan with a judgement  not participation  she refuses to let him believe she did it for him  twice  in the same breath in which she hands him the witness","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p75-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.4 §4.1: she names the witness, and refuses the credit<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.75–81<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">She appears at AK&#x27;s door unannounced, the first time in the volume she seeks him out: &quot;Just then, my doorbell rang and a visitor appeared... While I considered who this new visitor might be, she peered through the door.&quot;<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a> · <a href=\"sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Have you made any progress finding the witness?&quot; — AK: &quot;asked Horikita, looking as if she already knew the response.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.75<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I’m only telling you this because it’s you, but I may have found out something—&quot; — she stops mid-sentence on seeing shoes at the door and turns to leave; Kushida&#x27;s wave forces her in.<span class=\"pg\">p.76<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I didn’t particularly plan on helping. You don’t appear to have found the witness yet, right?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.76<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>12 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> Her verdict on Kushida&#x27;s plan, given without being asked to join it: &quot;I wouldn’t say it’s a bad plan. Provided you have sufficient time, your labors may actually bear fruit.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.76<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I’ll give you just one piece of advice, to help your pathetic odds,&quot; — then the advice itself: &quot;It’s hard to see what’s right in front of you. If someone actually witnessed Sudou’s incident, then that person is close by.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.77<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Sakura-san.&quot; — then, on being pressed: &quot;She’s the witness. She saw the incident.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.77<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> The whole method, in one answer: &quot;When Kushida-san said that she was looking for a witness in class, Sakura looked down. A lot of students were staring at Kushida-san. Sakura was the only one who didn’t appear interested. She wouldn’t have acted that way without some connection to the incident.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.77<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> AK&#x27;s measure of what she did: &quot;I hadn’t noticed that at all. I was genuinely impressed by Horikita’s observational prowess. She’d noticed a classmate’s very minor gesture.&quot; — and his summary of the chapter&#x27;s turn: &quot;While we’d been paralyzed by uncertainty, Horikita had stepped up and taken control.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.77<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;No, Sakura-san is undoubtedly the witness. Her actions confirmed it. Although she may not admit to it, she is definitely the one.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.78<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> She rejects the rescue narrative outright: &quot;Don’t misunderstand. I just didn’t want to waste more time looking for the witness, and letting other classes see us in such a shameful light. That’s all.&quot; and &quot;You are free to interpret things however you wish, but I’m telling you that you’re wrong.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.78<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Limit<\/span> She will move on reasons but never on appeal — the difference between AK&#x27;s point argument, which lands, and Ike&#x27;s or Sudou&#x27;s gratitude, which she calls wrong.<span class=\"pg\">p.73, p.78<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Ike&#x27;s playful shove on the shoulder ends with her tossing him to the ground and putting him in a headlock: &quot;Don’t touch me. This is your one warning. The next time you try it, I’ll despise you all the way to graduation.&quot; AK&#x27;s note on the technique: &quot;those weren’t the defensive moves of a normal girl. Since I knew that her older brother practiced karate and aikido, she might have learned something, too?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.78<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> She leaves the second the room turns to teasing her — &quot;Goodbye.&quot; — before anyone can convert her help into belonging.<span class=\"pg\">p.81<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> Kushida is the one who physically keeps her in the room and then the one who asks for her advice; she answers Kushida&#x27;s plan with a judgement, not participation.<span class=\"pg\">p.76–80<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> She refuses to let him believe she did it for him, twice, in the same breath in which she hands him the witness.<span class=\"pg\">p.78<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p67-1\">← Before: Ch.4 §4.0: the class-change question, and a point-based reason to save Sudou<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p88-1\">→ After: Ch.4 §4.2–4.3: she writes Sudou off out loud, and prices the witness<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p88-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune ch 4  4 2 4 3  she writes sudou off out loud  and prices the witness  my  how unfortunate  kushida failed to persuade her    spoken as kushida s approach to sakura collapses in front of the class  ak agrees   horikita was correct  if kushida couldn t do it  then i didn t think that anyone else in our class would be able to  the thesis she alone will say  that a bad witness is a better outcome   she won t testify on your behalf  they ll determine you caused the incident  in the end  class d will be affected by your actions  but we ll be okay  we have testimony that they lied about the violence  it s hard to imagine that the school would penalize us by more than 100 or 200 points for being involved in this incident  that way we ll only lose 87 points  and you won t face expulsion  however  we ll shoulder more of the blame than class c will  ak s tag on that speech   horikita relentlessly spoke her thoughts out loud  as if she d been hiding them deep inside her all this time   i don t think self defense is all that helpful in this case    to sudou  after he invokes it again   even your friends don t wish to help you  how unfortunate    and when sudou calls the class useless jerks   what an interesting thing to say  sudou kun  haven t you noticed that everyone is turning on you   i don t show mercy to people who don t attempt to better themselves  he s caused us nothing but harm  and has no redeeming features    ak s silent counter   well  you don t exactly show any mercy even to people who do attempt such things   i don t intend to deny that it could happen in 10 years  time  but i m looking for things to help me reach class a right now  if he can t help us right now  then he s worthless to me  ike is the one she interrogates about sudou s actual character   you get along with sudou  don t you  you eat together with him  her evidentiary standard  delivered as a dismissal of the whole search   considering the circumstances  even if we get sakura san s testimony  i believe it ll have minimal impact  the school will probably have doubts about a witness just suddenly appearing from class d  and  they ll consider the witness s testimony along with her possible intentions  they won t take her word as absolute proof  the only case that would actually work   the best and most miraculous situation would be if there was a trusted witness from another class or grade who saw the entire incident from start to finish  there isn t anyone who fits that description  though    ak   said horikita with confidence  and  i thought the same  she takes no part in stopping sudou from hitting koenji  the physical intervention is hirata s  and her contribution is the sentence that made him angry enough to need it","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p88-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.4 §4.2–4.3: she writes Sudou off out loud, and prices the witness<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.88–94<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Ike is the one she interrogates about Sudou&#x27;s actual character: &quot;You get along with Sudou, don’t you? You eat together with him.&quot;<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;My, how unfortunate. Kushida failed to persuade her.&quot; — spoken as Kushida&#x27;s approach to Sakura collapses in front of the class; AK agrees: &quot;Horikita was correct. If Kushida couldn’t do it, then I didn’t think that anyone else in…<span class=\"pg\">p.88<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">The thesis she alone will say, that a bad witness is a better outcome: &quot;She won’t testify on your behalf. They’ll determine you caused the incident. In the end, Class D will be affected by your actions, but we’ll be okay. We have…<span class=\"pg\">p.90–91<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I don’t think self-defense is all that helpful in this case.&quot; — to Sudou, after he invokes it again.<span class=\"pg\">p.91<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>9 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;My, how unfortunate. Kushida failed to persuade her.&quot; — spoken as Kushida&#x27;s approach to Sakura collapses in front of the class; AK agrees: &quot;Horikita was correct. If Kushida couldn’t do it, then I didn’t think that anyone else in our class would be able to.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.88<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> The thesis she alone will say, that a bad witness is a better outcome: &quot;She won’t testify on your behalf. They’ll determine you caused the incident. In the end, Class D will be affected by your actions, but we’ll be okay. We have testimony that they lied about the violence. It’s hard to imagine that the school would penalize us by more than 100 or 200 points for being involved in this incident. That way we’ll only lose 87 points, and you won’t face expulsion. However, we’ll shoulder more of the blame than Class C will.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.90–91<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> AK&#x27;s tag on that speech: &quot;Horikita relentlessly spoke her thoughts out loud, as if she’d been hiding them deep inside her all this time.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.91<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Even your friends don’t wish to help you. How unfortunate,&quot; — and when Sudou calls the class useless jerks: &quot;What an interesting thing to say, Sudou-kun. Haven’t you noticed that everyone is turning on you?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.91<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I don’t show mercy to people who don’t attempt to better themselves. He’s caused us nothing but harm, and has no redeeming features.&quot; — AK&#x27;s silent counter: &quot;Well, you don’t exactly show any mercy even to people who do attempt such things.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.93<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I don’t intend to deny that it could happen in 10 years’ time, but I’m looking for things to help me reach Class A right now. If he can’t help us right now, then he’s worthless to me.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.94<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> Her evidentiary standard, delivered as a dismissal of the whole search: &quot;Considering the circumstances, even if we get Sakura-san’s testimony, I believe it’ll have minimal impact. The school will probably have doubts about a witness just suddenly appearing from Class D.&quot; and &quot;They’ll consider the witness’s testimony along with her possible intentions. They won’t take her word as absolute proof.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.94<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> The only case that would actually work: &quot;the best and most miraculous situation would be if there was a trusted witness from another class or grade who saw the entire incident from start to finish. There isn’t anyone who fits that description, though,&quot; — AK: &quot;said Horikita with confidence.&quot; and &quot;I thought the same.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.94<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Limit<\/span> She takes no part in stopping Sudou from hitting Kōenji; the physical intervention is Hirata&#x27;s, and her contribution is the sentence that made him angry enough to need it.<span class=\"pg\">p.93<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p75-1\">← Before: Ch.4 §4.1: she names the witness, and refuses the credit<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p95-1\">→ After: Ch.4 §4.4: she invites Ayanokōji out, and decides on Class B<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p95-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka ichinose-honami horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune ch 4  4 4  she invites ayanokoji out  and decides on class b she initiates  for the first time in the volume   ayanokouji kun  do you want to head back together    and asks for a ten minute stop on the way   it should only take about 10 minutes  she absorbs an unasked for physical check without punishment  after ak s hand goes to her forehead she says only  do you mind  your hand    where minutes earlier she had put ike in a headlock for touching her shoulder  a contrast ak s own line records  her first question at the special building is about him  not the case   you ve really changed  haven t you  it s odd that you stuck your neck out in this case  the witness has already been found  and we ve confirmed that there s nothing left to be done  what are you even trying to do   well  your way of thinking isn t relevant to me  ayanokouji kun  so you re free to think whatever you like  also  i appreciate that you say those two are hard to deal with    and on being asked whether she just hates hirata and kushida   having a common enemy tends to lead to cooperation  she audits the building for evidence rather than waiting for it    looks like there aren t any here  too bad  and  when asked what she means   cameras  like the ones in the classrooms  if there were cameras here  we d have solid evidence  i can t find any    and sets the rule s boundary   if i had to think of places where they wouldn t be installed  i d probably say the bathrooms and the locker rooms  right  her actual objective  once she stops pretending she has none   sudou has many qualities i can t stomach  however  i want to lessen the blame they re placing upon him  the best possible outcome is we ll still have some points  even if class d s image worsens    ak s note   she sounded honest  normally  she wasn t quite so candid   like i said  unless a perfect witness appears  proving sudou kun s innocence will be impossible  if those class c students admitted that they lied  i suppose things might turn out fine  do you think that s likely  she steps at a stranger the instant an opening appears   i have something i d like to ask you  sakura san    and ak has to physically restrain her from pursuing   i tried to gently restrain horikita  gesturing for her for stop chasing sakura   i can t help but think there s an ulterior motive    to ichinose  uninvited  before any question is answered   i don t want to talk with someone who is  just curious  do what you want    ak   horikita tried to put some distance between them   are you finished  you heard what you wanted     horikita spoke sharply and with a sigh  trying to drive ichinose away  the reversal  in one sentence  after weighing nothing out loud   let s accept her help  ayanokouji kun    ak   horikita had made a decision  probably determining that the benefits outweighed the risks  she gives her name first  which ak reads as the act of opening an alliance   horikita gave her name candidly  as if doing so approved our cooperative relationship   this is the first i m hearing about it affecting our class points  i ll have to complain to chabashira sensei later    ak   mumbled horikita  a little disgruntled  she accepts being cast as the threat in his speech to sakura without argument   are you talking about me    muttered  then dropped  hostility on sight  then a partnership in the same afternoon  she is the one who says no twice  the one who says yes  and the one whose name seals it","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p95-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.4 §4.4: she invites Ayanokōji out, and decides on Class B<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.95–107<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">She initiates, for the first time in the volume: &quot;Ayanokouji-kun, do you want to head back together?&quot; — and asks for a ten-minute stop on the way, &quot;It should only take about 10 minutes.&quot; She steps at a stranger the instant an opening appears: &quot;I have something I’d like to ask you, Sakura-san,&quot; — and AK has to physically restrain her from pursuing: &quot;I tried to gently restrain Horikita, gesturing for her for stop chasing Sakura.&quot;<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">Her first question at the special building is about him, not the case: &quot;You’ve really changed, haven’t you? It’s odd that you stuck your neck out in this case. The witness has already been found, and we’ve confirmed that there’s…<span class=\"pg\">p.97<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Well, your way of thinking isn’t relevant to me, Ayanokouji-kun, so you’re free to think whatever you like. Also, I appreciate that you say those two are hard to deal with.&quot; — and on being asked whether she just hates Hirata and…<span class=\"pg\">p.98<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">Her actual objective, once she stops pretending she has none: &quot;Sudou has many qualities I can’t stomach. However, I want to lessen the blame they’re placing upon him. The best possible outcome is we’ll still have some points…<span class=\"pg\">p.99<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>14 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> She absorbs an unasked-for physical check without punishment: after AK&#x27;s hand goes to her forehead she says only &quot;Do you mind? Your hand.&quot; — where minutes earlier she had put Ike in a headlock for touching her shoulder, a contrast AK&#x27;s own line records.<span class=\"pg\">p.95–96<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> Her first question at the special building is about him, not the case: &quot;You’ve really changed, haven’t you? It’s odd that you stuck your neck out in this case. The witness has already been found, and we’ve confirmed that there’s nothing left to be done. What are you even trying to do?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.97<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Well, your way of thinking isn’t relevant to me, Ayanokouji-kun, so you’re free to think whatever you like. Also, I appreciate that you say those two are hard to deal with.&quot; — and on being asked whether she just hates Hirata and Kushida: &quot;Having a common enemy tends to lead to cooperation.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.98<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> She audits the building for evidence rather than waiting for it — &quot;Looks like there aren’t any here. Too bad,&quot; and, when asked what she means: &quot;Cameras, like the ones in the classrooms. If there were cameras here, we’d have solid evidence. I can’t find any.&quot; — and sets the rule&#x27;s boundary: &quot;If I had to think of places where they wouldn’t be installed, I’d probably say the bathrooms and the locker rooms. Right?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.98<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> Her actual objective, once she stops pretending she has none: &quot;Sudou has many qualities I can’t stomach. However, I want to lessen the blame they’re placing upon him. The best possible outcome is we’ll still have some points, even if Class D’s image worsens.&quot; — AK&#x27;s note: &quot;She sounded honest. Normally, she wasn’t quite so candid.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.99<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Like I said, unless a perfect witness appears, proving Sudou-kun’s innocence will be impossible. If those Class C students admitted that they lied, I suppose things might turn out fine. Do you think that’s likely?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.99–100<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I can’t help but think there’s an ulterior motive,&quot; — to Ichinose, uninvited, before any question is answered.<span class=\"pg\">p.104<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I don’t want to talk with someone who is ‘just curious.’ Do what you want.&quot; — AK: &quot;Horikita tried to put some distance between them.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.105<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Are you finished? You heard what you wanted.&quot; — &quot;Horikita spoke sharply and with a sigh, trying to drive Ichinose away.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.106<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> The reversal, in one sentence, after weighing nothing out loud: &quot;Let’s accept her help, Ayanokouji-kun.&quot; — AK: &quot;Horikita had made a decision, probably determining that the benefits outweighed the risks.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.106<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> She gives her name first, which AK reads as the act of opening an alliance: &quot;Horikita gave her name candidly, as if doing so approved our cooperative relationship.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.106<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;This is the first I’m hearing about it affecting our class points. I’ll have to complain to Chabashira-sensei later,&quot; — AK: &quot;mumbled Horikita, a little disgruntled.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.107<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> She accepts being cast as the threat in his speech to Sakura without argument: &quot;Are you talking about me?&quot; — muttered, then dropped.<span class=\"pg\">p.102<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> Hostility on sight, then a partnership in the same afternoon: she is the one who says no twice, the one who says yes, and the one whose name seals it.<span class=\"pg\">p.102–107<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p88-1\">← Before: Ch.4 §4.2–4.3: she writes Sudou off out loud, and prices the witness<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p108-1\">→ After: Ch.4 §4.4–4.5: she follows him to his room and names what she thinks he is<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p108-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune ch 4  4 4 4 5  she follows him to his room and names what she thinks he is her only environmental protest in the volume  delivered to a stranger   a school that constantly runs air conditioning in empty buildings and is unkind to the environment is the worst    ichinose laughs anyway   ha ha ha  that s probably true  you re pretty interesting  she outsources the social half of the alliance to him with a look   horikita shot me a look that seemed to say  i don t want to do it  give her yours  she declines a spare key to his room before being offered one  and calls the visit itself a failing   for your room  ike kun asked earlier if i wanted one  i refused     after all  it s rare for me to visit your room  ayanokouji kun  besides  coming here is a shameful act in itself  a disgrace  understand    ak   i wasn t hurt at all  i definitely wasn t thinking anything like  wow  that was unexpectedly harsh  the one moment of her own body language he gets to see  and she names it herself   why are you tracing letters on the wall with your finger     to hide my pounding heart  or something  her agenda for the visit  stated as two problems   ayanokouji kun  i want to hear your thoughts on sudou kun s case once again  also  i find kushida san s actions a bit concerning   impossible  the very person in question didn t recognize what was happening  i m only now reluctantly offering to help for the sake of our class  frankly  i still think it would have been better to abandon him  the pedagogical claim she makes for not saving him   that was different  even if we managed to miraculously prove his innocence  do you think he ll mature  saving him might have the opposite effect    ak s tag   her defiant glare seemed to say  do you understand my point  she turns his own reasoning back on him in real time   knowing sudou s flawed personality  you realized from the very beginning how difficult it would be to prove his innocence  didn t you  that way  it s easier to think he d be better off accepting his punishment  especially better for those who hate him    ak s record of being caught   i felt like i d been backed against a wall  unable to run  if i tried to forcefully deny  she would just dig deeper  her verdict on the rest of class d  delivered as mercilessly as ak notes   kushida san and ike kun and the others haven t noticed at all  it seems  they simply believe in sudou kun  and want to save him from the lie for his sake and our class s sake  they don t understand the urgency of the situation   a little bit  so she realized it by herself  then  and  you told her  didn t you    ak   she cornered me with her words  it was like being interrogated  a little scary  the accusation that he engineered the midterm operations   you came up with the idea of getting the old test questions  and purchasing exam points  i can t say i m surprised  you do seem quite cunning at times  but i m dissatisfied  her full description of him  the volume s closest attempt at a characterisation of ayanokoji by another student   honestly  there s so much about you that i don t understand  you re a mystery  you re the most difficult person to predict in our class  you re versatile  yet you often idle your time away  you never seem to stay still  it s as though you cannot be categorized  then the sentence he cannot deflect   i guess what i should say is that you re just blending in and hiding your true talents  you re hiding in plain sight  you disgust me more than anyone else  she does not actually know what he did  and stops at a feeling   i see  i wondered if being called out like that was normal  it seemed i d taken the bait and gotten caught in horikita s trap  a small failure on my part    ak s own accounting of the conversation s cost  her koenji assessment  offered as the counter example to his mysteriousness   he s surprisingly easy to understand  he studies well  is athletic  and gets excellent grades  his personality is the problem  in the end  i can easily categorize and summarize his behavioral problems in only a few words  he s self centered  she is candid only in private and only with one person  the entire volume s worth of her actual analysis of class d   sudou  kushida  ayanokoji  koenji   is delivered in his room in one sitting  and none of it survives as anything but privately held when she re enters a classroom  ak s own note on the setting  which should not be over read   i wondered why i felt a little nervous being alone with horikita behind closed doors  ak s projection of her  the chapter s last word on her   at this rate  when she reached adulthood  she d probably become a teacher like chabashira sensei","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p108-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.4 §4.4–4.5: she follows him to his room and names what she thinks he is<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.108–113<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">She outsources the social half of the alliance to him with a look: &quot;Horikita shot me a look that seemed to say, I don’t want to do it. Give her yours.&quot; The one moment of her own body language he gets to see, and she names it herself: “Why are you tracing letters on the wall with your finger?” / “To hide my pounding heart. Or something.”<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">Her only environmental protest in the volume, delivered to a stranger: “A school that constantly runs air conditioning in empty buildings and is unkind to the environment is the worst,” — Ichinose laughs anyway: &quot;Ha ha ha, that’s…<span class=\"pg\">p.108<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">She declines a spare key to his room before being offered one, and calls the visit itself a failing: “For your room? Ike-kun asked earlier if I wanted one. I refused.” … “After all, it’s rare for me to visit your room…<span class=\"pg\">p.110<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">Her agenda for the visit, stated as two problems: “Ayanokouji-kun, I want to hear your thoughts on Sudou-kun’s case once again. Also, I find Kushida-san’s actions a bit concerning.”<span class=\"pg\">p.110<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>15 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> Her only environmental protest in the volume, delivered to a stranger: “A school that constantly runs air conditioning in empty buildings and is unkind to the environment is the worst,” — Ichinose laughs anyway: &quot;Ha ha ha, that’s probably true. You’re pretty interesting.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.108<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> She declines a spare key to his room before being offered one, and calls the visit itself a failing: “For your room? Ike-kun asked earlier if I wanted one. I refused.” … “After all, it’s rare for me to visit your room, Ayanokouji-kun. Besides, coming here is a shameful act in itself. A disgrace. Understand?” — AK: &quot;I wasn’t hurt at all. I definitely wasn’t thinking anything like, Wow, that was unexpectedly harsh.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.110<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Impossible. The very person in question didn’t recognize what was happening. I’m only now reluctantly offering to help for the sake of our class. Frankly, I still think it would have been better to abandon him.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.110–111<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> The pedagogical claim she makes for not saving him: “That was different. Even if we managed to miraculously prove his innocence, do you think he’ll mature? Saving him might have the opposite effect.” — AK&#x27;s tag: &quot;Her defiant glare seemed to say, Do you understand my point?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.111<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> She turns his own reasoning back on him in real time: “Knowing Sudou’s flawed personality, you realized from the very beginning how difficult it would be to prove his innocence, didn’t you? That way, it’s easier to think he’d be better off accepting his punishment. Especially better for those who hate him.” — AK&#x27;s record of being caught: &quot;I felt like I’d been backed against a wall, unable to run. If I tried to forcefully deny, she would just dig deeper.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.111<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> Her verdict on the rest of Class D, delivered as mercilessly as AK notes: “Kushida-san and Ike-kun and the others haven’t noticed at all, it seems. They simply believe in Sudou-kun, and want to save him from the lie for his sake and our class’s sake. They don’t understand the urgency of the situation.”<span class=\"pg\">p.111<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “A little bit? So she realized it by herself, then?” and “You told her, didn’t you?” — AK: &quot;She cornered me with her words. It was like being interrogated. A little scary.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.111<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> The accusation that he engineered the midterm operations: “You came up with the idea of getting the old test questions, and purchasing exam points. I can’t say I’m surprised. You do seem quite cunning at times, but…I’m dissatisfied.”<span class=\"pg\">p.111–112<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> Her full description of him, the volume&#x27;s closest attempt at a characterisation of Ayanokōji by another student: “Honestly, there’s so much about you that I don’t understand. You’re a mystery. You’re the most difficult person to predict in our class. You’re versatile, yet you often idle your time away. You never seem to stay still. It’s as though you cannot be categorized.”<span class=\"pg\">p.112<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> Then the sentence he cannot deflect: “I guess what I should say is that you’re just blending in and hiding your true talents. You’re hiding in plain sight. You disgust me more than anyone else.”<span class=\"pg\">p.112<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Limit<\/span> She does not actually know what he did, and stops at a feeling: &quot;I see. I wondered if being called out like that was normal. It seemed I’d taken the bait and gotten caught in Horikita’s trap. A small failure on my part.&quot; — AK&#x27;s own accounting of the conversation&#x27;s cost.<span class=\"pg\">p.112<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> Her Kōenji assessment, offered as the counter-example to his mysteriousness: “He’s surprisingly easy to understand. He studies well, is athletic, and gets excellent grades. His personality is the problem. In the end, I can easily categorize and summarize his behavioral problems in only a few words: he’s self-centered.”<span class=\"pg\">p.112<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> She is candid only in private and only with one person; the entire volume&#x27;s worth of her actual analysis of Class D — Sudou, Kushida, Ayanokōji, Kōenji — is delivered in his room in one sitting, and none of it survives as anything but privately held when she re-enters a classroom.<span class=\"pg\">p.110–113<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> AK&#x27;s own note on the setting, which should not be over-read: &quot;I wondered why I felt a little nervous being alone with Horikita behind closed doors.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.110<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> AK&#x27;s projection of her, the chapter&#x27;s last word on her: &quot;At this rate, when she reached adulthood, she’d probably become a teacher like Chabashira-sensei.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.113<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p95-1\">← Before: Ch.4 §4.4: she invites Ayanokōji out, and decides on Class B<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p118-1\">→ After: Ch.4 §4.6–4.8: named by everyone, present nowhere<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p118-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune ch 4  4 6 4 8  named by everyone  present nowhere the narrator s roster of who is actually carrying class d  in his own words   actually  the ones who had to work especially hard were horikita  hirata  and kushida  the first name in his private list of students wrongly sorted into class d   horikita  kouenji  and yukimura were undoubtedly three people who deserved to be at the top based on their academics alone  kushida  relaying her conclusion to the one person horikita will not speak to directly   horikita san seems convinced that sakura saw everything  kushida s summary of her  offered as the standing question of the class   speaking of special  don t you think that horikita san is way more special than someone like me  she s great at studying and excels at sports  it makes me wonder why she s in class d  kushida s probe about her   but doesn t she behave normally with you  ayanokouji kun  how ayanokoji describes her to a third party  which is the only version of her kushida receives   when i think of my relationship with horikita  it s like there s a wall between us  or perhaps i should say that s the extent of our relationship  if you understand what i m getting at  his withheld verdict on her exceptionalism  kept off the phone   horikita wasn t special  she belonged to a unique class of people  i kept quiet  though  afraid that if i badmouthed her she d find out about it  the plan that would place her beside the witness is cancelled before it is proposed  by the person organising the errand   while taking horikita along would probably be the best option  it was delusional to think that horikita and kushida would spend their day off together  all of this is secondhand  the second half of chapter 4 contains no horikita scene  her last appearance is alone with ayanokoji in his room  and the class s entire summer facing strategy is discussed without her in the room where it is decided","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p118-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.4 §4.6–4.8: named by everyone, present nowhere<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.118–130<\/span><\/h3><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">Kushida, relaying her conclusion to the one person Horikita will not speak to directly: &quot;Horikita-san seems convinced that Sakura saw everything.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.129<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">Kushida&#x27;s summary of her, offered as the standing question of the class: &quot;Speaking of special, don’t you think that Horikita-san is way more special than someone like me? She’s great at studying and excels at sports. It makes me…<span class=\"pg\">p.130<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">Kushida&#x27;s probe about her: &quot;But doesn’t she behave normally with you, Ayanokouji-kun?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.130<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>7 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> The narrator&#x27;s roster of who is actually carrying Class D, in his own words: &quot;Actually, the ones who had to work especially hard were Horikita, Hirata, and Kushida.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.118<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> The first name in his private list of students wrongly sorted into Class D: &quot;Horikita, Kouenji, and Yukimura were undoubtedly three people who deserved to be at the top based on their academics alone.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.119<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> Kushida&#x27;s summary of her, offered as the standing question of the class: &quot;Speaking of special, don’t you think that Horikita-san is way more special than someone like me? She’s great at studying and excels at sports. It makes me wonder why she’s in Class D.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.130<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> How Ayanokōji describes her to a third party, which is the only version of her Kushida receives: &quot;When I think of my relationship with Horikita, it’s like there’s a wall between us. Or perhaps I should say that’s the extent of our relationship, if you understand what I’m getting at.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.130<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> His withheld verdict on her exceptionalism, kept off the phone: &quot;Horikita wasn’t special. She belonged to a unique class of people. I kept quiet, though, afraid that if I badmouthed her she’d find out about it.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.130<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Limit<\/span> The plan that would place her beside the witness is cancelled before it is proposed, by the person organising the errand: &quot;While taking Horikita along would probably be the best option, it was delusional to think that Horikita and Kushida would spend their day off together.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.129<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> All of this is secondhand. The second half of Chapter 4 contains no Horikita scene; her last appearance is alone with Ayanokōji in his room, and the class&#x27;s entire summer-facing strategy is discussed without her in the room where it is decided.<span class=\"pg\">p.118–130<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p108-1\">← Before: Ch.4 §4.4–4.5: she follows him to his room and names what she thinks he is<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p159-1\">→ After: Ch.5 §5.1: the face she does not intend to make<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p159-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune ch 5  5 1  the face she does not intend to make morning  the classroom  she asks about his day off in what the narrator calls  an icy voice   did you spend your day off with kushida san   really  i didn t intend to make any kind of face  i should look the same as i always do  however  i will say that i admire how freely you ve been moving  when i ask you for help  you re often reluctant  but when kushida san asks you  you accept readily  i was calmly and discretely analyzing the difference between us  the denial is contradicted on the page   i looked over at my neighbor  and saw an expression on horikita s face that i d never glimpsed before  then  she did not remotely look calm and discreet  kushida reads the same face as exclusion  the narrator refuses that reading and then concedes a realization he cannot name","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p159-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.5 §5.1: the face she does not intend to make<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.159–162<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Morning, the classroom; she asks about his day off in what the narrator calls &quot;an icy voice&quot;.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Did you spend your day off with Kushida-san?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.159<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Really? I didn’t intend to make any kind of face. I should look the same as I always do. However, I will say that I admire how freely you’ve been moving. When I ask you for help, you’re often reluctant, but when Kushida-san asks…<span class=\"pg\">p.159<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Really? I didn’t intend to make any kind of face. I should look the same as I always do. However, I will say that I admire how freely you’ve been moving. When I ask you for help, you’re often reluctant, but when Kushida-san asks you, you accept readily. I was calmly and discretely analyzing the difference between us.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.159<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The denial is contradicted on the page: &quot;I looked over at my neighbor, and saw an expression on Horikita’s face that I’d never glimpsed before.&quot; then &quot;She did not remotely look calm and discreet.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.159–160<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Kushida reads the same face as exclusion; the narrator refuses that reading and then concedes a realization he cannot name.<span class=\"pg\">p.162<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p118-1\">← Before: Ch.4 §4.6–4.8: named by everyone, present nowhere<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p165-1\">→ After: Ch.5 §5.2–5.3: she takes the seats and refuses the optimism<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p165-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune ch 5  5 2 5 3  she takes the seats and refuses the optimism  well  naturally that was the result  it s to be expected   now then  kushida san  it would be best for ayanokouji kun and me to sit in on the deliberation  i fully understand you supporting sakura san  however  if it comes to a debate  then that s a different story  she takes the two observer places kushida asked for  and sakura is left agreeing to it  at lunch she eats  her bread in silence  while the others argue   don t bring your dirty face so close to me   i can t help but be mystified by your belief that your innocence can easily be proven  although you ve gained evidence that works in your favor  you re still in a very disadvantageous situation","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p165-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.5 §5.2–5.3: she takes the seats and refuses the optimism<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.165–167<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">At lunch she eats &quot;her bread in silence&quot; while the others argue.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Well, naturally that was the result. It’s to be expected.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.165<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Now then, Kushida-san. It would be best for Ayanokouji-kun and me to sit in on the deliberation. I fully understand you supporting Sakura-san. However, if it comes to a debate, then that’s a different story.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.165<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Don’t bring your dirty face so close to me.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.167<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> She takes the two observer places Kushida asked for, and Sakura is left agreeing to it.<span class=\"pg\">p.166<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I can’t help but be mystified by your belief that your innocence can easily be proven. Although you’ve gained evidence that works in your favor, you’re still in a very disadvantageous situation.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.167<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p159-1\">← Before: Ch.5 §5.1: the face she does not intend to make<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p170-1\">→ After: Ch.5 §5.4: the elevator, and a question she answers herself<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p170-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune ch 5  5 4  the elevator  and a question she answers herself the elevator  she is inside with shopping bags  the thirteenth floor button lit  he presses eleven   what  you re not getting on   i was out shopping  did you not see   this isn t the tenth floor  is that okay   for someone who dislikes trouble  you ve been extremely proactive in involving yourself with this case  or perhaps you have ulterior motives   you re going to meet with sakura san  aren t you   well  i suppose where you go is none of my business  she asks the question  then withdraws it  without waiting for the answer he does not give","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p170-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.5 §5.4: the elevator, and a question she answers herself<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.170–171<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">The elevator: she is inside with shopping bags, the thirteenth-floor button lit; he presses eleven.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;What? You’re not getting on?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.170<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I was out shopping. Did you not see?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.170<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;This isn’t the tenth floor. Is that okay?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.170<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;For someone who dislikes trouble, you’ve been extremely proactive in involving yourself with this case. Or perhaps you have ulterior motives?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.170<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;You’re going to meet with Sakura-san, aren’t you?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.170<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Well. I suppose where you go is none of my business.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.171<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> She asks the question, then withdraws it, without waiting for the answer he does not give.<span class=\"pg\">p.170–171<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p165-1\">← Before: Ch.5 §5.2–5.3: she takes the seats and refuses the optimism<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p191-1\">→ After: Ch.6 open: the hearing she is not ready for<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p191-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune ch 6 open  the hearing she is not ready for class d s room  ten minutes before the hearing  sudo asks her to hear him out and she answers by refusing to reassure him   have you prepared for this  sudou kun   don t do anything selfish  actually listening right now would be the clever thing to do  yes  the narrator reads the exchange as habitual combat without hatred  sudo  would ve absolutely refused her help  if he truly resented her  kushida s send off    do your best  horikita san  sudou kun    is the only encouragement horikita receives before the hearing  and she does not answer it  outside the faculty room  chabashira lets slip that the student council will sit in  horikita freezes at the words   i ll go  i m fine  the glance she gives the narrator is read as a request not to worry on her account","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p191-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6 open: the hearing she is not ready for<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.191–192<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Class D’s room, ten minutes before the hearing; Sudō asks her to hear him out and she answers by refusing to reassure him. Outside the faculty room, Chabashira lets slip that the student council will sit in; Horikita freezes at the words.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Have you prepared for this, Sudou-kun?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.191<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Don’t do anything selfish. Actually listening right now would be the clever thing to do, yes?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.191<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I’ll go. I’m fine.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.192<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The narrator reads the exchange as habitual combat without hatred: Sudō &quot;would’ve absolutely refused her help&quot; if he truly resented her.<span class=\"pg\">p.191<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Kushida’s send-off — &quot;Do your best, Horikita-san. Sudou-kun.&quot; — is the only encouragement Horikita receives before the hearing, and she does not answer it.<span class=\"pg\">p.191<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The glance she gives the narrator is read as a request not to worry on her account.<span class=\"pg\">p.192<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p170-1\">← Before: Ch.5 §5.4: the elevator, and a question she answers herself<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p193-1\">→ After: Ch.6 §6.1: frozen, then roused, then cross-examining<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p193-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"action spoken","w":"horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune ch 6  6 1  frozen  then roused  then cross examining her brother s presence undoes her before testimony begins   horikita  horikita the younger sister  i mean couldn t hide her trembling  and the narrator concludes their kinship makes the room  extremely disadvantageous   hyah   w wait  s stop  stop  she is physically roused by the narrator s tickling and returns to the room glaring  with startling intensity   tch   excuse me  may i ask a question   earlier  you said that sudou kun called you over to the special building  but who exactly did sudou call  and why   please answer   so then  why exactly were you in the special building  ishizaki kun  you re not on the basketball team  so you have no connection to this case  i d think your presence there would be rather odd   so in other words  you felt the situation might turn violent   i see  so you brought along ishizaki kun as your bodyguard  since he was reputed to be rather good at fighting  just in case there was an emergency   i do have some knowledge of martial arts  if only to a certain extent  i understand that when you re fighting against multiple enemies  victory becomes exponentially more difficult  so i don t understand how you were defeated so handily  how the fight could be so one sided  when you had a skilled fighter like ishizaki kun with you   the primary factor in triggering a fight is the collision of the  energy  between opponents  in the event that you don t have any intention of fighting  or that you re nonviolent  the probability that you ll be hurt should be very low  especially when there are three of you  her cross examination turns the witness list into a contradiction  if ishizaki came as a bodyguard because sudo was reputed violent  a rehearsed nonviolent group should not have been beaten so one sidedly  the narrator credits the method as  very objective  grounded in evidence  rules  and her own logic  and notes komiya answers it with his actual injuries rather than with argument   it s true that sudou injured the other students  however  class c started the fight  there is one student witness who saw the entire incident and can attest to this","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p193-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6 §6.1: frozen, then roused, then cross-examining<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.193–200<\/span><\/h3><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Hyah?!&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.197<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;W-wait. S-stop, stop!&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.197<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Tch…&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.197<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>13 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Her brother’s presence undoes her before testimony begins: &quot;Horikita —Horikita the younger sister, I mean—couldn’t hide her trembling,&quot; and the narrator concludes their kinship makes the room &quot;extremely disadvantageous.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.193–194<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> She is physically roused by the narrator’s tickling and returns to the room glaring &quot;with startling intensity.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.196–197<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Excuse me. May I ask a question?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.197<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Earlier, you said that Sudou-kun called you over to the special building. But who exactly did Sudou call, and why?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.197<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Please answer.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.197<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;So then, why exactly were you in the special building, Ishizaki-kun? You’re not on the basketball team, so you have no connection to this case. I’d think your presence there would be rather odd.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.197<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;So in other words, you felt the situation might turn violent?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.198<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I see. So you brought along Ishizaki-kun as your bodyguard, since he was reputed to be rather good at fighting. Just in case there was an emergency.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.198<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I do have some knowledge of martial arts, if only to a certain extent. I understand that when you’re fighting against multiple enemies, victory becomes exponentially more difficult. So I don’t understand how you were defeated so handily, how the fight could be so one-sided, when you had a skilled fighter like Ishizaki-kun with you.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.198<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;The primary factor in triggering a fight is the collision of the ‘energy’ between opponents. In the event that you don’t have any intention of fighting, or that you’re nonviolent, the probability that you’ll be hurt should be very low. Especially when there are three of you.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.198<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Her cross-examination turns the witness list into a contradiction: if Ishizaki came as a bodyguard because Sudō was reputed violent, a rehearsed nonviolent group should not have been beaten so one-sidedly.<span class=\"pg\">p.197–199<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The narrator credits the method as &quot;very objective, grounded in evidence, rules, and her own logic,&quot; and notes Komiya answers it with his actual injuries rather than with argument.<span class=\"pg\">p.198<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;It’s true that Sudou injured the other students. However, Class C started the fight. There is one student witness who saw the entire incident and can attest to this.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.199<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p191-1\">← Before: Ch.6 open: the hearing she is not ready for<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p203-1\">→ After: Ch.6 §6.1: the answer to the false-witness charge<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p203-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune ch 6  6 1  the answer to the false witness charge  that is not the case  it is certainly true that sakura san is not good at speaking before others  however  it is precisely because she witnessed the incident that she is standing here today  otherwise  she most likely would not  even if we d asked her  don t you think that if we needed someone who could speak boldly  we would have found a replacement  sakagami answers it by claiming the choice of a poor speaker is itself the staging   it would establish a sense of realism that you yourself could not","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p203-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6 §6.1: the answer to the false-witness charge<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.203<\/span><\/h3><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;That is not the case. It is certainly true that Sakura-san is not good at speaking before others. However, it is precisely because she witnessed the incident that she is standing here today. Otherwise, she most likely would not…<span class=\"pg\">p.203<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;That is not the case. It is certainly true that Sakura-san is not good at speaking before others. However, it is precisely because she witnessed the incident that she is standing here today. Otherwise, she most likely would not, even if we’d asked her. Don’t you think that if we needed someone who could speak boldly, we would have found a replacement?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.203<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Sakagami answers it by claiming the choice of a poor speaker is itself the staging: &quot;it would establish a sense of realism that you yourself could not.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.203<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p193-1\">← Before: Ch.6 §6.1: frozen, then roused, then cross-examining<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p207-1\">→ After: Ch.6 §6.1: the false concession, then the refusal<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p207-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune ch 6  6 1  the false concession  then the refusal  i understand   i think that sudou  who caused the incident  has a problem  he doesn t ever stop to consider his actions  which inconveniences everyone around him  he has a history of getting in fights  he s the type to raise his voice and fists right away whenever something displeases him  in the event of an uproar such as this  well  it should be obvious who caused it   you need to understand  sudou  your attitude caused all of this   this is why i wasn t motivated at all to help sudou kun in the beginning  i knew that even if i forced myself to lend a hand  he would just repeat the same mistakes again and again  the closing statement is a trap  she lets sakagami treat it as surrender  then refuses to sit  and the silence is what gives her the floor back   he should reflect on his actions  however  not in this particular case  when i say he should reflect  i mean that he should look back on his past actions  in regards to this particular incident  however  i don t think sudou kun did anything wrong  this was not an unfortunate event that occurred merely by chance  i m convinced that this was a deliberate move made by class c  i have absolutely no intention of meekly accepting defeat   if you did not understand  i will say it once again  we claim that sudou kun is completely innocent  therefore  we cannot accept his suspension from school  even for just one day   sudou kun is the victim  just as the witness testified  please do not make any errors in your judgment  the reversal is made for sakura s sake as much as sudo s  the narrator guesses she  had to be brave in front of sakura   would be possible to have a little more time before we reconvene  the line answering the president s question to class d    i haven t lied  everything we ve said has been the truth    is untagged in the translation  it is recorded as class d s answer  not attributed to her by name on the page","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p207-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6 §6.1: the false concession, then the refusal<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.207–209<\/span><\/h3><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I understand…&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.207<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I think that Sudou, who caused the incident, has a problem. He doesn’t ever stop to consider his actions, which inconveniences everyone around him. He has a history of getting in fights. He’s the type to raise his voice and…<span class=\"pg\">p.207<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;You need to understand, Sudou. Your attitude caused all of this.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.207<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>9 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I think that Sudou, who caused the incident, has a problem. He doesn’t ever stop to consider his actions, which inconveniences everyone around him. He has a history of getting in fights. He’s the type to raise his voice and fists right away whenever something displeases him. In the event of an uproar such as this, well, it should be obvious who caused it.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.207<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;This is why I wasn’t motivated at all to help Sudou-kun in the beginning. I knew that even if I forced myself to lend a hand, he would just repeat the same mistakes again and again.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.207<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> The closing statement is a trap: she lets Sakagami treat it as surrender, then refuses to sit, and the silence is what gives her the floor back.<span class=\"pg\">p.207–208<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;He should reflect on his actions. However, not in this particular case. When I say he should reflect, I mean that he should look back on his past actions. In regards to this particular incident, however, I don’t think Sudou-kun did anything wrong. This was not an unfortunate event that occurred merely by chance. I’m convinced that this was a deliberate move made by Class C. I have absolutely no intention of meekly accepting defeat.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.208<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;If you did not understand, I will say it once again. We claim that Sudou-kun is completely innocent. Therefore, we cannot accept his suspension from school, even for just one day.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.208<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Sudou-kun is the victim, just as the witness testified. Please do not make any errors in your judgment.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.208<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The reversal is made for Sakura’s sake as much as Sudō’s: the narrator guesses she &quot;had to be brave in front of Sakura.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.208<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Would be possible to have a little more time before we reconvene?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.209<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The line answering the president’s question to Class D — &quot;I haven’t lied. Everything we’ve said has been the truth.&quot; — is untagged in the translation; it is recorded as Class D’s answer, not attributed to her by name on the page.<span class=\"pg\">p.209<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p203-1\">← Before: Ch.6 §6.1: the answer to the false-witness charge<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p210-1\">→ After: Ch.6 §6.1: what she says to Sakura on the way out<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p210-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune ch 6  6 1  what she says to sakura on the way out  i won t give up  i will keep fighting to support your testimony until the end   i have no intention of losing  well then  i must excuse myself  she leaves immediately after the promise rather than staying to comfort sakura  and the chapter reads the haste as strategy  not coldness","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p210-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6 §6.1: what she says to Sakura on the way out<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.210<\/span><\/h3><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I won’t give up. I will keep fighting to support your testimony until the end,&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.210<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I have no intention of losing. Well then, I must excuse myself.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.210<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> She leaves immediately after the promise rather than staying to comfort Sakura, and the chapter reads the haste as strategy, not coldness.<span class=\"pg\">p.210<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p207-1\">← Before: Ch.6 §6.1: the false concession, then the refusal<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p216-1\">→ After: Ch.6 §6.2: the request she makes of Class B<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p216-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune ch 6  6 2  the request she makes of class b  i sincerely appreciate the offer  but it s not necessary   we cannot get sudou acquitted  even if a new witness were to come from class a or b  it would be impossible  however there is something i would like you to prepare for us  it is the only possible solution   i understand that i m in no position to ask this   the burden i d be placing upon you is exceptionally great  but   you re certainly right about that  well then  if i can convince you  will you cooperate with us   you should understand the risks as well as the usefulness of this strategy   just before the deliberation ended  only by chance  though   don t worry about that part  i ve confirmed it   if you ask the professor to assist us  it should be good  i ll talk to him   sure  i promise   well then  ayanokouji kun  there s something i d like you to help me with   helping others is fundamentally bothersome and time consuming  she has a plan before the hearing ends and has already verified that its material exists by the time she explains it in the entranceway  the plan requires a lie from a person who hates lying  horikita acknowledges the burden instead of softening it  and ichinose supplies the justification herself","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p216-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6 §6.2: the request she makes of Class B<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.216–218<\/span><\/h3><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I sincerely appreciate the offer, but it’s not necessary.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.216<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;We cannot get Sudou acquitted. Even if a new witness were to come from Class A or B, it would be impossible. However…there is something I would like you to prepare for us. It is the only possible solution.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.216<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I understand that I’m in no position to ask this,&quot; &quot;The burden I’d be placing upon you is exceptionally great. But—&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.216<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>10 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;You’re certainly right about that. Well then, if I can convince you, will you cooperate with us?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.216<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;You should understand the risks as well as the usefulness of this strategy,&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.216<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Just before the deliberation ended. Only by chance, though.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.216<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Don’t worry about that part. I’ve confirmed it.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.217<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;If you ask the Professor to assist us, it should be good. I’ll talk to him.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.217<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Sure. I promise.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.218<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Well then, Ayanokouji-kun. There’s something I’d like you to help me with.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.218<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Helping others is fundamentally bothersome and time-consuming.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.218<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> She has a plan before the hearing ends and has already verified that its material exists by the time she explains it in the entranceway.<span class=\"pg\">p.216<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Limit<\/span> The plan requires a lie from a person who hates lying; Horikita acknowledges the burden instead of softening it, and Ichinose supplies the justification herself.<span class=\"pg\">p.216–217<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p210-1\">← Before: Ch.6 §6.1: what she says to Sakura on the way out<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p218-1\">→ After: Ch.6 §6.2: the debt she collects<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p218-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"action spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune ch 6  6 2  the debt she collects she answers the hearing s tickling with a blow to the narrator s side that drops him into the corner   i ll forgive you for touching me this time  however  next time i ll pay you back double  the chapter runs her from paralysis to leadership and closes the account with the blow  she accepts his intervention in the hearing and prices it immediately","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p218-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6 §6.2: the debt she collects<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.218<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I’ll forgive you for touching me this time. However, next time I’ll pay you back double.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.218<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> She answers the hearing’s tickling with a blow to the narrator’s side that drops him into the corner.<span class=\"pg\">p.218<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> The chapter runs her from paralysis to leadership and closes the account with the blow: she accepts his intervention in the hearing and prices it immediately.<span class=\"pg\">p.196–218<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p216-1\">← Before: Ch.6 §6.2: the request she makes of Class B<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p220-1\">→ After: Ch.7 §7.0–7.1: waiting on the path, judging the change<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p220-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune ch 7  7 0 7 1  waiting on the path  judging the change  good morning  ayanokouji kun   yes  i was waiting for you   are you an idiot   i was thinking maybe i made a mistake  the wrong choice   if sudou kun is penalized for this  it ll be my responsibility   the truth is that we re gambling  i m a little anxious of the outcome  are you okay   nothing  after we settle this case   what s with her   people don t change so easily  trying to change yourself is virtually impossible  the page calls it a  brief but realistic statement  that shattered the image ayanokoji had built   as long as she doesn t overdo it  i think it ll be fine   if she tries to do what isn t possible for someone like her yet  she ll just set herself up to fail  the warning lands with  a mysterious yet convincing power  almost as if she were speaking from experience   do you want to die for good","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p220-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.7 §7.0–7.1: waiting on the path, judging the change<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.220–223<\/span><\/h3><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Good morning, Ayanokouji-kun.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.220<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Yes. I was waiting for you.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.220<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Are you an idiot?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.220<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>11 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I was thinking…maybe I made a mistake. The wrong choice…&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.220<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;If Sudou-kun is penalized for this, it’ll be my responsibility.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.220<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;The truth is that we’re gambling. I’m a little anxious of the outcome. Are you okay?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.220<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Nothing. After we settle this case,&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.221<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;What’s with her?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.222<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;People don’t change so easily. Trying to change yourself is virtually impossible.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.222<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The page calls it a &quot;brief but realistic statement&quot; that shattered the image Ayanokōji had built.<span class=\"pg\">p.222<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;As long as she doesn’t overdo it, I think it’ll be fine.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.223<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;If she tries to do what isn’t possible for someone like her yet, she’ll just set herself up to fail.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.223<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The warning lands with &quot;a mysterious yet convincing power,&quot; almost as if she were speaking from experience.<span class=\"pg\">p.223<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Do you want to die for good?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.223<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p218-1\">← Before: Ch.6 §6.2: the debt she collects<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p242-1\">→ After: Ch.7 §7.5: the retrial, from her side<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p242-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"action inner spoken","w":"horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune ch 7  7 5  the retrial  from her side she and sudo arrive ten minutes before deliberation  tachibana is already in the room  and neither her brother nor class c has come in yet  the chapter turns to her first person here   i feel the same as ever  the line she has committed to   i d declared that sudou was completely innocent  after all  if my strategy failed  it would be for nothing   reconciliation was another name for defeat  on a failed strategy   it would likely devolve into a verbal battle where we hurled abuse at each other  when the doors open for her brother she turns her eyes away from him and faces the opponents who matter today   even though i should have understood it  i felt attacked   i was wracked with various symptoms such as trembling  nervousness  and dizziness  but i couldn t repeat yesterday s mistakes   he s not participating   well  even if he s not here  the results will be the same  her read on chabashira s puzzlement   i had the gut feeling that what chabashira sensei was seeing was the evidence of ayanokouji kun s involvement   this was a battle between truth and lies  we could bandy about ideas  but there could only be one solution","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p242-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.7 §7.5: the retrial, from her side<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.242–243<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">She and Sudō arrive ten minutes before deliberation; Tachibana is already in the room, and neither her brother nor Class C has come in yet. The chapter turns to her first person here.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I feel the same as ever.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.242<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;He’s not participating.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.243<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Well, even if he’s not here, the results will be the same.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.243<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>8 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> The line she has committed to: &quot;I’d declared that Sudou was completely innocent, after all. If my strategy failed, it would be for nothing.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.242<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> &quot;Reconciliation was another name for defeat.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.242<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> On a failed strategy: &quot;it would likely devolve into a verbal battle where we hurled abuse at each other.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.242<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> When the doors open for her brother she turns her eyes away from him and faces the opponents who matter today.<span class=\"pg\">p.242<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> &quot;Even though I should have understood it, I felt attacked.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.242<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> &quot;I was wracked with various symptoms such as trembling, nervousness, and dizziness. But I couldn’t repeat yesterday’s mistakes.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.242<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> Her read on Chabashira’s puzzlement: &quot;I had the gut feeling that what Chabashira-sensei was seeing was the evidence of Ayanokouji-kun’s involvement.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.243<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> &quot;This was a battle between truth and lies. We could bandy about ideas, but there could only be one solution.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.243<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p220-1\">← Before: Ch.7 §7.0–7.1: waiting on the path, judging the change<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p244-1\">→ After: Ch.7 §7.5: the withdrawal she did not have to ask for<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p244-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"action inner spoken","w":"horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune ch 7  7 5  the withdrawal she did not have to ask for  it wasn t just me  everyone else noticed that this situation was strange   it seemed that ayanokouji kun and ichinose san had handled things quite well  i tried to act calm and collected  without letting my relief show  she grabs sudo s arm to stop his question and pulls him down into his seat   shut up   if the complaint was withdrawn there would be no winners or losers  this was what we d been working toward  the regulations line that announces a point payment for the deliberation expenses is printed with no speaker attached","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p244-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.7 §7.5: the withdrawal she did not have to ask for<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.244–245<\/span><\/h3><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q inner\">&quot;It wasn’t just me. Everyone else noticed that this situation was strange.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.244<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q inner\">&quot;It seemed that Ayanokouji-kun and Ichinose-san had handled things quite well. I tried to act calm and collected, without letting my relief show.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.244<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Shut up.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.245<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> She grabs Sudō’s arm to stop his question and pulls him down into his seat.<span class=\"pg\">p.245<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> &quot;If the complaint was withdrawn there would be no winners or losers. This was what we’d been working toward.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.245<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The regulations line that announces a point payment for the deliberation expenses is printed with no speaker attached.<span class=\"pg\">p.245<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p242-1\">← Before: Ch.7 §7.5: the retrial, from her side<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p246-1\">→ After: Ch.7 §7.5: the verdict, and Chabashira’s lecture to Sudō<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p246-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"inner spoken","w":"chabashira-sae horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune ch 7  7 5  the verdict  and chabashira s lecture to sudo  you will no longer face suspension  the school will not consider you a problem child  you will be able to participate in club activities from today onward  right  she notes that kushida san and hirata kun s actions in the hearing  would be rewarded as well   no  i don t    asked whether sudo will become a model student  however sudou kun certainly made some progress today  he admitted he was at fault  so i m sure that he ll grow more tomorrow   no  i ve already abandoned him  i just won t allow him to run loose anymore  on his exit for club practice   he was not remorseful  he was definitely going to cause trouble for us again soon  he was a nuisance  she stays behind at chabashira s request once her brother and tachibana are sent out","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p246-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.7 §7.5: the verdict, and Chabashira’s lecture to Sudō<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.246–248<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"chabashira-sae.html\">Chabashira Sae<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;You will no longer face suspension. The school will not consider you a problem child. You will be able to participate in club activities from today onward. Right?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.246<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;No, I don’t.&quot; — asked whether Sudō will become a model student<span class=\"pg\">p.247<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;However…Sudou-kun certainly made some progress today. He admitted he was at fault. So I’m sure that he’ll grow more tomorrow.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.248<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> She notes that Kushida-san and Hirata-kun’s actions in the hearing &quot;would be rewarded as well.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.246<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;No, I’ve already abandoned him. I just won’t allow him to run loose anymore.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.248<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> On his exit for club practice: &quot;He was not remorseful. He was definitely going to cause trouble for us again soon. He was a nuisance.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.248<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> She stays behind at Chabashira’s request once her brother and Tachibana are sent out.<span class=\"pg\">p.248<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p244-1\">← Before: Ch.7 §7.5: the withdrawal she did not have to ask for<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p248-1\">→ After: Ch.7 §7.5: the private lesson about Ayanokōji<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p248-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"inner spoken","w":"chabashira-sae horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune ch 7  7 5  the private lesson about ayanokoji  what do you mean   why do you care about that   i ll leave that to your imagination   we d fabricated a lie because we were backed into a corner   i don t want to admit this  but ayanokouji kun might have something exceptional to him   is that surprising  you were the one who first put me together with ayanokouji kun  chabashira sensei  you did it because you couldn t overlook ayanokouji kun s potential  right   though he does try to hide his ability by pretending to be an idiot  for some mysterious reason   yes  he was truly incomprehensible  i could not find meaning in such behavior   i don t intend to admit that i have a defect  but i do understand   we ve already established it  he already knows what his own defect is   he  dislikes trouble  answering with confidence  she still feels  a strange sense of discomfort that i couldn t explain   no  it s because he said it himself   had he deliberately poked his nose into this incident as well   that unconscious realization must have been the cause of my earlier discomfort   chabashira sensei  do you really understand what about him can be considered defective   why was chabashira sensei telling me such things  the session ends with chabashira saying nothing more and horikita carrying the questions out of the room","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p248-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.7 §7.5: the private lesson about Ayanokōji<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.248–251<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"chabashira-sae.html\">Chabashira Sae<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;What do you mean?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.248<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Why do you care about that?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.248<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I’ll leave that to your imagination.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.248<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>15 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> &quot;We’d fabricated a lie because we were backed into a corner.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.248<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I don’t want to admit this, but Ayanokouji-kun…might have something exceptional to him.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.249<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Is that surprising? You were the one who first put me together with Ayanokouji-kun, Chabashira-sensei. You did it because you couldn’t overlook Ayanokouji-kun’s potential, right?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.249<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Though he does try to hide his ability by pretending to be an idiot, for some mysterious reason.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.249<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> &quot;Yes, he was truly incomprehensible. I could not find meaning in such behavior.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.249<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I don’t intend to admit that I have a defect. But I do understand.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.249<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;We’ve already established it. He already knows what his own defect is.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.249<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;He ‘dislikes trouble,’&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.249<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Answering with confidence, she still feels &quot;a strange sense of discomfort that I couldn’t explain.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.249<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;No… It’s because he said it himself.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.250<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> &quot;Had he deliberately poked his nose into this incident as well?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.250<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> &quot;That unconscious realization must have been the cause of my earlier discomfort.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.250<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Chabashira-sensei, do you really understand what about him can be considered defective?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.250<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> &quot;Why was Chabashira-sensei telling me such things?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.251<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> The session ends with Chabashira saying nothing more and Horikita carrying the questions out of the room.<span class=\"pg\">p.248–251<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p246-1\">← Before: Ch.7 §7.5: the verdict, and Chabashira’s lecture to Sudō<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p253-1\">→ After: Ch.7 §7.6: the puppet question<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p253-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune ch 7  7 6  the puppet question  you d already know  right   hey  ayanokouji kun  am i just your puppet   ayanokouji kun  you brought up the idea of surveillance cameras in the classrooms  next  you took me to the special building and made me realize that there were no cameras  then  you guided me to the idea of inventing false evidence  so that we could parse the truth from lies  when i look back on it now  that s all i can think of   who are you    thrown back at him after he calls her account of the case  just coincidence   and you are    to the black haired boy who stops in front of them  wait  we re not done talking  ayanokouji kun   you promised  right  you promised you d help me reach class a   that s not what i meant  i want to know what you re thinking   if you really hated drawing attention  you wouldn t make all this effort to get involved  you say you re someone who  dislikes trouble  after all  yet you act all evasive and non committal even while you help me  why  the chapter ends with her accusation of being steered and his evasion  unanswered","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p253-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.7 §7.6: the puppet question<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.253–255<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;You’d already know, right?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.253<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Hey, Ayanokouji-kun. Am I just your puppet?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.253<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Ayanokouji-kun, you brought up the idea of surveillance cameras in the classrooms. Next, you took me to the special building and made me realize that there were no cameras. Then, you guided me to the idea of inventing false…<span class=\"pg\">p.253–254<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>8 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Ayanokouji-kun, you brought up the idea of surveillance cameras in the classrooms. Next, you took me to the special building and made me realize that there were no cameras. Then, you guided me to the idea of inventing false evidence, so that we could parse the truth from lies… When I look back on it now, that’s all I can think of.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.253–254<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Who are you?&quot; — thrown back at him after he calls her account of the case &quot;just coincidence&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.254<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;And you are?&quot; — to the black-haired boy who stops in front of them<span class=\"pg\">p.254<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Wait. We’re not done talking, Ayanokouji-kun.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.254<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;You promised, right? You promised you’d help me reach Class A.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.254<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;That’s not what I meant. I want to know what you’re thinking.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.255<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;If you really hated drawing attention, you wouldn’t make all this effort to get involved. You say you’re someone who ‘dislikes trouble,’ after all. Yet you act all evasive and non-committal even while you help me. Why?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.255<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> The chapter ends with her accusation of being steered and his evasion, unanswered.<span class=\"pg\">p.253–255<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p248-1\">← Before: Ch.7 §7.5: the private lesson about Ayanokōji<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p22-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune ch 2  2 0  she comes down from the ship wrong deck of the liner at disembark call  class d waits in the heat   even horikita  normally so meticulous  was concerned about her appearance  right now  though  her hair was disheveled    and she rubs her arms as if cold   i was just reading a book in my room  for whom the bell tolls  you wouldn t know it  her stated excuse for locking herself away doesn t cover what ayanokoji saw  the chapter leaves the gap open","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p22-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2 §2.0: she comes down from the ship wrong<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.22–23<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Deck of the liner at disembark call; Class D waits in the heat.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“I was just reading a book in my room. For Whom the Bell Tolls. You wouldn’t know it.”<span class=\"pg\">p.22<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> &quot;Even Horikita, normally so meticulous, was concerned about her appearance. Right now, though, her hair was disheveled.&quot; — and she rubs her arms as if cold.<span class=\"pg\">p.22<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Limit<\/span> Her stated excuse for locking herself away doesn&#x27;t cover what Ayanokōji saw; the chapter leaves the gap open.<span class=\"pg\">p.23<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p33-1\">→ After: Ch.2 §2.1: she asks the questions that price the test<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p33-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"spoken","w":"hirata-yousuke ayanokouji-kiyotaka horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune ch 2  2 1  she asks the questions that price the test class d s first rules huddle on the beach after mashima s announcement   in the event that someone were to retire after we had already used all 300 points  what would happen    the question that establishes the floor at zero  stands beside ayanokoji watching hirata fail to decide   class d has no leadership  which worries me  besides  hirata s a pushover  he can t even make one decision  can he   i m the same as the others  i ve never lived in such an environment before  so i can t really make any predictions  what an unpleasant test    her first open admission that academics don t transfer here  asks him to take her side on endurance  he agrees  classes a and b are already moving into the forest while c and d still can t start","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p33-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2 §2.1: she asks the questions that price the test<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.33–45<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Class D&#x27;s first rules huddle on the beach after Mashima&#x27;s announcement.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> · <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“In the event that someone were to retire after we had already used all 300 points, what would happen?” — the question that establishes the floor at zero.<span class=\"pg\">p.33<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I’m the same as the others. I’ve never lived in such an environment before, so I can’t really make any predictions… What an unpleasant test.” — her first open admission that academics don&#x27;t transfer here.<span class=\"pg\">p.44<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Stands beside Ayanokōji watching Hirata fail to decide: &quot;Class D has no leadership, which worries me. Besides, Hirata’s a pushover. He can’t even make one decision, can he?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.43–44<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Asks him to take her side on endurance; he agrees; Classes A and B are already moving into the forest while C and D still can&#x27;t start.<span class=\"pg\">p.44–45<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p22-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.0: she comes down from the ship wrong<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p47-1\">→ After: Ch.2 §2.2: she admits the isolation, and blocks the probe<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p47-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune ch 2  2 2  she admits the isolation  and blocks the probe walking from beach to forest  she trails the group alone   to be honest  i m depressed  these kinds of things just aren t for me  life on an island seems primitive  and worst of all  i can t be alone  concedes the classroom verdict against her own tools   this test will likely fall outside of my academic abilities  i d determined that ike kun and sudou kun would be hindrances  but they took the initiative to go out searching  i wasn t able to do anything   it doesn t feel good to have someone pry into your past    and names chabashira as the leak   chabashira sensei leaked the information  don t misunderstand me  all right  besides  we re still not friends  don t forget that  ends the exchange on her own terms before he can go deeper","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p47-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2 §2.2: she admits the isolation, and blocks the probe<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.47–49<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Walking from beach to forest; she trails the group alone.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“To be honest, I’m depressed. These kinds of things just aren’t for me. Life on an island seems primitive, and worst of all, I can’t be alone.”<span class=\"pg\">p.47<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“It doesn’t feel good to have someone pry into your past” — and names Chabashira as the leak: “Chabashira-sensei leaked the information. Don’t misunderstand me. All right? Besides, we’re still not friends. Don’t forget that.”<span class=\"pg\">p.49<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Limit<\/span> Concedes the classroom verdict against her own tools: &quot;This test will likely fall outside of my academic abilities. I’d determined that Ike-kun and Sudou-kun would be hindrances, but they took the initiative to go out searching. I wasn’t able to do anything.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.48<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Ends the exchange on her own terms before he can go deeper.<span class=\"pg\">p.49<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p33-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.1: she asks the questions that price the test<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p63-1\">→ After: Ch.2 §2.4: the leader&#x27;s card, and the favour she can&#x27;t do herself<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p63-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"spoken","w":"kushida-kikyou sudou-ken ayanokouji-kiyotaka horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune ch 2  2 4  the leader s card  and the favour she can t do herself the circle that picks class d s spot leader  kushida nominates her as the responsible choice  she accepts without visible surprise   i understand  i accept    after sudou tries to take the role to spare her  becomes class d s designated leader  hirata files her name with chabashira and the card is handed over  the class touches the device together to hide who holds it  his defence of her wishes is the trigger that makes her take the role rather than dodge it  delegates the ike problem    i m relying on you because i know i can t do it  can i count on you    then delivers the standard put down   i suppose it must be relaxing to be unreliable and underachieving    isn t it  ayanokouji kun  the chapter s closing read of her  alone she is  amazing but only alone  the school  had made her isolated life impossible","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p63-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2 §2.4: the leader&#x27;s card, and the favour she can&#x27;t do herself<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.63–71<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">The circle that picks Class D&#x27;s spot-leader.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a> · <a href=\"sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a> · <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“I understand. I accept.” — after Sudou tries to take the role to spare her.<span class=\"pg\">p.66<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> Kushida nominates her as the responsible choice; she accepts without visible surprise.<span class=\"pg\">p.66<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Becomes Class D&#x27;s designated leader; Hirata files her name with Chabashira and the card is handed over; the class touches the device together to hide who holds it.<span class=\"pg\">p.66–67<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> His defence of her wishes is the trigger that makes her take the role rather than dodge it.<span class=\"pg\">p.66<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Delegates the Ike problem — &quot;I&#x27;m relying on you because I know I can&#x27;t do it. Can I count on you?&quot; — then delivers the standard put-down: “I suppose it must be relaxing to be unreliable and underachieving. … Isn’t it, Ayanokouji-kun?”<span class=\"pg\">p.70–71<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The chapter&#x27;s closing read of her: alone she is &quot;amazing…but only alone&quot;; the school &quot;had made her isolated life impossible.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.71<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p47-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.2: she admits the isolation, and blocks the probe<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p73-1\">→ After: Ch.2 §2.5 &amp; §2.8: she refuses the assistantship, and votes last<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p73-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka kushida-kikyou horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune ch 2  2 5    2 8  she refuses the assistantship  and votes last on becoming hirata s assistant   me  his assistant  don t joke around  i d rather dance with a mongoose  names her own usable condition    if there were a clear enemy and a goal  i might be of use    and admits she still can t decide how far the class should spend  raises her hand for river water last  with ayanokoji  after the whole class has already committed","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p73-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2 §2.5 &amp; §2.8: she refuses the assistantship, and votes last<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.73–74, p.92<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> On becoming Hirata&#x27;s assistant: “Me, his assistant? Don’t joke around. I’d rather dance with a mongoose.”<span class=\"pg\">p.73<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Limit<\/span> Names her own usable condition — &quot;If there were a clear enemy and a goal, I might be of…use&quot; — and admits she still can&#x27;t decide how far the class should spend.<span class=\"pg\">p.73–74<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> Raises her hand for river water last, with Ayanokōji, after the whole class has already committed.<span class=\"pg\">p.92<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p63-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.4: the leader&#x27;s card, and the favour she can&#x27;t do herself<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p106-1\">→ After: Ch.3 §3.1: called out of the tent<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p106-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune ch 3  3 1  called out of the tent summoned from the girls  tent after the class c provocation  the cloth moves  and she steps out   the cheap provocation coming from class c  yes  i heard   i don t want to move too much  since i m the leader  if i stand out too much  we ll be in a bad spot  concedes she cannot stay hidden   the president s younger sister  seen watching ryuen and ichinose   you re right  i suppose i can t say what s correct  fine  i m rather concerned about the state of the other classes  let s go  takes his read that hiding will not change anything and sets out with him for the class c beach","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p106-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3 §3.1: called out of the tent<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.106–107<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Summoned from the girls&#x27; tent after the Class C provocation; the cloth moves, and she steps out.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“The cheap provocation coming from Class C? Yes, I heard.”<span class=\"pg\">p.106<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I don&#x27;t want to move too much. Since I&#x27;m the leader, if I stand out too much, we&#x27;ll be in a bad spot.”<span class=\"pg\">p.106<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Limit<\/span> Concedes she cannot stay hidden — the president&#x27;s younger sister, seen watching Ryūen and Ichinose: “You&#x27;re right. I suppose I can&#x27;t say what&#x27;s correct. Fine. I&#x27;m rather concerned about the state of the other classes. Let&#x27;s go.”<span class=\"pg\">p.107<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Takes his read that hiding will not change anything and sets out with him for the Class C beach.<span class=\"pg\">p.107<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p73-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.5 &amp; §2.8: she refuses the assistantship, and votes last<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p108-1\">→ After: Ch.3 §3.2: the confrontation on the beach<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p108-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"spoken","w":"ryuuen-kakeru ibuki-mio horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune ch 3  3 2  the confrontation on the beach the class c beach spectacle  she cannot believe what she is looking at   no way  all this stuff  is it even possible  walks up to his chair with ayanokoji and holds the confrontation to the end   if the person on top is incompetent  those below him will suffer  this is pitiful   we re trying to warn you  you re an idiot  the translation leaves the line untagged  his reply is thrown back at her  asks who hit ibuki roundabout    her face is swollen  who did that to her    and gets the admission of a light punishment   there is one more piece of business  you know ibuki  of course   you used up all your points on the first day  didn t you   see you later  suzune   i don t know where exactly you found that out  but do not call me by my first name so casually  also untagged  she is the one addressed by the first name call","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p108-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3 §3.2: the confrontation on the beach<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.108–114<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">The Class C beach spectacle; she cannot believe what she is looking at.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"ibuki-mio.html\">Ibuki Mio<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“No way… All this stuff… Is it even possible?”<span class=\"pg\">p.108<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“If the person on top is incompetent, those below him will suffer. This is pitiful,”<span class=\"pg\">p.111<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“We&#x27;re trying to warn you. You&#x27;re an idiot.”<span class=\"pg\">p.111<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>8 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Walks up to his chair with Ayanokōji and holds the confrontation to the end.<span class=\"pg\">p.109–114<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The translation leaves the line untagged; his reply is thrown back at her.<span class=\"pg\">p.111<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ibuki Mio<\/b> Asks who hit Ibuki roundabout — “Her face is swollen. Who did that to her?” — and gets the admission of a light punishment.<span class=\"pg\">p.112–113<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “There is one more piece of business. You know Ibuki, of course?”<span class=\"pg\">p.112<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You…used up all your points on the first day, didn&#x27;t you?”<span class=\"pg\">p.113<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “See you later, Suzune.”<span class=\"pg\">p.114<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I don&#x27;t know where exactly you found that out, but do not call me by my first name so casually.”<span class=\"pg\">p.114<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Also untagged; she is the one addressed by the first-name call.<span class=\"pg\">p.114<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p106-1\">← Before: Ch.3 §3.1: called out of the tent<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p116-1\">→ After: Ch.3 §3.3: the walk back, and Class B’s camp<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p116-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"action spoken","w":"ichinose-honami hirata-yousuke horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune ch 3  3 3  the walk back  and class b s camp walking inland from the class c shore  she is still arguing over ryuen s spending when the visit to class b s camp begins   we ought to think of a way to get points back without giving up  ryuuen is most definitely wrong  i cannot possibly understand him  rejects the zero points route on principle  points are to be won back  not written off  arrives as a visitor with ayanokoji and declines the hammock offer  so ichinose sits instead   i was wondering if it might behoove us to tentatively enter into a cooperative relationship  like last time  listens through the whole tour   well  water shower  toilet  vinyl  heat   without interrupting  afterward lays out class d s situation completely  holding nothing back in the interest of fairness   yeah  there s a lot to make us uneasy right now  but we have to try and make it through   i was thinking that we should talk about that  too  if we didn t have to be on guard with even one class  we d really appreciate it  as long as you don t mind  ichinose san  i d like you to accept the proposal  the cooperation exchange is untagged  she is the one addressing ichinose by name  and ichinose s proposal and reply are recorded under her   this class has fallen in line far better than i could have imagined  i suppose that s because you re the one taking command  right  judges class b by its order  every student carrying out a role  and doing the duty happily  with nobody trying to skip out   no  we do have a boy named hirata  though  everyone in class clusters around him  names him as the one class d gathers around  then changes the topic   ichinose san  i m terribly sorry to keep asking you questions  but we want to confirm class a s status  can you tell us anything that will help us capture their base camp  even something you know about the area might really help   secretive  what kind of measures has class a taken   you can t use any sly tricks in this test  ryuuen has most definitely spent almost all of their points  they might be having fun right now  but they re going to regret it later  the line is untagged  the narration that follows anchors the withheld withdrawal plan on her   i think it s about time to get going  ayanokouji kun  we ll be a bother to class b if we linger too long   in general  i think we re all on the same page  but they re further ahead  i can t deny it  says it as a declaration of defeat  the distance between d and b is not only a matter of points  the two untagged verdict lines that follow are left as a chapter attribution gap","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p116-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3 §3.3: the walk back, and Class B’s camp<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.116–125<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Walking inland from the Class C shore, she is still arguing over Ryūen&#x27;s spending when the visit to Class B&#x27;s camp begins.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a> · <a href=\"hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“We ought to think of a way to get points back without giving up. Ryuuen is most definitely wrong. I cannot possibly understand him,”<span class=\"pg\">p.116<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I was wondering if it might behoove us to tentatively enter into a cooperative relationship, like last time,”<span class=\"pg\">p.120<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Yeah. There’s a lot to make us uneasy right now, but we have to try and make it through.”<span class=\"pg\">p.122<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>18 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Rejects the zero-points route on principle: points are to be won back, not written off.<span class=\"pg\">p.116<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> Arrives as a visitor with Ayanokōji and declines the hammock offer, so Ichinose sits instead.<span class=\"pg\">p.117–118<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Listens through the whole tour — well, water shower, toilet, vinyl, heat — without interrupting.<span class=\"pg\">p.121<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Afterward lays out Class D&#x27;s situation completely, holding nothing back in the interest of fairness.<span class=\"pg\">p.122<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I was thinking that we should talk about that, too. If we didn’t have to be on guard with even one class, we’d really appreciate it. As long as you don’t mind, Ichinose-san, I’d like you to accept the proposal.”<span class=\"pg\">p.122<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The cooperation exchange is untagged; she is the one addressing Ichinose by name, and Ichinose&#x27;s proposal and reply are recorded under her.<span class=\"pg\">p.122<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “This class has fallen in line far better than I could have imagined. I suppose that’s because you’re the one taking command, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.122<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Judges Class B by its order: every student carrying out a role, and doing the duty happily, with nobody trying to skip out.<span class=\"pg\">p.122<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “No. We do have a boy named Hirata, though. Everyone in class clusters around him.”<span class=\"pg\">p.123<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Names him as the one Class D gathers around, then changes the topic.<span class=\"pg\">p.123<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ichinose-san. I’m terribly sorry to keep asking you questions, but we want to confirm Class A’s status. Can you tell us anything that will help us capture their base camp? Even something you know about the area might really help.”<span class=\"pg\">p.123<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Secretive? What kind of measures has Class A taken?”<span class=\"pg\">p.123<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You can’t use any sly tricks in this test. Ryuuen has most definitely spent almost all of their points. They might be having fun right now, but they’re going to regret it later.”<span class=\"pg\">p.124<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The line is untagged; the narration that follows anchors the withheld withdrawal plan on her.<span class=\"pg\">p.124<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I think it’s about time to get going, Ayanokouji-kun. We’ll be a bother to Class B if we linger too long.”<span class=\"pg\">p.125<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “In general, I think we’re all on the same page, but they’re further ahead. I can’t deny it,”<span class=\"pg\">p.125<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> Says it as a declaration of defeat: the distance between D and B is not only a matter of points.<span class=\"pg\">p.125<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The two untagged verdict lines that follow are left as a chapter attribution gap.<span class=\"pg\">p.125<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p108-1\">← Before: Ch.3 §3.2: the confrontation on the beach<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p126-1\">→ After: Ch.3 §3.4: talking past Class A at the cave<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p126-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"spoken","w":"totsuka-yahiko katsuragi-kouhei horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune ch 3  3 4  talking past class a at the cave she and ayanokoji walk up to the class a cave together after watching from a distance fails to show anything   what are you planning  we gain nothing by carelessly exposing ourselves  the approach dialogue is untagged  the question and answer chain  and the question tagged to her at the end of it  put these on her   we came to snoop  you have a problem   i mean  i would ve thought that since you re in class a you d be clever  but  switches into a deliberate provocation   the narration calls it a daring switch flipped in her brain   well  rather than clever  i d say you re underhanded  what cowardly methods   i m horikita  from class d   stupid  huh  in that case  there s no harm in us seeing what s inside  right  or does that make you feel uncomfortable   so it s not a problem if we look  you re in the way   we re just going to look inside  that itself isn t a violation of the rules  right   oh  so you occupy this place  i didn t know that  is there a device inside  provokes him on purpose and talks past every block he puts up   well  there definitely aren t any rules that say we can t go into the cave  it s certainly true that we cannot use the cave while it s being occupied  but that s not the same as the right to monopolize it or anything  we should have the right to look inside  or at least to verify if there s equipment  right  if we couldn t do that  then people could just forcibly monopolize every spot  that s not what this test is about  the monopoly argument  occupation bars use  not looking  and a spot that nobody may inspect could be seized by anyone   you re forcefully monopolizing control of the spot  the rules don t protect such actions  both p 128 lines are untagged  the second is answered by katsuragi conceding the point  matched and stopped by his unspoken rule argument   well  fine  i look forward to seeing the results  and class a s abilities  leaves with the wind knocked out of her  without katsuragi s arrival she would have gone through the vinyl  her mutters  w wait  and  ugh  what an unintelligible  half assed answer  are untagged  the second answers his own admission","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p126-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3 §3.4: talking past Class A at the cave<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.126–129<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">She and Ayanokōji walk up to the Class A cave together after watching from a distance fails to show anything.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"totsuka-yahiko.html\">Totsuka Yahiko<\/a> · <a href=\"katsuragi-kouhei.html\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“What are you planning? We gain nothing by carelessly exposing ourselves.”<span class=\"pg\">p.126<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“We came to snoop. You have a problem?”<span class=\"pg\">p.127<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I mean, I would’ve thought that since you’re in Class A you’d be clever, but…”<span class=\"pg\">p.127<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>17 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The approach dialogue is untagged; the question-and-answer chain, and the question tagged to her at the end of it, put these on her.<span class=\"pg\">p.126<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Switches into a deliberate provocation — the narration calls it a daring switch flipped in her brain.<span class=\"pg\">p.127<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, rather than clever, I’d say you’re underhanded. What cowardly methods.”<span class=\"pg\">p.127<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m Horikita, from Class D.”<span class=\"pg\">p.127<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Stupid, huh? In that case, there’s no harm in us seeing what’s inside, right? Or does that make you feel uncomfortable?”<span class=\"pg\">p.127<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “So it’s not a problem if we look? You’re in the way.”<span class=\"pg\">p.127<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “We’re just going to look inside. That itself isn’t a violation of the rules, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.127<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Oh? So you occupy this place. I didn’t know that. Is there a device inside?”<span class=\"pg\">p.127<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Totsuka Yahiko<\/b> Provokes him on purpose and talks past every block he puts up.<span class=\"pg\">p.127–129<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, there definitely aren’t any rules that say we can’t go into the cave. It’s certainly true that we cannot use the cave while it’s being occupied, but that’s not the same as the right to monopolize it or anything. We should have the right to look inside, or at least to verify if there’s equipment, right? If we couldn’t do that, then people could just forcibly monopolize every spot. That’s not what this test is about.”<span class=\"pg\">p.128<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> The monopoly argument: occupation bars use, not looking, and a spot that nobody may inspect could be seized by anyone.<span class=\"pg\">p.128<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You’re forcefully monopolizing control of the spot. The rules don’t protect such actions.”<span class=\"pg\">p.128<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Both p.128 lines are untagged; the second is answered by Katsuragi conceding the point.<span class=\"pg\">p.128<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> Matched and stopped by his unspoken-rule argument.<span class=\"pg\">p.128–129<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, fine. I look forward to seeing the results, and Class A’s abilities.”<span class=\"pg\">p.129<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Limit<\/span> Leaves with the wind knocked out of her; without Katsuragi&#x27;s arrival she would have gone through the vinyl.<span class=\"pg\">p.129<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Her mutters “W-wait.” and “Ugh, what an unintelligible, half-assed answer.” are untagged; the second answers his own admission.<span class=\"pg\">p.126<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p116-1\">← Before: Ch.3 §3.3: the walk back, and Class B’s camp<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p152-1\">→ After: Ch.5 §5.2: the invitation at her desk<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p152-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"spoken","w":"sudou-ken horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune ch 5  5 2  the invitation at her desk closing ceremonies at her desk neighbour s side  sudou s summer invitation arrives the moment the bell rings   why   how stupid  it doesn t matter at all that it s summer vacation  why are you even inviting me out in the first place  refuses him flatly  then finishes getting ready and leaves the classroom without another word while he is still mid pitch  the call that opens the exchange and the sign off at the end are untagged between the three of them  both are left with the chapter s gaps","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p152-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.5 §5.2: the invitation at her desk<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.152–153<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Closing ceremonies at her desk neighbour’s side; Sudou’s summer invitation arrives the moment the bell rings.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Why?”<span class=\"pg\">p.152<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“How stupid. It doesn’t matter at all that it’s summer vacation. Why are you even inviting me out in the first place?”<span class=\"pg\">p.152<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> Refuses him flatly, then finishes getting ready and leaves the classroom without another word while he is still mid-pitch.<span class=\"pg\">p.152–153<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The call that opens the exchange and the sign-off at the end are untagged between the three of them; both are left with the chapter’s gaps.<span class=\"pg\">p.152–153<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p126-1\">← Before: Ch.3 §3.4: talking past Class A at the cave<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p171-1\">→ After: Ch.6 §6.1: the objection<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p171-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"spoken","w":"karuizawa-kei ayanokouji-kiyotaka horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune ch 6  6 1  the objection breaks the girls  unanimity by objecting to karuizawa  distrusting hirata as much as the other boys   wait a minute  i d like to raise an objection especially against you  karuizawa san   i don t particularly mind dividing up the living areas for men and women  as long as the culprit hasn t been found  it is certainly a good idea to keep our distance from the men  considering the likelihood that the culprit is among them  however  i don t trust hirata kun  i cannot dismiss the possibility that he might be the underwear thief  also  i m unconvinced that he should be excluded from the ban on men   that s just your personal belief  isn t it  don t force your way of thinking on me  is left untagged in the translation  it sits between karuizawa s two lines about hirata and is placed here as her reply   don t make me repeat myself  nothing you can say will convince me   i won t speak impulsively  simply put  i would be fine if you increased the number by one more guy  if you did  they d be effective in watching each other s backs  is left untagged in the translation  placed here as her answer   might this be happening due to your naive handling of crisis management  maybe there is an ulterior motive for stealing the underwear that we don t yet understand   i don t care that your underwear was stolen  that kind of thing happens every day  and there s nothing you can really do about it  it s likely someone here bears a grudge against you  she is considering that the culprit s goal was not the underwear itself but humiliating karuizawa  socializing is her weak point  smart  but with difficulty relating to other people  the public clash  karuizawa calls her clueless about boyfriends  and she calls the crisis management naive   i agree with you  considering how these three behave on a daily basis  they are completely untrustworthy  i ve thought it over very carefully  and i intend to choose someone who can t be the culprit   you  ayanokouji kun  nominates him as the one other boy the girls can trust  over karuizawa s objections   is it okay for us to continue the discussion now  this farce is a waste of time  silently watches karuizawa s excoriation of sakura  then sighs and brushes a hand through her hair as if she d observed something completely boring   you re naive  karuizawa san   it s certainly true that ayanokouji kun has many unlikable qualities   but we need to ask if hirata kun can trust ayanokouji kun  it would only be awkward and uncomfortable if you endorsed someone meaningless to hirata kun  the truth is  there is not one thing that i trust about him  but i have no intention of inserting my own personal feelings into the matter  by process of elimination  i ve concluded that he is the most trustworthy boy in the class  or is another boy in our class preferable  if there is  i d like for you to tell me  the other girls treat her poorly  both sides ignore each other  and living together now makes a clash of tempers inevitable","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p171-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6 §6.1: the objection<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.171–178<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Breaks the girls’ unanimity by objecting to Karuizawa, distrusting Hirata as much as the other boys.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a> · <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Wait a minute. I’d like to raise an objection—especially against you, Karuizawa-san.”<span class=\"pg\">p.172<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I don’t particularly mind dividing up the living areas for men and women. As long as the culprit hasn’t been found, it is certainly a good idea to keep our distance from the men, considering the likelihood that the culprit is…”<span class=\"pg\">p.172<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Don’t make me repeat myself. Nothing you can say will convince me.”<span class=\"pg\">p.173<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>17 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I don’t particularly mind dividing up the living areas for men and women. As long as the culprit hasn’t been found, it is certainly a good idea to keep our distance from the men, considering the likelihood that the culprit is among them. However, I don’t trust Hirata-kun. I cannot dismiss the possibility that he might be the underwear thief. Also, I’m unconvinced that he should be excluded from the ban on men.”<span class=\"pg\">p.172<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> “That’s just your personal belief, isn’t it? Don’t force your way of thinking on me.” is left untagged in the translation; it sits between Karuizawa’s two lines about Hirata and is placed here as her reply.<span class=\"pg\">p.173<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> “I won’t speak impulsively. Simply put, I would be fine if you increased the number by one more guy. If you did, they’d be effective in watching each other’s backs.” is left untagged in the translation; placed here as her answer.<span class=\"pg\">p.173<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Might this be happening due to your naïve handling of crisis management? Maybe there is an ulterior motive for stealing the underwear that we don’t yet understand.”<span class=\"pg\">p.173<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I don’t care that your underwear was stolen. That kind of thing happens every day, and there’s nothing you can really do about it. It’s likely someone here bears a grudge against you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.173<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inference, not stated<\/span> She is considering that the culprit’s goal was not the underwear itself but humiliating Karuizawa.<span class=\"pg\">p.173<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Socializing is her weak point: smart, but with difficulty relating to other people.<span class=\"pg\">p.173<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> The public clash: Karuizawa calls her clueless about boyfriends, and she calls the crisis management naïve.<span class=\"pg\">p.173<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I agree with you. Considering how these three behave on a daily basis, they are completely untrustworthy. I’ve thought it over very carefully, and I intend to choose someone who can’t be the culprit.”<span class=\"pg\">p.174<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You. Ayanokouji-kun.”<span class=\"pg\">p.174<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Nominates him as the one other boy the girls can trust, over Karuizawa’s objections.<span class=\"pg\">p.174<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Is it okay for us to continue the discussion now? This farce is a waste of time.”<span class=\"pg\">p.176<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Silently watches Karuizawa’s excoriation of Sakura, then sighs and brushes a hand through her hair as if she’d observed something completely boring.<span class=\"pg\">p.176<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You’re naïve, Karuizawa-san.”<span class=\"pg\">p.177<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It’s certainly true that Ayanokouji-kun has many unlikable qualities,”<span class=\"pg\">p.177<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “But we need to ask if Hirata-kun can trust Ayanokouji-kun. It would only be awkward and uncomfortable if you endorsed someone meaningless to Hirata-kun. The truth is, there is not one thing that I trust about him, but I have no intention of inserting my own personal feelings into the matter. By process of elimination, I’ve concluded that he is the most trustworthy boy in the class. Or is another boy in our class preferable? If there is, I’d like for you to tell me.”<span class=\"pg\">p.177<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The other girls treat her poorly; both sides ignore each other, and living together now makes a clash of tempers inevitable.<span class=\"pg\">p.177<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p152-1\">← Before: Ch.5 §5.2: the invitation at her desk<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p184-1\">→ After: Ch.6 §6.3: points and the fever<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p184-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune ch 6  6 3  points and the fever pulls ayanokoji into the girls  tent to show what the class has been spending  then proposes a partnership against the split   it must be really tough  being forced to do routine chores   there was no other way  hirata kun can t be trusted  and i needed insurance   i suppose that s true  i m certainly not two faced   however  most create a distinction between their public persona and how they really are on the inside  you do it  too  i do not trust anyone because good intentions and hypocrisy are two sides of the same coin  the narration reads her distrust as referring to kushida as well  not only hirata   at any rate  you seem to trust hirata kun very much   count on him  can you say that he s had a positive effect on the class just by being around   exactly  trustworthy hirata kun has kept his mouth shut about it   the tent on the other side has the exact same things in it  too  a total of twelve points  the girls  comfort items   floor mat  air pillows  battery powered fan   cost a total of twelve points   karuizawa san and the others asked for these   i only found out after they d already ordered everything  it s difficult to do anything when the rules say anyone may buy an item and spend points   karuizawa san reported this to hirata kun  so he definitely knew about it  but you didn t know  nor did he inform anyone else  i think he absolutely should have shared this information   if things stay as they are and nothing happens  people will probably stay quiet  but things could get bad if the case of the stolen underwear isn t resolved  if the culprit is nearby  he or she might be trying to hinder us  that s why i want to find the culprit as soon as possible   yes  now that there s a divide between us and the boys  there are many things i can t do by myself  asks him to work with her now that the boys and the girls are cut off from each other   i m trying to understand you  do you have some other intention   well  whatever  it s settled then   you have such a serious look on your face  do you really hate being treated like a criminal that much   our cooperation was a complete coincidence  class d didn t really have any sense of teamwork to begin with  it s ending rather badly  though  especially because of the broken trust between the guys and girls  of course it would ve been better to stay united until the end of the test   let s not get ahead of ourselves  sorry  but i m going back into the tent   confessed  confessed what   not really any more than usual   when did you notice   yeah  and i told you i d been reading in my room   and on what evidence do you base that conclusion  a fever close to 38 c  hidden since the ship  reporting illness would hit the class with a bigger penalty   i just need to hang in there for another few days  if i give up now  it ll   all be for nothing  goodnight  she intends to soldier through to the bitter end   an iron will","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p184-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6 §6.3: points and the fever<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.184–189<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Pulls Ayanokōji into the girls’ tent to show what the class has been spending, then proposes a partnership against the split.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“It must be really tough, being forced to do routine chores,”<span class=\"pg\">p.184<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“There was no other way. Hirata-kun can’t be trusted, and I needed insurance.”<span class=\"pg\">p.184<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I suppose that’s true. I’m certainly not two-faced.”<span class=\"pg\">p.184<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>26 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “However, most create a distinction between their public persona and how they really are on the inside. You do it, too. I do not trust anyone because good intentions and hypocrisy are two sides of the same coin.”<span class=\"pg\">p.184<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The narration reads her distrust as referring to Kushida as well, not only Hirata.<span class=\"pg\">p.184<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “At any rate, you seem to trust Hirata-kun very much,”<span class=\"pg\">p.185<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Count on him? Can you say that he’s had a positive effect on the class just by being around?”<span class=\"pg\">p.185<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Exactly. Trustworthy Hirata-kun has kept his mouth shut about it.”<span class=\"pg\">p.185<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “The tent on the other side has the exact same things in it, too. A total of twelve points.”<span class=\"pg\">p.186<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Numbers<\/span> The girls’ comfort items — floor mat, air pillows, battery-powered fan — cost a total of twelve points.<span class=\"pg\">p.186<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Karuizawa-san and the others asked for these.”<span class=\"pg\">p.186<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I only found out after they’d already ordered everything. It’s difficult to do anything when the rules say anyone may buy an item and spend points.”<span class=\"pg\">p.186<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Karuizawa-san reported this to Hirata-kun, so he definitely knew about it. But you didn’t know, nor did he inform anyone else. I think he absolutely should have shared this information.”<span class=\"pg\">p.186<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If things stay as they are and nothing happens, people will probably stay quiet. But things could get bad if the case of the stolen underwear isn’t resolved. If the culprit is nearby, he or she might be trying to hinder us. That’s why I want to find the culprit as soon as possible.”<span class=\"pg\">p.186<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yes. Now that there’s a divide between us and the boys, there are many things I can’t do by myself.”<span class=\"pg\">p.187<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Asks him to work with her now that the boys and the girls are cut off from each other.<span class=\"pg\">p.187<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m trying to understand you… Do you have some other intention?”<span class=\"pg\">p.187<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, whatever. It’s settled then.”<span class=\"pg\">p.187<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You have such a serious look on your face. Do you really hate being treated like a criminal that much?”<span class=\"pg\">p.187<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Our cooperation was a complete coincidence. Class D didn’t really have any sense of teamwork to begin with. It’s ending rather badly, though, especially because of the broken trust between the guys and girls. Of course it would’ve been better to stay united until the end of the test.”<span class=\"pg\">p.187<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Let’s not get ahead of ourselves… Sorry, but I’m going back into the tent.”<span class=\"pg\">p.187<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Confessed? Confessed what?”<span class=\"pg\">p.187<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Not really any more than usual.”<span class=\"pg\">p.188<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “When…did you notice?”<span class=\"pg\">p.188<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yeah, and I told you I’d been reading in my room.”<span class=\"pg\">p.188<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “And on what evidence do you base that conclusion?”<span class=\"pg\">p.188<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> A fever close to 38°C, hidden since the ship; reporting illness would hit the class with a bigger penalty.<span class=\"pg\">p.188<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I just need to hang in there for another few days. If I give up now, it’ll … all be for nothing. Goodnight.”<span class=\"pg\">p.188<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> She intends to soldier through to the bitter end — an iron will.<span class=\"pg\">p.189<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p171-1\">← Before: Ch.6 §6.1: the objection<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p191-1\">→ After: Ch.6 §6.4: search in pairs<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p191-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"action spoken","w":"kushida-kikyou ayanokouji-kiyotaka horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune ch 6  6 4  search in pairs overhears kushida s excuse for being left behind  then takes the lead on the last forage   why were you left behind  what about your usual group of friends   even if she s not feeling well  it s a natural physiological phenomenon  she should be fine  i suppose that s to be expected  though  however  why did you deliberately choose our group  you must have had other options available  grills her for choosing this group   she detests kushida  and kushida knows it   i don t have enough free time to spend it with you unnecessarily   you got too close  remember to stay out of my personal space  slaps yamauchi when he peers into her face from a centimetre away   for the time being  let s begin with the area   how long do you want to travel  we need to search for food  right   don t make any moves alone  search in pairs  be especially careful  let s go  ayanokouji kun   i always have it on me   when we update the device  i ll slip in among the students hirata kun s gathered so i can be undetected  ibuki san and the other students aren t supposed to know  hands over her leader card for him to inspect away from base camp   maybe  but what do you plan to do after i show you   er  right  if you have proof  that would be a huge achievement   well  is this the same card that katsuragi kun had   the keycards might have a different color scheme based on the class   yeah  but we don t have enough evidence to make a solid judgment  if we make a mistake  we won t recover from it  snatches the dropped card from the mud  then keeps her distance from him in fury","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p191-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6 §6.4: search in pairs<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.191–199<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Overhears Kushida’s excuse for being left behind, then takes the lead on the last forage.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a> · <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Why were you left behind? What about your usual group of friends?”<span class=\"pg\">p.192<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Even if she’s not feeling well, it’s a natural physiological phenomenon. She should be fine. I suppose that’s to be expected, though. However, why did you deliberately choose our group? You must have had other options available.”<span class=\"pg\">p.193<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I don’t have enough free time to spend it with you unnecessarily.”<span class=\"pg\">p.193<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>15 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> Grills her for choosing this group — she detests Kushida, and Kushida knows it.<span class=\"pg\">p.193<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You got too close. Remember to stay out of my personal space.”<span class=\"pg\">p.196<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Slaps Yamauchi when he peers into her face from a centimetre away.<span class=\"pg\">p.196<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “For the time being, let’s begin with the area,”<span class=\"pg\">p.197<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “How long do you want to travel? We need to search for food, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.197<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Don’t make any moves alone. Search in pairs. Be especially careful. Let’s go, Ayanokouji-kun.”<span class=\"pg\">p.197<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I always have it on me.”<span class=\"pg\">p.198<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “When we update the device, I’ll slip in among the students Hirata-kun’s gathered so I can be undetected. Ibuki-san and the other students aren’t supposed to know.”<span class=\"pg\">p.198<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Hands over her leader card for him to inspect away from base camp.<span class=\"pg\">p.198<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Maybe, but what do you plan to do after I show you?”<span class=\"pg\">p.198<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Er, right. If you have proof, that would be a huge achievement.”<span class=\"pg\">p.198<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well? Is this the same card that Katsuragi-kun had?”<span class=\"pg\">p.198<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “The keycards might have a different color scheme based on the class.”<span class=\"pg\">p.199<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yeah, but we don’t have enough evidence to make a solid judgment. If we make a mistake, we won’t recover from it.”<span class=\"pg\">p.199<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Snatches the dropped card from the mud, then keeps her distance from him in fury.<span class=\"pg\">p.199<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p184-1\">← Before: Ch.6 §6.3: points and the fever<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p200-1\">→ After: Ch.6 §6.5: thrown, then washed<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p200-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"action spoken","w":"yamauchi-haruki horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune ch 6  6 5  thrown  then washed ill and distracted  she does not see yamauchi coming until mud goes over her hair   she throws him without a word   ha ha ha ha  you re all covered in mud  horikita  hilarious  grabs his pointing arm and throws him the moment he laughs  takes his lifetime grudge line for the mud  he cowers behind ayanokoji   i m going to hold a grudge against you for the rest of my life  you d best prepare yourself   yeah  this situation is rather painful   right  looks like i don t have any other choice  with the shower line blocked by karuizawa s group  she takes the river instead  washes the mud off in the cold river while sick  then appears in a swimsuit with kushida","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p200-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6 §6.5: thrown, then washed<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.200–202<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Ill and distracted, she does not see Yamauchi coming until mud goes over her hair — she throws him without a word.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"yamauchi-haruki.html\">Yamauchi Haruki<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Yamauchi Haruki<\/b> “Ha ha ha ha! You’re all covered in mud, Horikita! Hilarious!”<span class=\"pg\">p.200<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I’m going to hold a grudge against you for the rest of my life. You’d best prepare yourself.”<span class=\"pg\">p.201<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Yeah… This situation is rather painful.”<span class=\"pg\">p.201<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Grabs his pointing arm and throws him the moment he laughs.<span class=\"pg\">p.200<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yamauchi Haruki<\/b> Takes his lifetime-grudge line for the mud; he cowers behind Ayanokōji.<span class=\"pg\">p.201<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Right. Looks like I don’t have any other choice.”<span class=\"pg\">p.201<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> With the shower line blocked by Karuizawa’s group, she takes the river instead.<span class=\"pg\">p.201<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Washes the mud off in the cold river while sick, then appears in a swimsuit with Kushida.<span class=\"pg\">p.202<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p191-1\">← Before: Ch.6 §6.4: search in pairs<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p203-1\">→ After: Ch.6 §6.6: the confession<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p203-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"action spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune ch 6  6 6  the confession she draws ayanokoji into the forest and tells him the key card was stolen   ayanokouji kun  could you please come here for a moment   follow me  we can t talk here   this happened because of my carelessness  i am aware that i made a mistake  okay   a mistake   it was stolen   w wait  your underwear was stolen  too   no  this is much  much worse  the key card  a complete blunder on my part   i wanted to talk to you because i trust you  i absolutely couldn t consult with someone who might be the culprit  this is so humiliating  i want  to die   such a huge failure   no  the one who stole it is to blame  right   even so  this is an issue of responsibility  it has nothing to do with me being sick or covered in mud   i wasn t supposed to let go of the card for a single second  but i   don t blame yourself  i doubt this ll be any consolation  but i think you did your absolute best   it s probably better if we don t make this information public  we should get to the truth first   yes  i think so  too   i suspect two people  either karuizawa san  or ibuki san   unfortunately  the chances of that are low  karuizawa was in front of the shower the whole time   you re sure about that   yeah  same goes for her flunkies  too   if that s the case  it s highly likely ibuki san is the culprit  it s possible she came to know about the card this morning  and the timing is just far too good   if we examine the timing and talk with ibuki  we can understand what happened  if we suspect ibuki  we shouldn t take our eyes off of her  her escape would probably be the worst case scenario  right   that s right  i m sorry  but can you go back to camp first  that way you can start following her immediately   sure  i understand  i ll keep an eye on her  sent back to camp alone  likely wanting room to be sick by herself","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p203-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6 §6.6: the confession<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.203–205<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">She draws Ayanokōji into the forest and tells him the key card was stolen.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Ayanokouji-kun. Could you please come here for a moment?”<span class=\"pg\">p.203<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Follow me. We can’t talk here.”<span class=\"pg\">p.203<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“This happened because of my carelessness. I am aware that I made a mistake. Okay?”<span class=\"pg\">p.203<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>21 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “A mistake?”<span class=\"pg\">p.203<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It was stolen.”<span class=\"pg\">p.203<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “W-wait, your underwear was stolen, too?”<span class=\"pg\">p.203<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “No. This is much, much worse. The…key card. A complete blunder on my part.”<span class=\"pg\">p.203<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I wanted to talk to you because I trust you. I absolutely couldn’t consult with someone who might be the culprit. This is so humiliating. I want… to die…”<span class=\"pg\">p.203<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Such a huge failure.”<span class=\"pg\">p.204<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “No, the one who stole it is to blame. Right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.204<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Even so, this is an issue of responsibility. It has nothing to do with me being sick or covered in mud.”<span class=\"pg\">p.204<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I wasn’t supposed to let go of the card for a single second. But I…”<span class=\"pg\">p.204<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Don’t blame yourself. I doubt this’ll be any consolation, but I think you did your absolute best.”<span class=\"pg\">p.204<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It’s probably better if we don’t make this information public. We should get to the truth first.”<span class=\"pg\">p.204<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yes. I think so, too.”<span class=\"pg\">p.204<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I suspect two people. Either Karuizawa-san, or Ibuki-san.”<span class=\"pg\">p.204<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Unfortunately, the chances of that are low. Karuizawa was in front of the shower the whole time.”<span class=\"pg\">p.204<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You’re sure about that?”<span class=\"pg\">p.204<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yeah. Same goes for her flunkies, too.”<span class=\"pg\">p.204<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If that’s the case, it’s highly likely Ibuki-san is the culprit. It’s possible she came to know about the card this morning, and the timing is just far too good.”<span class=\"pg\">p.204<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If we examine the timing and talk with Ibuki, we can understand what happened. If we suspect Ibuki, we shouldn’t take our eyes off of her. Her escape would probably be the worst-case scenario, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.205<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s right. I’m sorry, but can you go back to camp first? That way you can start following her immediately.”<span class=\"pg\">p.205<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Sure. I understand. I’ll keep an eye on her.”<span class=\"pg\">p.205<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Sent back to camp alone, likely wanting room to be sick by herself.<span class=\"pg\">p.205<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p200-1\">← Before: Ch.6 §6.5: thrown, then washed<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p206-1\">→ After: Ch.6 §6.7: the fire from her side<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p206-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"action spoken","w":"ibuki-mio horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune ch 6  6 7  the fire from her side returns to a smoke filled camp and turns the fire straight onto ibuki   i can t see ibuki  the fire might have been her handiwork  where is she  ready to call out to ibuki at the fire  but hesitates when she sees her genuine confusion   did the manual get burned   it s just one thing after another  gone from the camp by the time the luggage is secured   she has set out after ibuki","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p206-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6 §6.7: the fire from her side<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.206–208<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Returns to a smoke-filled camp and turns the fire straight onto Ibuki.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ibuki-mio.html\">Ibuki Mio<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“I can’t see Ibuki. The fire might have been her handiwork. Where is she?”<span class=\"pg\">p.206<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Did the manual get burned?”<span class=\"pg\">p.206<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“It’s just one thing after another…”<span class=\"pg\">p.206<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ibuki Mio<\/b> Ready to call out to Ibuki at the fire, but hesitates when she sees her genuine confusion.<span class=\"pg\">p.206<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Gone from the camp by the time the luggage is secured — she has set out after Ibuki.<span class=\"pg\">p.212<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p203-1\">← Before: Ch.6 §6.6: the confession<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p213-1\">→ After: Ch.6 §6.8: the pursuit<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p213-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"action inner spoken","w":"ibuki-mio horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune ch 6  6 8  the pursuit her viewpoint  she chases ibuki s footprints through the downpour  sick and alone  until ibuki waits for her as if expecting her   what are you doing  horikita   when did you notice me   right from the start   why were you following me   do you really not know   no  i don t know   you clearly know why i was following you  don t you   i really have no idea what you re talking about   why should i lie   i d at least like to hear why you followed me  from your own lips   the underwear theft and the fire  misfortune continues to befall class d   so what   do you realize that some people suspect you   ah  i suppose since i m an outsider  there s not much i can do about that   that s what i m talking about   you re saying i m the culprit  do you have any proof   unfortunately  i don t have a single shred of evidence related to the underwear theft  but i think it was you   that s a pretty terrible thing to say  you don t have any evidence  yet you suspect me   i suspect you because of today  you don t need me to explain that  do you   let me cut to the chase  i want you to return something you took from me   i don t know what you re talking about   where are you going   who knows   i have to make up for my mistake  i have to make up for my mistake   i can handle it well  i can do it  i can do it  the fever peaks in the downpour  she can no longer hold her head up   ibuki san  i m going to investigate you with everything i ve got  you don t mind   with everything you ve got  could you be a bit more specific  you mean you re going to resort to violence   this is your last warning  return it  she recalls condemning sudou after his class c trial   and abandoning him   now that she is considering the same violence   oh  you re good   an act of violence means immediate disqualification   someone might see us here  you mean  weren t you willing to use violence  too  thrown into the mud  she slips ibuki s grip  rolls away  and rises   the first real thanks her martial arts practice gets her   oh  you can really move  surprisingly  you practice or something   i ve been nothing but a complete and utter failure in this test   i mocked people  i hated useless things  labeling them incompetent  while i was useless myself   it was you  wasn t it  you stole the keycard  meets ibuki s trained footwork in a back and forth exchange   no hesitation on either side to hurt   you ve been trying really hard until now  i ll tell you the truth  as a reward  i stole the card  watches ibuki draw the card out and show the engraved name   you gave up the truth pretty easily   it doesn t matter if i admit it or not now  there s no evidence i used violence against you  it s not as though the school can make a judgment here  isn t that right  the card is back in ibuki s pocket  fingerprints on it are her only argument for recovering it  drives her left fist into ibuki s solar plexus with her last strength   it pins her but does not knock her down   this is the worst  i m already  at my limit   i don t understand  i thought you were involved   involved  in what   i didn t burn the manual   you intend to keep lying even now   what would i gain by burning it  it was inevitable that people would begin searching for the criminal after the uproar  besides  people would suspect me rather strongly  there was nothing to gain and a lot to lose   do you think he s in class d  there s a guy who figured me out before you did  ibuki leaves the man s name out  the page names no one   so  you can t mean   this conversation is over  knocked out cold by a blunt strike to the head as the talk  ends   do you think they ll permit such coercive methods   come on  now  i don t feel like answering that   by attempting to fix that mistake myself  i ended up turning it into a situation that couldn t be fixed","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p213-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6 §6.8: the pursuit<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.213–220<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Her viewpoint: she chases Ibuki’s footprints through the downpour, sick and alone, until Ibuki waits for her as if expecting her.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ibuki-mio.html\">Ibuki Mio<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ibuki Mio<\/b> “What are you doing, Horikita?”<span class=\"pg\">p.213<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“When did you notice me?”<span class=\"pg\">p.213<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ibuki Mio<\/b> “Right from the start.”<span class=\"pg\">p.213<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>56 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Why were you following me?”<span class=\"pg\">p.213<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Do you really not know?”<span class=\"pg\">p.213<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “No, I don’t know.”<span class=\"pg\">p.213<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You clearly know why I was following you, don’t you?”<span class=\"pg\">p.213<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I really have no idea what you’re talking about.”<span class=\"pg\">p.213<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Why should I lie?”<span class=\"pg\">p.213<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’d at least like to hear why you followed me, from your own lips.”<span class=\"pg\">p.213<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “The underwear theft and the fire. Misfortune continues to befall Class D.”<span class=\"pg\">p.214<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “So what?”<span class=\"pg\">p.214<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Do you realize that some people suspect you?”<span class=\"pg\">p.214<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ah. I suppose since I’m an outsider, there’s not much I can do about that.”<span class=\"pg\">p.214<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s what I’m talking about.”<span class=\"pg\">p.214<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You’re saying I’m the culprit? Do you have any proof?”<span class=\"pg\">p.214<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Unfortunately, I don’t have a single shred of evidence related to the underwear theft. But I think it was you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.214<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s a pretty terrible thing to say. You don’t have any evidence, yet you suspect me?”<span class=\"pg\">p.214<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I suspect you because of today. You don’t need me to explain that, do you?”<span class=\"pg\">p.214<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Let me cut to the chase. I want you to return something you took from me,”<span class=\"pg\">p.214<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I don’t know what you’re talking about.”<span class=\"pg\">p.214<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Where are you going?”<span class=\"pg\">p.214<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Who knows?”<span class=\"pg\">p.214<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> “I have to make up for my mistake. I have to make up for my mistake.”<span class=\"pg\">p.215<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> “I can handle it well. I can do it. I can do it.”<span class=\"pg\">p.215<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Limit<\/span> The fever peaks in the downpour; she can no longer hold her head up.<span class=\"pg\">p.216<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ibuki-san. I’m going to investigate you with everything I’ve got. You don’t mind?”<span class=\"pg\">p.216<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “With everything you’ve got? Could you be a bit more specific? You mean you’re going to resort to violence?”<span class=\"pg\">p.216<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “This is your last warning. Return it…”<span class=\"pg\">p.216<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Backstory<\/span> She recalls condemning Sudou after his Class C trial — and abandoning him — now that she is considering the same violence.<span class=\"pg\">p.216<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Oh, you’re good,”<span class=\"pg\">p.217<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “An act of violence means immediate disqualification…”<span class=\"pg\">p.217<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Someone might see us here, you mean? Weren’t you willing to use violence, too?”<span class=\"pg\">p.217<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Thrown into the mud; she slips Ibuki’s grip, rolls away, and rises — the first real thanks her martial arts practice gets her.<span class=\"pg\">p.217<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Oh? You can really move, surprisingly. You practice or something?”<span class=\"pg\">p.217<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’ve…been nothing but a complete and utter failure in this test.”<span class=\"pg\">p.217<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> “I mocked people. I hated useless things, labeling them incompetent, while I was useless myself.”<span class=\"pg\">p.217<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It was you, wasn’t it? You stole the keycard.”<span class=\"pg\">p.217<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Meets Ibuki’s trained footwork in a back-and-forth exchange — no hesitation on either side to hurt.<span class=\"pg\">p.218<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You’ve been trying really hard until now. I’ll tell you the truth, as a reward. I stole the card.”<span class=\"pg\">p.218<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Watches Ibuki draw the card out and show the engraved name.<span class=\"pg\">p.218<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You gave up the truth pretty easily.”<span class=\"pg\">p.218<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It doesn’t matter if I admit it or not now. There’s no evidence I used violence against you. It’s not as though the school can make a judgment here. Isn’t that right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.218<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> The card is back in Ibuki’s pocket; fingerprints on it are her only argument for recovering it.<span class=\"pg\">p.218<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Drives her left fist into Ibuki’s solar plexus with her last strength — it pins her but does not knock her down.<span class=\"pg\">p.219<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “This is the worst… I’m already… At my limit…”<span class=\"pg\">p.219<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I don’t understand… I thought you were involved.”<span class=\"pg\">p.219<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Involved? In what?”<span class=\"pg\">p.219<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I didn’t burn the manual.”<span class=\"pg\">p.219<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You intend to keep lying even now?”<span class=\"pg\">p.219<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What would I gain by burning it? It was inevitable that people would begin searching for the criminal after the uproar. Besides, people would suspect me rather strongly. There was nothing to gain and a lot to lose.”<span class=\"pg\">p.219<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Do you think he’s in Class D? There’s a guy who figured me out before you did.”<span class=\"pg\">p.220<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Ibuki leaves the man’s name out; the page names no one.<span class=\"pg\">p.220<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “So. You can’t mean…”<span class=\"pg\">p.220<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “This conversation is over.”<span class=\"pg\">p.220<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Knocked out cold by a blunt strike to the head as the talk “ends”.<span class=\"pg\">p.220<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Do you think they’ll permit such coercive methods?”<span class=\"pg\">p.220<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Come on, now. I don’t feel like answering that.”<span class=\"pg\">p.220<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> “By attempting to fix that mistake myself, I ended up turning it into a situation that couldn’t be fixed.”<span class=\"pg\">p.220<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p206-1\">← Before: Ch.6 §6.7: the fire from her side<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p229-1\">→ After: Ch.6 §6.10: in his arms<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p229-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"action spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka ryuuen-kakeru horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune ch 6  6 10  in his arms wakes in his arms under the tree  fever high  and pieces the day together before choosing to go on alone   are you awake   ayano kouji kun   you have a high fever  don t push yourself   i knew it ibuki san stole my card   this isn t a test where you can just hide for twenty four hours a day  right  no matter what you do  you can be open to attack   i could ve avoided this if i knew how to rely on someone   when i was losing consciousness  i felt like i could hear ryuuen s voice  it s strange  i thought he d already retired  half convinced she heard his voice while unconscious  though she took him for retired   you were losing consciousness  maybe you had a dream   if it was a dream  it was a nightmare   i m sorry   why are you apologizing to me   there s no one i can apologize to except for you   if you think things are bad  then make some reliable friends  start there first   that s difficult advice  no one would want to be with me   it s unpleasant to be made fun of  though   it s just that you ve started to sound like you need allies   nobody would say that   i should have understood this a long time ago   don t talk  you re sick   i m going to try to get up to class a using my own abilities  i ll definitely recover from this failure   i m prepared to be hated by everyone else  this was all my mistake  states her goal out loud  class a on her own abilities  for her brother to acknowledge her   according to this school s system  if you fight by yourself  you won t reach class a  we need to cooperate with our classmates  it s unavoidable   i can t accept that  no matter how hard it is  i m still alone   ah  shut up already  stop talking  right now  you won t be able to convince anyone   you can t bear every responsibility  you re not that strong  unfortunately   so you re telling me to give up  i have a dream to reach class a  a dream for my brother to acknowledge me   no one said you have to give up   if you can t fight by yourself  it s better to fight with a partner  i ll lend you a hand   why  you re not the kind of person who would say such things   well  why then  i wonder  grabs his sleeve while she appeals   her grip is weak but he still feels it   i can t do that  we can t afford to lose thirty points because of me  i was the one who confronted karuizawa san and the others about using points  right  it would make me look like such an idiot   not just that  the keycard was stolen from me  too  you understand what that means   just leave me here and head back  if you do  i ll be the only one absent from roll call   what are you planning to do   by tomorrow morning  i ll try to return by myself  somehow  if i can deal with my poor health during roll call  then i ll do something about retirement   still  there s nothing else i can do  covers her eyes with her arm to hide the tears while he works out the points   yes  that s the correct decision  everything was my responsibility   can you really make it back alone by tomorrow morning   yeah  i ll be fine   horikita  do you really think that not retiring is the right decision   of course i do  retiring isn t an option for me   hey  why do you think that we ve been backed into such a corner   i failed due to my negligence  that s all   you re wrong  you re completely wrong   go  because i think of you as my friend  please listen to my request  she calls him a friend  then covers her mouth in surprise at her own words   i m going to make this right  as if it didn t happen at all   no  this is the wrong choice  the reply is untagged in the translation  it answers her plan to go on alone  so it is recorded as his   it s fine  i can  by myself  ugh   go  please  loses consciousness again while he holds her  carried unconscious to the ship and retires with a high fever at 7 58  minutes before roll call","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p229-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6 §6.10: in his arms<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.229–235<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Wakes in his arms under the tree, fever high, and pieces the day together before choosing to go on alone.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “Are you awake?”<span class=\"pg\">p.229<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Ayano…kouji-kun?”<span class=\"pg\">p.229<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “You have a high fever. Don’t push yourself.”<span class=\"pg\">p.229<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>54 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I knew it…Ibuki-san stole my card.”<span class=\"pg\">p.229<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “This isn’t a test where you can just hide for twenty-four hours a day, right? No matter what you do, you can be open to attack.”<span class=\"pg\">p.229<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I could’ve avoided this if I knew how to rely on someone…”<span class=\"pg\">p.229<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “When I was losing consciousness, I felt like I could hear Ryuuen’s voice… It’s strange, I thought he’d already retired…”<span class=\"pg\">p.229<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Half-convinced she heard his voice while unconscious, though she took him for retired.<span class=\"pg\">p.229<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You were losing consciousness. Maybe you had a dream?”<span class=\"pg\">p.229<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If it was a dream, it was a nightmare…”<span class=\"pg\">p.229<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m sorry…”<span class=\"pg\">p.230<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Why are you apologizing to me?”<span class=\"pg\">p.230<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “There’s no one I can apologize to except for you…”<span class=\"pg\">p.230<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If you think things are bad, then make some reliable friends. Start there first.”<span class=\"pg\">p.230<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s difficult advice… No one would want to be with me.”<span class=\"pg\">p.230<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It’s unpleasant to be made fun of, though…”<span class=\"pg\">p.230<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It’s just that you’ve started to sound like you need allies.”<span class=\"pg\">p.230<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Nobody would say that…”<span class=\"pg\">p.230<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I should have understood this a long time ago…”<span class=\"pg\">p.230<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Don’t talk. You’re sick.”<span class=\"pg\">p.230<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m going to try to get up to Class A using my own abilities. I’ll definitely recover from this failure…”<span class=\"pg\">p.231<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m prepared to be hated by everyone else… This was all my mistake.”<span class=\"pg\">p.231<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Goal<\/span> States her goal out loud: Class A on her own abilities, for her brother to acknowledge her.<span class=\"pg\">p.231<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “According to this school’s system, if you fight by yourself, you won’t reach Class A. We need to cooperate with our classmates. It’s unavoidable.”<span class=\"pg\">p.231<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I can’t accept that. No matter how hard it is, I’m still…alone.”<span class=\"pg\">p.231<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ah, shut up already! Stop talking. Right now, you won’t be able to convince anyone.”<span class=\"pg\">p.231<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You can’t bear every responsibility. You’re not that strong, unfortunately.”<span class=\"pg\">p.231<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “So you’re telling me to give up? I have a dream to reach Class A, a dream for my brother to acknowledge me.”<span class=\"pg\">p.231<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “No one said you have to give up.”<span class=\"pg\">p.231<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If you can’t fight by yourself, it’s better to fight with a partner. I’ll lend you a hand.”<span class=\"pg\">p.231<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Why? You’re not the kind of person who would say such things…”<span class=\"pg\">p.231<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, why then? I wonder.”<span class=\"pg\">p.231<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Voice<\/span> Grabs his sleeve while she appeals — her grip is weak but he still feels it.<span class=\"pg\">p.231<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I can’t do that. We can’t afford to lose thirty points because of me… I was the one who confronted Karuizawa-san and the others about using points, right? It would make me look like such an idiot…”<span class=\"pg\">p.233<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Not just that… The keycard was stolen from me, too. You understand what that means?”<span class=\"pg\">p.233<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Just leave me here and head back. If you do, I’ll be the only one absent from roll call.”<span class=\"pg\">p.233<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What are you planning to do?”<span class=\"pg\">p.233<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “By tomorrow morning, I’ll…try to return by myself, somehow. If I can deal with my poor health during roll call, then I’ll do something about retirement.”<span class=\"pg\">p.233<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Still, there’s nothing else I can do…”<span class=\"pg\">p.233<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Covers her eyes with her arm to hide the tears while he works out the points.<span class=\"pg\">p.233<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yes. That’s the correct decision. Everything was my responsibility.”<span class=\"pg\">p.234<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Can you really make it back alone by tomorrow morning?”<span class=\"pg\">p.234<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yeah… I’ll be fine.”<span class=\"pg\">p.234<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Horikita. Do you really think that not retiring is the right decision?”<span class=\"pg\">p.234<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Of course I do. Retiring isn’t an option for me.”<span class=\"pg\">p.234<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Hey. Why do you think that we’ve been backed into such a corner?”<span class=\"pg\">p.234<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I failed due to my negligence. That’s all.”<span class=\"pg\">p.234<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You’re wrong. You’re completely wrong.”<span class=\"pg\">p.234<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Go… Because I think of you as my friend, please listen to my request…”<span class=\"pg\">p.234<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> She calls him a friend, then covers her mouth in surprise at her own words.<span class=\"pg\">p.234<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m going to make this right… As if it didn’t happen at all.”<span class=\"pg\">p.235<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “No, this is the wrong choice.”<span class=\"pg\">p.235<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The reply is untagged in the translation; it answers her plan to go on alone, so it is recorded as his.<span class=\"pg\">p.235<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It’s fine. I can… By myself… Ugh…”<span class=\"pg\">p.235<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Go, please…”<span class=\"pg\">p.235<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Loses consciousness again while he holds her.<span class=\"pg\">p.235<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> Carried unconscious to the ship and retires with a high fever at 7:58, minutes before roll call.<span class=\"pg\">p.237<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p213-1\">← Before: Ch.6 §6.8: the pursuit<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p245-1\">→ After: Ch.7: the deck and the apology<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p245-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"action spoken","w":"sudou-ken hirata-yousuke karuizawa-kei horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune ch 7  the deck and the apology returns to the class on the ship s deck still pale after her retirement  sudou greets her  she takes back the first name permission  and karuizawa apologizes to her face   i m not too bad  i can t say that i m back to full health  more than anything else  retiring was a big mistake on my part   don t worry about it  accepts the first name for one line  then withdraws the permission   by the way  sudou kun  don t just go around calling me by my first name without permission  understand   y y yeah   but what happened  why was class d ranked first  runs untagged before karuizawa s tagged line and is left out as a chapter attribution gap   well  karuizawa san  i think you should talk to horikita san first  don t you agree   horikita san  do you have a minute   yes  there s something that we re supposed to talk about  right  faces her to eat humble pie after the accusation about the points   i m sorry   ibuki san stole my underwear  ayanokouji kun told us everything   huh  the one word reply follows the narration that she was puzzled  recorded as hers   horikita san  when you noticed that ibuki san was the culprit  she tried to run because you questioned her  right  that s why you ended up collapsing and getting sick   i heard about it from hirata kun first  he said that you found out the leaders of class a and c  that s why we had so many points  so  i m sorry for everything i said   wait a minute  i  you said i found out the leaders  identities  but i retired   wait  ayanokouji kun  what did you  both replies keep the printed three quarter marks  the classmates  praise lines    there s no need for you to be humble   horikita san  you were so incredibly awesome   when i heard that you d retired    run untagged from unnamed speakers and are left out as chapter attribution gaps   w wait a second  is buried in the crowd s congratulations while he withdraws  and shouts after him from inside it","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p245-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.7: the deck and the apology<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.245–247<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Returns to the class on the ship’s deck still pale after her retirement; Sudou greets her, she takes back the first-name permission, and Karuizawa apologizes to her face.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a> · <a href=\"hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> · <a href=\"karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“I’m not too bad. I can’t say that I’m back to full health. More than anything else, retiring was a big mistake on my part.”<span class=\"pg\">p.246<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> “Don’t worry about it.”<span class=\"pg\">p.246<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“By the way, Sudou-kun. Don’t just go around calling me by my first name without permission. Understand?”<span class=\"pg\">p.246<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>18 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> Accepts the first name for one line, then withdraws the permission.<span class=\"pg\">p.246<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Y-y-yeah.”<span class=\"pg\">p.246<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> “But…what happened? Why was Class D ranked first?” runs untagged before Karuizawa’s tagged line and is left out as a chapter attribution gap.<span class=\"pg\">p.246<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, Karuizawa-san, I think you should talk to Horikita-san first, don’t you agree?”<span class=\"pg\">p.246<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Horikita-san, do you have a minute?”<span class=\"pg\">p.246<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yes. There’s something that we’re supposed to talk about. Right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.246<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> Faces her to eat humble pie after the accusation about the points.<span class=\"pg\">p.246<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m sorry.”<span class=\"pg\">p.246<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ibuki-san stole my underwear. Ayanokouji-kun told us everything.”<span class=\"pg\">p.246<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Huh?”<span class=\"pg\">p.246<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The one-word reply follows the narration that she was puzzled; recorded as hers.<span class=\"pg\">p.246<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Horikita-san, when you noticed that Ibuki-san was the culprit, she tried to run because you questioned her, right? That’s why you ended up collapsing and getting sick…”<span class=\"pg\">p.247<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I heard about it from Hirata-kun first. He said that you found out the leaders of Class A and C. That’s why we had so many points. So, I’m…sorry for everything I said.”<span class=\"pg\">p.247<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Wait a minute. I… You said I found out the leaders’ identities? But I retired¾”<span class=\"pg\">p.247<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Wait. Ayanokouji-kun, what did you¾”<span class=\"pg\">p.247<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Both replies keep the printed three-quarter marks. The classmates’ praise lines — “There’s no need for you to be humble…”, “Horikita-san, you were so incredibly awesome!…”, “When I heard that you’d retired…” — run untagged from unnamed speakers and are left out as chapter attribution gaps.<span class=\"pg\">p.247<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “W-wait a second!”<span class=\"pg\">p.247<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Is buried in the crowd’s congratulations while he withdraws, and shouts after him from inside it.<span class=\"pg\">p.247<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p229-1\">← Before: Ch.6 §6.10: in his arms<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p250-1\">→ After: Ch.7 §7.1: the whole explanation<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p250-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"action spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka yamauchi-haruki horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune ch 7  7 1  the whole explanation section 7 1 opens with her storming the lounge for the full story  he gives it on one condition   she never investigates him   what do these test results mean  what in the world happened   you look like you don t have any idea at all   i just can t imagine it  i don t understand it at all  i have a mountain of questions   i ll tell you everything  however  my one condition is that you stay quiet on this matter  i won t compromise on this  sets the price of the story  her silence  with no compromise   what would you like to ask   what were you doing during the test  tell me  she said   when the special test was announced  i didn t focus on anything except for the additional rules  i roughly understood how to manage the 300 points  but you couldn t manipulate them as an individual   but the additional rules were really difficult to understand  if you did things normally  you wouldn t have been able to identify the leaders  right   yeah  first of all  i volunteered to join the search for the base camp  able to move freely  i planned to search out spot locations ahead of everyone else   you make it sound simple  but no one should have known the spot locations   that s not true  you didn t understand because you were ill and holed up inside the ship  but the school already gave us hints about the locations when we were sailing around the island  the circling ship   nearly three times a usual cruise s speed   and the phrase  significant scenery  were the school s hints about the spot locations  katsuragi and koenji had noticed the same hint   then  i reached the cave  i thought it was the most important base   the cave was the most important base  don t you think that the river and the well would have been more convenient  though   the spot itself wasn t what was important  its location was   but what advantage is there in going into the cave if you don t have a keycard   well  i d intended to explore various things  but in the end i discovered the leader s identity   well  i suppose that katsuragi kun was careless   no  that wasn t it   there was that guy  yahiko  remember  the one following katsuragi around  he was the leader  i saw katsuragi and yahiko at the cave  but i didn t see the moment they occupied it  after the two of them walked away  i checked if the cave was occupied or not  totsuka yahiko was class a s leader  katsuragi only displayed the card while the two were at the cave   wouldn t you have mistaken katsuragi kun as the leader  she asked   do you think that the leader would have shown off the card so carelessly in front of people   but why  why bother deliberately holding onto the card  then   because he didn t have any other choice  as far as i can tell  katsuragi is a calm and collected man  excessively cautious  there s no way he didn t understand the high risk of occupying a spot immediately after finding it  in other words  the person who occupied it was enticed by shortsighted greed   that s why there was another person   yes   so  aside from their base  class a held down at least two spots  but we didn t confirm how many they were occupying by the end of the test  if i correctly guessed the identity of their leader  though  i could invalidate all of their points   i m still not convinced  if he figured out the spot s location at such an early stage  and if he were acting alongside a lot of other people  shouldn t he have avoided trouble  even if he just had someone standing watch by the cave  it should have been sufficient claim of ownership  why would they occupy it   that was probably class a s disadvantage   their class appears perfect at first glance  but it actually has a huge schism in it  class a s internal schism is the reason katsuragi could not rely on other people   why the methods revealed class a so easily   that s why i excluded class a at that stage  and turned my attention toward class c  katsuragi was easy to understand  but with ryuuen  there were many unknown variables  to tell you the truth  he was gathering more information than i was  he d found out the identities of all of the leaders   w wait  he found out the identities of all of the leaders  so not only class d  but also the leaders for classes b and a  but that s strange  we were far from being penalized  we ended up getting first place by a wide margin  how do you intend to explain that   this is a little difficult to explain  but the reason i made you retire is the answer   wait  the answer is you made me retire  what in the world did you do   oh  that reminds me  i didn t return it to the school yet  takes the single card he hands her  the engraved name reads  ayanokouji kiyotaka   this is a keycard  why do you   wait  why does  the leader card in his pocket bears his own name   the test had to be fair  the rules were fundamentally created to be fair   that s  the leader would be absent  so the rights of exclusive possession would disappear   wrong  in the manual  it says   it is impossible to change the leader without suitable justification  don t you think that retirement is suitable enough justification  the manual s leader change clause   retirement is suitable justification  the additional rules were made to be broken when someone is out through poor health or injury  with the base camp clause as the parallel case   so then  you made me  horikita suzune retired and he was appointed in her place   the leader the other classes were supposed to guess at the end  there can only be one   that s why even though class c knew you were the leader  we avoided penalties   but wait  ibuki san stole my card  but what if i d protected it really thoroughly   did you drop the card on purpose back then  well  i suppose that yamauchi kun s actions might have provided ibuki san the opportunity to hatch a plan to steal the keycard  the mud bribe she took read back as the opening that let ibuki take the card   unless i knew what ibuki san was aiming for right at the start  i couldn t have done anything  ibuki was picked up by class d  but not by chance   the near coincidence of two people saved by two separate classes dissolved once kaneda in class b came out as a spy ryuuen had sent   besides  ibuki has a habit of looking people in the eye when she s lying   wait  when she lied she would look the person in the eye  isn t it usually the opposite   generally speaking  you avoid eye contact if you have a guilty conscience  however  it was the opposite for her  i think that she made eye contact to make the person think that the lie was the truth  she probably didn t even notice it herself   her goal was probably to find the keycard  but she might have intended to disrupt class d at the same time   but i have to wonder why ibuki san specifically stole my keycard  all she needed was to check my name   that was likely ibuki s intention from the start  however  she ran into unexpected trouble  ibuki carried a digital camera to take a picture of the keycard  a photo would have made the leader s identity clear to anyone and let her profit   to take a picture with the camera  why would she go so far   if she had a picture  then the leader s identity would have been clear for anyone to see  right  if she had convincing evidence  she would have profited   i don t quite understand  did ryuuen kun not trust ibuki san   that wasn t it   from here on out  i don t have any evidence of what i m saying  think of it as my intuition  which i derived from the test results  at the end of the test  class a had 270 points  his own label  intuition from the results  with no evidence   class a ended the test with 270 points and had not used a single one  classes a and c were connected behind the scenes  class c sacrificed its own points and bought whatever class a needed  and by taking all of c s tools class a spent the week without using any points   ibuki s evidence went to someone in class a   by the way  i became aware of class c s leader after half of the students retired  it was certain that the leader would have remained on the island  right   even so  we weren t supposed to know who was left   no  i was almost one hundred percent sure that ryuuen was still on the island  ibuki hiding a wireless transceiver in the ground proved someone was left on the island for her to contact  ryuuen set it on a table unguarded while on vacation   no one else controlled it  and his mistake was trusting no one   my god  i don t even have the words  horikita answered  facing the truth  the test in one line  class a failed on its internal rift  class b ran defense only and paid for believing kaneda  class c sent spies and negotiated with a  and class d avoided damage because he had been appointed the leader   i don t like this  you completely used me  like a pawn   yeah  i can t deny that  i wouldn t be surprised if you never want to speak to me ever again  accepts the charge without defense  he was aware of what he had done   well  i ll be heading back to my room now  i m really tired  i said   wait  we re not done talking   what  i just want to relax in my room  if possible   after you explain everything  there are still some things we need to talk about  right   well like what   the reason why you participated in this special test  was it to fight alone  i don t care that you used me this time  i want to know why you put in the effort when you dislike trouble   i wonder  her real question is his principles  not the test   the explanation so far was the less important part to her   i don t have any room for doubt  i understand your talents now  if you help me  aiming for class a seems a realistic enough goal  but what are your principles  why did you do this  names her own goal with him in it  class a  realistically  if his principles hold   because i was touched that you tried to fight all alone when you were ill   you wouldn t normally say that kind of thing  it s easy to spot the lie   well  what i mean is i don t feel like explaining it   i don t mind helping you get up to class a  however  i have one condition  do not investigate me  if you promise not to touch on this subject ever again  i will help you  the deal is struck  his help toward class a in exchange for his past staying buried   if you don t want to talk  there s nothing i can really do about that  if you ll help  i have no reason to refuse you  i m not interested in digging things up that are better left buried  after all  you dislike trouble  takes his hand without hesitation  the handshake is firm    i work for me  you do things for yourself    and the battle to raise the class from the bottom begins","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p250-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.7 §7.1: the whole explanation<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.250–258<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Section 7.1 opens with her storming the lounge for the full story; he gives it on one condition — she never investigates him.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"yamauchi-haruki.html\">Yamauchi Haruki<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“What do these test results mean? What in the world happened?”<span class=\"pg\">p.250<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “You look like you don’t have any idea at all.”<span class=\"pg\">p.250<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I just can’t imagine it. I don’t understand it at all. I have a mountain of questions.”<span class=\"pg\">p.250<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>91 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’ll tell you everything. However, my one condition is that you stay quiet on this matter. I won’t compromise on this.”<span class=\"pg\">p.250<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Sets the price of the story: her silence, with no compromise.<span class=\"pg\">p.250<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What would you like to ask?”<span class=\"pg\">p.250<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What were you doing during the test? Tell me,” she said.<span class=\"pg\">p.250<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “When the special test was announced, I didn’t focus on anything except for the additional rules. I roughly understood how to manage the 300 points, but you couldn’t manipulate them as an individual.”<span class=\"pg\">p.250<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “But the additional rules were really difficult to understand. If you did things normally, you wouldn’t have been able to identify the leaders. Right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.250<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yeah. First of all, I volunteered to join the search for the base camp. Able to move freely, I planned to search out spot locations ahead of everyone else.”<span class=\"pg\">p.250<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You make it sound simple, but no one should have known the spot locations.”<span class=\"pg\">p.251<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s not true. You didn’t understand because you were ill and holed up inside the ship, but the school already gave us hints about the locations when we were sailing around the island.”<span class=\"pg\">p.251<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Fact<\/span> The circling ship — nearly three times a usual cruise’s speed — and the phrase “significant scenery” were the school’s hints about the spot locations; Katsuragi and Kōenji had noticed the same hint.<span class=\"pg\">p.251<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Then, I reached the cave. I thought it was the most important base.”<span class=\"pg\">p.251<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “The cave was the most important base? Don’t you think that the river and the well would have been more convenient, though?”<span class=\"pg\">p.251<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “The spot itself wasn’t what was important. Its location was.”<span class=\"pg\">p.251<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “But what advantage is there in going into the cave if you don’t have a keycard?”<span class=\"pg\">p.251<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, I’d intended to explore various things, but in the end I discovered the leader’s identity.”<span class=\"pg\">p.251<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, I suppose that Katsuragi-kun was careless.”<span class=\"pg\">p.251<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “No, that wasn’t it.”<span class=\"pg\">p.251<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “There was that guy, Yahiko, remember? The one following Katsuragi around? He was the leader. I saw Katsuragi and Yahiko at the cave, but I didn’t see the moment they occupied it. After the two of them walked away, I checked if the cave was occupied or not.”<span class=\"pg\">p.251<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Fact<\/span> Totsuka Yahiko was Class A’s leader; Katsuragi only displayed the card while the two were at the cave.<span class=\"pg\">p.251<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Wouldn’t you have mistaken Katsuragi-kun as the leader?” she asked.<span class=\"pg\">p.252<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Do you think that the leader would have shown off the card so carelessly in front of people?”<span class=\"pg\">p.252<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “But why? Why bother deliberately holding onto the card, then?”<span class=\"pg\">p.252<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Because he didn’t have any other choice. As far as I can tell, Katsuragi is a calm and collected man, excessively cautious. There’s no way he didn’t understand the high risk of occupying a spot immediately after finding it. In other words, the person who occupied it was enticed by shortsighted greed.”<span class=\"pg\">p.252<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s…why there was another person.”<span class=\"pg\">p.252<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yes.”<span class=\"pg\">p.252<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “So, aside from their base, Class A held down at least two spots, but we didn’t confirm how many they were occupying by the end of the test. If I correctly guessed the identity of their leader, though, I could invalidate all of their points.”<span class=\"pg\">p.252<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m still not convinced. If he figured out the spot’s location at such an early stage, and if he were acting alongside a lot of other people, shouldn’t he have avoided trouble? Even if he just had someone standing watch by the cave, it should have been sufficient claim of ownership. Why would they occupy it?”<span class=\"pg\">p.252<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That was probably Class A’s disadvantage.”<span class=\"pg\">p.253<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Their class appears perfect at first glance, but it actually has a huge schism in it.”<span class=\"pg\">p.253<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Fact<\/span> Class A’s internal schism is the reason Katsuragi could not rely on other people — why the methods revealed Class A so easily.<span class=\"pg\">p.253<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s why I excluded Class A at that stage, and turned my attention toward Class C. Katsuragi was easy to understand, but with Ryuuen, there were many unknown variables. To tell you the truth, he was gathering more information than I was. He’d found out the identities of all of the leaders.”<span class=\"pg\">p.253<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “W-wait, he found out the identities of all of the leaders… So not only Class D, but also the leaders for Classes B and A? But that’s strange. We were far from being penalized; we ended up getting first place by a wide margin. How do you intend to explain that?”<span class=\"pg\">p.253<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “This is a little difficult to explain, but the reason I made you retire is the answer.”<span class=\"pg\">p.253<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Wait, the answer is you made me retire? What in the world did you do?”<span class=\"pg\">p.253<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Oh, that reminds me. I didn’t return it to the school yet.”<span class=\"pg\">p.253<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Takes the single card he hands her; the engraved name reads “Ayanokouji Kiyotaka.”<span class=\"pg\">p.253<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “This is a keycard. Why do you…?!”<span class=\"pg\">p.253<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Wait, why does…?”<span class=\"pg\">p.253<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Fact<\/span> The leader card in his pocket bears his own name.<span class=\"pg\">p.253<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “The test had to be fair. The rules were fundamentally created to be fair.”<span class=\"pg\">p.253<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s… The leader would be absent. So the rights of exclusive possession would disappear…”<span class=\"pg\">p.254<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Wrong. In the manual, it says, ‘It is impossible to change the leader without suitable justification.’ Don’t you think that retirement is suitable enough justification?”<span class=\"pg\">p.254<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> The manual’s leader-change clause — retirement is suitable justification; the additional rules were made to be broken when someone is out through poor health or injury, with the base-camp clause as the parallel case.<span class=\"pg\">p.254<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “So then, you made me…?”<span class=\"pg\">p.254<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Fact<\/span> Horikita Suzune retired and he was appointed in her place — the leader the other classes were supposed to guess at the end, there can only be one.<span class=\"pg\">p.254<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s why even though Class C knew you were the leader, we avoided penalties.”<span class=\"pg\">p.254<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “But wait. Ibuki-san stole my card, but what if I’d protected it really thoroughly?”<span class=\"pg\">p.254<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Did you drop the card on purpose back then? Well, I suppose that Yamauchi-kun’s actions might have provided Ibuki-san the opportunity to hatch a plan to steal the keycard…”<span class=\"pg\">p.254<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yamauchi Haruki<\/b> The mud bribe she took read back as the opening that let Ibuki take the card.<span class=\"pg\">p.254<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Unless I knew what Ibuki-san was aiming for right at the start, I couldn’t have done anything…”<span class=\"pg\">p.254<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Fact<\/span> Ibuki was picked up by Class D, but not by chance — the near-coincidence of two people saved by two separate classes dissolved once Kaneda in Class B came out as a spy Ryuuen had sent.<span class=\"pg\">p.255<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Besides, Ibuki has a habit of looking people in the eye when she’s lying.”<span class=\"pg\">p.255<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Wait, when she lied she would look the person in the eye? Isn’t it usually the opposite?”<span class=\"pg\">p.255<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Generally speaking, you avoid eye contact if you have a guilty conscience. However, it was the opposite for her. I think that she made eye contact to make the person think that the lie was the truth. She probably didn’t even notice it herself.”<span class=\"pg\">p.255<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Her goal was probably to find the keycard, but she might have intended to disrupt Class D at the same time.”<span class=\"pg\">p.255<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “But I have to wonder why Ibuki-san specifically stole my keycard. All she needed was to check my name.”<span class=\"pg\">p.255<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That was likely Ibuki’s intention from the start. However, she ran into unexpected trouble.”<span class=\"pg\">p.255<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Fact<\/span> Ibuki carried a digital camera to take a picture of the keycard; a photo would have made the leader’s identity clear to anyone and let her profit.<span class=\"pg\">p.255<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “To take a picture…with the camera? Why would she go so far?”<span class=\"pg\">p.255<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If she had a picture, then the leader’s identity would have been clear for anyone to see, right? If she had convincing evidence, she would have profited.”<span class=\"pg\">p.255<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I don’t quite understand… Did Ryuuen-kun not trust Ibuki-san?”<span class=\"pg\">p.255<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That wasn’t it.”<span class=\"pg\">p.255<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “From here on out, I don’t have any evidence of what I’m saying. Think of it as my intuition, which I derived from the test results. At the end of the test, Class A had 270 points.”<span class=\"pg\">p.256<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inference, not stated<\/span> His own label: intuition from the results, with no evidence — Class A ended the test with 270 points and had not used a single one.<span class=\"pg\">p.256<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Fact<\/span> Classes A and C were connected behind the scenes: Class C sacrificed its own points and bought whatever Class A needed, and by taking all of C’s tools Class A spent the week without using any points — Ibuki’s evidence went to someone in Class A.<span class=\"pg\">p.256<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “By the way, I became aware of Class C’s leader after half of the students retired. It was certain that the leader would have remained on the island, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.256<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Even so, we weren’t supposed to know who was left.”<span class=\"pg\">p.256<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “No, I was almost one hundred percent sure that Ryuuen was still on the island.”<span class=\"pg\">p.256<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Fact<\/span> Ibuki hiding a wireless transceiver in the ground proved someone was left on the island for her to contact; Ryuuen set it on a table unguarded while on vacation — no one else controlled it, and his mistake was trusting no one.<span class=\"pg\">p.256<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “My god… I don’t even have the words,” Horikita answered, facing the truth.<span class=\"pg\">p.257<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Fact<\/span> The test in one line: Class A failed on its internal rift, Class B ran defense-only and paid for believing Kaneda, Class C sent spies and negotiated with A, and Class D avoided damage because he had been appointed the leader.<span class=\"pg\">p.257<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I don’t like this. You completely used me, like a pawn.”<span class=\"pg\">p.257<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yeah. I can’t deny that. I wouldn’t be surprised if you never want to speak to me ever again.”<span class=\"pg\">p.257<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Accepts the charge without defense; he was aware of what he had done.<span class=\"pg\">p.257<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, I’ll be heading back to my room now. I’m really tired,” I said.<span class=\"pg\">p.257<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Wait. We’re not done talking.”<span class=\"pg\">p.257<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What? I just want to relax in my room, if possible.”<span class=\"pg\">p.257<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “After you explain everything. There are still some things we need to talk about, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.257<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well…like what?”<span class=\"pg\">p.257<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “The reason why you participated in this special test. Was it to fight alone? I don’t care that you used me this time. I want to know why you put in the effort when you dislike trouble.”<span class=\"pg\">p.257<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I wonder.”<span class=\"pg\">p.257<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Her real question is his principles, not the test — the explanation so far was the less important part to her.<span class=\"pg\">p.257<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I don’t have any room for doubt. I understand your talents now. If you help me, aiming for Class A seems a realistic enough goal. But what are your principles? Why did you do this?”<span class=\"pg\">p.257<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Goal<\/span> Names her own goal with him in it: Class A, realistically, if his principles hold.<span class=\"pg\">p.257<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Because I was touched that you tried to fight all alone when you were ill.”<span class=\"pg\">p.257<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You wouldn’t normally say that kind of thing. It’s easy to spot the lie.”<span class=\"pg\">p.258<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, what I mean is I don’t feel like explaining it.”<span class=\"pg\">p.258<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I don’t mind helping you get up to Class A. However, I have one condition. Do not investigate me. If you promise not to touch on this subject ever again, I will help you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.258<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> The deal is struck: his help toward Class A in exchange for his past staying buried.<span class=\"pg\">p.258<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If you don’t want to talk, there’s nothing I can really do about that. If you’ll help, I have no reason to refuse you. I’m not interested in digging things up that are better left buried. After all, you dislike trouble.”<span class=\"pg\">p.258<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Takes his hand without hesitation; the handshake is firm — “I work for me. You do things for yourself.” — and the battle to raise the class from the bottom begins.<span class=\"pg\">p.258<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p245-1\">← Before: Ch.7: the deck and the apology<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4-p13-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"","w":"horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune ch 2  the three  the thief  the friend type named in the hallway defence of ayanokoji s small circle  hirata s counter  that s not true   he has sudou kun and the guys  and horikita san  listed with kushida and sakura as the three he could talk with   his school life wasn t all that bad  on the thanks for finding the culprit  he wasn t even useful   horikita found the underwear thief  said to hirata for him to understand  horikita isn t the type to make friends easily","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4-p13-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2: the three, the thief, the friend-type<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.13, p.15–16, p.20<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named in the hallway defence of Ayanokōji’s small circle.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Hirata’s counter: that’s not true — he has Sudou-kun and the guys, and Horikita-san.<span class=\"pg\">p.13<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Listed with Kushida and Sakura as the three he could talk with — his school life wasn’t all that bad.<span class=\"pg\">p.15<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> On the thanks for finding the culprit: he wasn’t even useful — Horikita found the underwear thief.<span class=\"pg\">p.16<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Said to Hirata for him to understand: Horikita isn’t the type to make friends easily.<span class=\"pg\">p.20<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4-p30-1\">→ After: Ch.2 §2.2: the message chat<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4-p30-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune ch 2  2 2  the message chat chat only  ayanokoji messages her about the school s test notice  she replies instantly   yeah  i did   chat reply  the translation leaves the thread s lines untagged   mine says 20 40  that seems like a pretty big difference   chat   because your time is earlier  i look forward to hearing your report   chat  replies instantly   against her usual half day  sometimes days  reading lag  two further chat lines sit unassigned in the translation   i m curious about the difference in start times  and  we can t know anything for sure at this point  the volume attribution list keeps them  off page  hirata s whole lunch ask is about winning her over  routed through ayanokoji  the chat partner with the earlier slot  she defers his report","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4-p30-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2 §2.2: the message chat<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.30–31<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Chat only: Ayanokōji messages her about the school’s test notice; she replies instantly.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Yeah. I did.” (chat reply; the translation leaves the thread’s lines untagged)<span class=\"pg\">p.30<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Mine says 20:40. That seems like a pretty big difference.” (chat)<span class=\"pg\">p.30<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Because your time is earlier, I look forward to hearing your report.” (chat)<span class=\"pg\">p.31<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Replies instantly — against her usual half-day, sometimes days, reading lag.<span class=\"pg\">p.30<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Two further chat lines sit unassigned in the translation: “I’m curious about the difference in start times…” and “We can’t know anything for sure at this point.” The volume attribution list keeps them.<span class=\"pg\">p.30–31<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Off-page: Hirata’s whole lunch ask is about winning her over, routed through Ayanokōji.<span class=\"pg\">p.17–19<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> The chat partner with the earlier slot; she defers his report.<span class=\"pg\">p.30–31<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4-p13-1\">← Before: Ch.2: the three, the thief, the friend-type<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4-p51-1\">→ After: Ch.2 §2.5: the Katsuragi warning and the cold exit<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4-p51-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"spoken","w":"katsuragi-kouhei kanzaki-ryuuji ryuuen-kakeru hirata-yousuke horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune ch 2  2 5  the katsuragi warning and the cold exit off screen first   ayanokoji reports the rabbit rules to her by chat   then on the second deck she faces katsuragi  holds against kanzaki s interlude  and turns her back on ryuen  receives his chat report on the rabbit group s rules  her reply is not printed   yes  i am  and what exactly does that have to do with you   to katsuragi   you wanted to speak with me  funny  didn t you completely ignore me the other day   that s rather petty  from class a s perspective  are we such a big deal  i mean  there s a significant gap in points between us   you needn t concern yourself  class d has always been regarded as inferior  i d welcome any change in our reputation   what do you mean   when katsuragi calls the island win luck   we haven t gotten into college yet  i don t think you and i are so different  the school arbitrarily divided us into different classes  don t forget that   if we re going to continue this pointless conversation  i d prefer to just go inside  besides  it s about time   flipping her hair away from ryuen  doesn t back down before the class a entourage  the narration credits her   weak willed students would ingratiate themselves  she acts as she always does  reads her own new reputation  other classes now treat her selfishness as class concern and fear her as a hidden mastermind  the pivot from his island test indifference to a class a threat  declines his rescue    you needn t concern yourself  exits on him mid provocation  both summoned to the 20 40 meeting  see hirata s row","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4-p51-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2 §2.5: the Katsuragi warning and the cold exit<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.51, p.55–61<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Off-screen first — Ayanokōji reports the Rabbit rules to her by chat — then on the second deck she faces Katsuragi, holds against Kanzaki’s interlude, and turns her back on Ryūen.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"katsuragi-kouhei.html\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/a> · <a href=\"kanzaki-ryuuji.html\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/a> · <a href=\"ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Yes, I am. And what exactly does that have to do with you?” (to Katsuragi)<span class=\"pg\">p.55<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“You wanted to speak with me? Funny. Didn’t you completely ignore me the other day?”<span class=\"pg\">p.55<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“That’s rather petty. From Class A’s perspective, are we such a big deal? I mean, there’s a significant gap in points between us.”<span class=\"pg\">p.56<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>11 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Receives his chat report on the Rabbit group’s rules; her reply is not printed.<span class=\"pg\">p.51<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You needn’t concern yourself. Class D has always been regarded as inferior. I’d welcome any change in our reputation.”<span class=\"pg\">p.56<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What do you mean?” (when Katsuragi calls the island win luck)<span class=\"pg\">p.57<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “We haven’t gotten into college yet. I don’t think you and I are so different. The school arbitrarily divided us into different classes. Don’t forget that.”<span class=\"pg\">p.57<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If we’re going to continue this pointless conversation, I’d prefer to just go inside. Besides, it’s about time.” (flipping her hair away from Ryūen)<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Doesn’t back down before the Class A entourage; the narration credits her — weak-willed students would ingratiate themselves, she acts as she always does.<span class=\"pg\">p.55–61<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Reads her own new reputation: other classes now treat her selfishness as class concern and fear her as a hidden mastermind.<span class=\"pg\">p.56<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> The pivot from his island-test indifference to a Class A threat.<span class=\"pg\">p.55–57<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/b> Declines his rescue — “You needn’t concern yourself.”<span class=\"pg\">p.56<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Exits on him mid-provocation.<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Both summoned to the 20:40 meeting (see Hirata’s row).<span class=\"pg\">p.54<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4-p30-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.2: the message chat<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4-p52-1\">→ After: Ch.2: summoned, and the smarts check<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4-p52-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"","w":"horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune ch 2  summoned  and the smarts check named in the wake up sequence   her meeting call is what moves the floor  he shuts off the alarm he d wanted to check on horikita with anyway  it was just before 20 30  the time she had been summoned   hirata and he step into the hallway  a reply in the hallway  he has not been thinking about the exam the way hirata  horikita  and yukimura have   and he isn t smart either  so he hasn t really noticed much","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4-p52-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2: summoned, and the smarts check<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.52–53<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named in the wake-up sequence — her meeting call is what moves the floor.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> He shuts off the alarm he’d wanted to check on Horikita with anyway; it was just before 20:30, the time she had been summoned — Hirata and he step into the hallway.<span class=\"pg\">p.52<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> A reply in the hallway: he has not been thinking about the exam the way Hirata, Horikita, and Yukimura have — and he isn’t smart either, so he hasn’t really noticed much.<span class=\"pg\">p.53<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4-p51-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.5: the Katsuragi warning and the cold exit<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4-p63-1\">→ After: Ch.3 §3.0: the Blue Ocean briefing<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4-p63-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"action spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka ryuuen-kakeru ibuki-mio katsuragi-kouhei hirata-yousuke kushida-kikyou sakayanagi-arisu horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune ch 3  3 0  the blue ocean briefing meets ayanokoji at the empty blue ocean cafe an hour early  hands over her memorized dragon group list at 8 00  and holds the table through ryuen s interrupt   you re rather early   that s not my problem  as i ve still arrived before the designated time  besides  how would i know if you d been waiting even ten hours or more  the narrator calls her one of the very few people at this school he could call a friend   and a thorn because she knows something about his hidden life  hands ayanokoji a slip of paper  the dragon roster she wrote and memorized  biased  to the point where i can t imagine it s a coincidence   you mean ichinose san being in your group  don t you  i suppose only the class b students know if she s really excellent or not  a leader s qualities and level of excellence aren t necessarily directly proportional  said horikita   from what we can deduce  i wonder if there s a certain method they re using to sort us into the twelve groups  ayanokouji kun  your grades are very similar to karuizawa san s  are they grouping us based on our scores  oh  but yukimura kun has high academic ability  and so does kouenji kun  they re at the top of the class  said horikita   no  we weren t chosen  i m not sure if we should be happy or sad   even so  i don t like how they wrote it  it s like they re saying i m not qualified to be the vip   i look forward to your results  said horikita   for the sake of reference  who are you most wary of  based on how things have been going  i wanted your thoughts  said horikita   that was fast   on his instant  ryuuen   what about katsuragi kun  it s because of him that class a managed to quickly hold down that prime spot on the island  isn t he someone worth watching   i m curious about some things concerning the vip s identity  even after reading the message and thinking about it  did you notice any unnatural sounding phrases in the school s email  and the strict  horikita said   cut off by ayanokoji s finger   i ve warned you not to call me by my first name  ryuuen kun  also  considering you were a turncoat who only pretended to be our friend  it s odd you d show your face  ibuki san   as if i would tell you  perhaps you d like to tell us about your message  horikita responded   i have nothing to tell you  horikita responded   regrettably  i must decline your offer  violent actions are considered a violation of the test rules  if you do happen to strike me  i will not hesitate to report it to the school  at any rate  please feel free to do whatever you please  she said flatly   since we re all together  how about we have some coffee  it seems a good time to enjoy a nice cup  horikita offered  narration credits her acting  she never shakes  and probably does not think of it as acting   well  that s understandable  he couldn t have guessed that someone from class d would do so well  isn t that why you and ibuki san are here  you came to check on me  am i wrong  asked horikita   of course  horikita answered  sipping her coffee  she seemed at ease  which was unusual   think whatever you like  though i wonder how did you figure out my strategy  you only saw the results of the test  how do you know the way in which points were gained and lost  those details are supposed to be unknown  countered horikita   do you think that was hard to deduce  any idiot could have figured that out if they thought about it for a minute  even katsuragi kun  who you ve been making fun of  answered horikita   is it possible that i d simply taken the proper precautions  preparing for the unknown is absolutely basic logic  the moment ibuki san met class d  i took all possibilities into account  you were so confident  but your argument ended up being flimsy  you ve said nothing surprising  responded horikita   i m afraid i can t understand you at all  i have no close friends  the closest i have would be ayanokouji kun here  and he s always dragging me down  i d be hard pressed to say that he s working with me  sad  but true  answered horikita  draws fire onto ayanokoji to make him look useless    well done  the narration says   while denying the second leader theory   however  if we did change leaders  he wouldn t be the most likely candidate   well  i m sorry  but what you re saying is complete nonsense    does it embarrass you that a girl managed to see through your   schemes  asked horikita   my goodness  that was rather thoughtful  said horikita   it sounds like you really want to believe that we have a secret weapon in our class  observed horikita  snaps when ryuen photographs her without permission   don t take my photo without permission   well  isn t that a good thing  i don t particularly care  besides  if you just arbitrarily jump to conclusions  why bother badgering me to confirm them  asked horikita   let me ask you something  i know it hurts that i saw through you  but why are you so fixated on me  aren t you concerned about anyone else  like ichinose san  or katsuragi kun  going by the rumors  there s someone named sakayanagi  too  shouldn t the people in the classes above c be your concern  you should be able to at least answer that  i think  said horikita   not really  it s just that i hate your sarcastic way of speaking  i ve always aimed to reach class a  so i assumed i d be attracting a lot of attention  she answered   really  i think he just doesn t like that i found him out  and wanted to trick me into revealing the truth  i can t imagine he narrowed down the list of potential candidates to you  besides  even if he knew your identity  you d be the only one in trouble  replied horikita   you re overthinking things  no one thinks you re involved  despite what he said  he thinks you re an ordinary person  considering your lackluster achievements in the first semester  said horikita   discussion is likely useless from here on out  we ll go our separate ways  anyway  excellent work  if you make any progress  give me a report  the morning partner  hands him the list  takes his wary name  and closes with a standing report request  the full confrontation   first name  spy  island result  photo   and she never leaves the seat until he does  names the turncoat  declines the rematch on rules  and offers her coffee  the dream team anchor  the worth watching rival  and the man ryuen says still credits her with the island win  dragon groupmate named on her list  dragon groupmate named on her list  the rumoured name she throws at ryuen to break his focus","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4-p63-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3 §3.0: the Blue Ocean briefing<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.63–77<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Meets Ayanokōji at the empty Blue Ocean café an hour early, hands over her memorized Dragon group list at 8:00, and holds the table through Ryūen’s interrupt.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"ibuki-mio.html\">Ibuki Mio<\/a> · <a href=\"katsuragi-kouhei.html\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/a> · <a href=\"hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> · <a href=\"kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a> <span class=\"n\">+1 more<\/span><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“You’re rather early.”<span class=\"pg\">p.63<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“That’s not my problem, as I’ve still arrived before the designated time. Besides, how would I know if you’d been waiting even ten hours or more?”<span class=\"pg\">p.63<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“You mean Ichinose-san being in your group, don’t you? I suppose only the Class B students know if she’s really excellent or not. A leader’s qualities and level of excellence aren’t necessarily directly proportional,” said…”<span class=\"pg\">p.64<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>42 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The narrator calls her one of the very few people at this school he could call a friend — and a thorn because she knows something about his hidden life.<span class=\"pg\">p.63<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Hands Ayanokōji a slip of paper: the Dragon roster she wrote and memorized, biased “to the point where I can’t imagine it’s a coincidence.”<span class=\"pg\">p.64<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You mean Ichinose-san being in your group, don’t you? I suppose only the Class B students know if she’s really excellent or not. A leader’s qualities and level of excellence aren’t necessarily directly proportional,” said Horikita.<span class=\"pg\">p.64<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “From what we can deduce, I wonder if there’s a certain method they’re using to sort us into the twelve groups? Ayanokouji-kun, your grades are very similar to Karuizawa-san’s. Are they grouping us based on our scores? Oh, but Yukimura-kun has high academic ability, and so does Kouenji-kun. They’re at the top of the class,” said Horikita.<span class=\"pg\">p.65<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “No, we weren’t chosen. I’m not sure if we should be happy or sad.”<span class=\"pg\">p.66<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Even so, I don’t like how they wrote it. It’s like they’re saying I’m not qualified to be the VIP.”<span class=\"pg\">p.66<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I look forward to your results,” said Horikita.<span class=\"pg\">p.67<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “For the sake of reference, who are you most wary of? Based on how things have been going, I wanted your thoughts,” said Horikita.<span class=\"pg\">p.67<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That was fast.” (on his instant “Ryuuen”)<span class=\"pg\">p.67<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What about Katsuragi-kun? It’s because of him that Class A managed to quickly hold down that prime spot on the island. Isn’t he someone worth watching?”<span class=\"pg\">p.67<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m curious about some things concerning the VIP’s identity. Even after reading the message and thinking about it, did you notice any unnatural-sounding phrases in the school’s email? And the strict—” Horikita said. (cut off by Ayanokōji’s finger)<span class=\"pg\">p.68<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’ve warned you not to call me by my first name, Ryuuen-kun. Also, considering you were a turncoat who only pretended to be our friend, it’s odd you’d show your face, Ibuki-san.”<span class=\"pg\">p.68<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “As if I would tell you. Perhaps you’d like to tell us about your message?” Horikita responded.<span class=\"pg\">p.68<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I have nothing to tell you,” Horikita responded.<span class=\"pg\">p.69<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Regrettably, I must decline your offer. Violent actions are considered a violation of the test rules. If you do happen to strike me, I will not hesitate to report it to the school. At any rate, please feel free to do whatever you please,” she said flatly.<span class=\"pg\">p.69<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Since we’re all together, how about we have some coffee? It seems a good time to enjoy a nice cup,” Horikita offered.<span class=\"pg\">p.69<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Narration credits her acting: she never shakes, and probably does not think of it as acting.<span class=\"pg\">p.69<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, that’s understandable. He couldn’t have guessed that someone from Class D would do so well. Isn’t that why you and Ibuki-san are here? You came to check on me. Am I wrong?” asked Horikita.<span class=\"pg\">p.70<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Of course,” Horikita answered, sipping her coffee. She seemed at ease, which was unusual.<span class=\"pg\">p.70<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Think whatever you like. Though I wonder…how did you figure out my strategy? You only saw the results of the test. How do you know the way in which points were gained and lost? Those details are supposed to be unknown,” countered Horikita.<span class=\"pg\">p.72<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Do you think that was hard to deduce? Any idiot could have figured that out if they thought about it for a minute. Even Katsuragi-kun, who you’ve been making fun of,” answered Horikita.<span class=\"pg\">p.72<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Is it possible that I’d simply taken the proper precautions? Preparing for the unknown is absolutely basic logic. The moment Ibuki-san met Class D, I took all possibilities into account. You were so confident, but your argument ended up being flimsy. You’ve said nothing surprising,” responded Horikita.<span class=\"pg\">p.72–73<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m afraid I can’t understand you at all. I have no close friends. The closest I have would be Ayanokouji-kun here, and he’s always dragging me down. I’d be hard-pressed to say that he’s working with me. Sad, but true,” answered Horikita.<span class=\"pg\">p.73<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Draws fire onto Ayanokōji to make him look useless — “Well done,” the narration says — while denying the second-leader theory.<span class=\"pg\">p.73<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “However, if we did change leaders, he wouldn’t be the most likely candidate.”<span class=\"pg\">p.73<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, I’m sorry, but what you’re saying is complete nonsense. … Does it embarrass you that a girl managed to see through your … schemes?” asked Horikita.<span class=\"pg\">p.73-74<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “My goodness, that was rather thoughtful,” said Horikita.<span class=\"pg\">p.74<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It sounds like you really want to believe that we have a secret weapon in our class,” observed Horikita.<span class=\"pg\">p.74<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Snaps when Ryūen photographs her without permission: “Don’t take my photo without permission!”<span class=\"pg\">p.74<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, isn’t that a good thing? I don’t particularly care. Besides, if you just arbitrarily jump to conclusions, why bother badgering me to confirm them?” asked Horikita.<span class=\"pg\">p.75<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Let me ask you something. I know it hurts that I saw through you, but why are you so fixated on me? Aren’t you concerned about anyone else? Like Ichinose-san, or Katsuragi-kun? Going by the rumors, there’s someone named Sakayanagi, too. Shouldn’t the people in the classes above C be your concern? You should be able to at least answer that, I think,” said Horikita.<span class=\"pg\">p.75<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Not really. It’s just that I hate your sarcastic way of speaking. I’ve always aimed to reach Class A, so I assumed I’d be attracting a lot of attention,” she answered.<span class=\"pg\">p.75<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Really? I think he just doesn’t like that I found him out, and wanted to trick me into revealing the truth. I can’t imagine he narrowed down the list of potential candidates to you. Besides, even if he knew your identity, you’d be the only one in trouble,” replied Horikita.<span class=\"pg\">p.75–76<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You’re overthinking things. No one thinks you’re involved. Despite what he said, he thinks you’re an ordinary person, considering your lackluster achievements in the first semester,” said Horikita.<span class=\"pg\">p.76<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Discussion is likely useless from here on out. We’ll go our separate ways. Anyway, excellent work. If you make any progress, give me a report.”<span class=\"pg\">p.76<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> The morning partner; hands him the list, takes his wary-name, and closes with a standing report request.<span class=\"pg\">p.63–77<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> The full confrontation — first name, spy, island result, photo — and she never leaves the seat until he does.<span class=\"pg\">p.68–75<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ibuki Mio<\/b> Names the turncoat, declines the rematch on rules, and offers her coffee.<span class=\"pg\">p.68–69<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> The dream-team anchor, the worth-watching rival, and the man Ryūen says still credits her with the island win.<span class=\"pg\">p.64, 67, 70, 72–75<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Dragon groupmate named on her list.<span class=\"pg\">p.64<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> Dragon groupmate named on her list.<span class=\"pg\">p.64<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/b> The rumoured name she throws at Ryūen to break his focus.<span class=\"pg\">p.75<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4-p52-1\">← Before: Ch.2: summoned, and the smarts check<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4-p84-1\">→ After: Ch.3: the logic twin and the used ally<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4-p84-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"","w":"horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune ch 3  the logic twin and the used ally named as the model ichinose s logic is measured against  ichinose s logic was similar to horikita s  but the crucial difference was that ichinose could bring people together  he wants opinions from people other than hirata and horikita on the strange test  on the island he d indirectly used sakura while also using horikita   and manipulated yamauchi through sakura s email","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4-p84-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3: the logic twin and the used ally<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.84, p.97, p.101<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named as the model Ichinose’s logic is measured against.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Ichinose’s logic was similar to Horikita’s, but the crucial difference was that Ichinose could bring people together.<span class=\"pg\">p.84<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> He wants opinions from people other than Hirata and Horikita on the strange test.<span class=\"pg\">p.97<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> On the island he’d indirectly used Sakura while also using Horikita — and manipulated Yamauchi through Sakura’s email.<span class=\"pg\">p.101<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4-p63-1\">← Before: Ch.3 §3.0: the Blue Ocean briefing<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4-p115-1\">→ After: Ch.3: the confused-call message<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4-p115-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune ch 3  the confused call message one message in the cabin chaos after kouenji ends the monkey group   i m sorry  things seem really confusing right now  i m going to give you a call   horikita messaged me   printed as her text  reaches him in the cabin minutes after the traitor notice  the call itself is not printed on these pages  the recipient of the promise to call","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4-p115-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3: the confused-call message<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.115<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">One message in the cabin chaos after Kouenji ends the Monkey group.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“I’m sorry. Things seem really confusing right now. I’m going to give you a call.” (Horikita messaged me — printed as her text)<span class=\"pg\">p.115<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> Reaches him in the cabin minutes after the traitor notice; the call itself is not printed on these pages.<span class=\"pg\">p.115<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> The recipient of the promise to call.<span class=\"pg\">p.115<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4-p84-1\">← Before: Ch.3: the logic twin and the used ally<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4-p116-1\">→ After: Ch.3: one of the two assets<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4-p116-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"","w":"horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune ch 3  one of the two assets named with sakura as the pair ayanokoji might still be able to use  he might still be able to use horikita and sakura   right now he needs more eyes and ears on his side","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4-p116-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3: one of the two assets<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.116<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named with Sakura as the pair Ayanokōji might still be able to use.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> He might still be able to use Horikita and Sakura — right now he needs more eyes and ears on his side.<span class=\"pg\">p.116<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4-p115-1\">← Before: Ch.3: the confused-call message<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4-p125-1\">→ After: Ch.4 §4.0: the Karuizawa brief and the planted phone<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4-p125-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"action spoken","w":"kouenji-rokusuke karuizawa-kei ryuuen-kakeru horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune ch 4  4 0  the karuizawa brief and the planted phone she meets ayanokoji face to face about kouenji s traitor exit  then argues karuizawa s worth while ryuuen s recording phone sits under his chair   you re joking  right   are you an idiot  why didn t you stop him  wasn t that your responsibility as his roommate  she asked   when i see him next time  i ll reprimand him myself  i ll make him beg for mercy   you already know that s pointless  right  he won t listen  he ll just confuse you and waste your time  it ll be a headache  for the time being  we should concentrate on our own groups  blames ayanokoji as kouenji s roommate  accepts the roommate can t stop him answer   you want to talk to me about karuizawa   i turned her down  though  you know that  i have no interest in karuizawa san  if you want information on her  why not talk to hirata kun  if he s helping you  you ll be able to contact her easily   do you think she s the vip  is that what you re worried about  horikita asked   well  isn t that none of your business  besides  her behavior isn t logical  i think it s a waste of time  she countered   write them off  what are you talking about   she has strong points  i can t really imagine any  isn t she just flawed  refuses the lunch invite history  calls her illogical  then listens to the outer inner self lecture and concedes time together may help   so karuizawa has some secret self   i m still not entirely convinced  however  i imagine you ll learn more about her by spending time together  she said   so  what are karuizawa san s good points  horikita asked   okay  let s say for the sake of argument that you re right  and she has that ability  what do you intend to do  are you thinking of making her your ally  too  asked horikita  the shade meeting  refuses to share plans  calls his no support claim out  snaps at the phone seizure idea  then works the planted phone cue with ayanokoji   it seems like you have an awful lot of free time  not that i care  but there s nothing for you here  said horikita   whatever my plans may be  i ve no intention of telling you  said horikita   that s an interesting thing to say  are you saying that you know who the vip is   no  i wouldn t  you don t have any support like ichinose san and katsuragi kun do  you only have enemies  i can t imagine you have reliable information  she countered   i see  anyone could think of that  but are they going to answer honestly  if the school has a rule that guarantees your anonymity  all they need to do is lie and gain 500 000 points  right  horikita countered   where someone can t lie   are you insane  the school doesn t allow that  if you were discovered  you d be expelled  snapped horikita   yes  but you haven t got the answer yet  if you had  you would ve sent an email to the school immediately  answered horikita   you don t know when someone else is going to figure it out  you shouldn t be so laid back  horikita snapped   ryuuen kun  while you re here  i d like to ask you something  the test ended for the monkey group yesterday  what do you think about that  she asked  probes ryuuen on the monkey group early end  he waves it off as small fry   i don t know how much of what he said is true  she said  spots the silent recording phone under ryuuen s chair  texts ayanokoji the caution line  if that phone is his  we probably shouldn t say anything careless   chat message  p 130   i have to wonder  i can t say i m 100  sure  but there s a possibility  i don t think we can keep up this test much longer  though   i ve got a lot of work for you to do  i need you to find the group s vip as soon as possible  said horikita   i won t expect too much from you  i just want information about the rabbit group  reads ryuuen s phone plant as reason to keep talking carefully  still assigns ayanokoji the rabbit vip hunt as cover","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4-p125-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.4 §4.0: the Karuizawa brief and the planted phone<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.125–133<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">She meets Ayanokōji face-to-face about Kouenji’s traitor exit, then argues Karuizawa’s worth while Ryuuen’s recording phone sits under his chair.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"kouenji-rokusuke.html\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/a> · <a href=\"karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a> · <a href=\"ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“You’re joking, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.125<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Are you an idiot? Why didn’t you stop him? Wasn’t that your responsibility as his roommate?” she asked.<span class=\"pg\">p.125<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“When I see him next time, I’ll reprimand him myself. I’ll make him beg for mercy.”<span class=\"pg\">p.125<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>32 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You already know that’s pointless, right? He won’t listen. He’ll just confuse you and waste your time. It’ll be a headache. For the time being, we should concentrate on our own groups.”<span class=\"pg\">p.125<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/b> Blames Ayanokōji as Kouenji’s roommate; accepts the roommate-can’t-stop-him answer.<span class=\"pg\">p.125<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You want to talk to me about Karuizawa?”<span class=\"pg\">p.126<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I turned her down, though. You know that. I have no interest in Karuizawa-san. If you want information on her, why not talk to Hirata-kun? If he’s helping you, you’ll be able to contact her easily.”<span class=\"pg\">p.126<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Do you think she’s the VIP? Is that what you’re worried about?” Horikita asked.<span class=\"pg\">p.126<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, isn’t that none of your business? Besides, her behavior isn’t logical. I think it’s a waste of time,” she countered.<span class=\"pg\">p.126<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Write them off? What are you talking about?”<span class=\"pg\">p.126<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “She has strong points? I can’t really imagine any. Isn’t she just flawed?”<span class=\"pg\">p.126<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> Refuses the lunch invite history, calls her illogical, then listens to the outer/inner-self lecture and concedes time-together may help.<span class=\"pg\">p.126-127<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “So Karuizawa has some secret self?”<span class=\"pg\">p.127<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m still not entirely convinced. However, I imagine you’ll learn more about her by spending time together,” she said.<span class=\"pg\">p.127<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “So, what are Karuizawa-san’s good points?” Horikita asked.<span class=\"pg\">p.127<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Okay. Let’s say for the sake of argument that you’re right, and she has that ability. What do you intend to do? Are you thinking of making her your ally, too?” asked Horikita.<span class=\"pg\">p.127<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> The shade meeting: refuses to share plans, calls his no-support claim out, snaps at the phone-seizure idea, then works the planted-phone cue with Ayanokōji.<span class=\"pg\">p.128-131<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It seems like you have an awful lot of free time. Not that I care, but there’s nothing for you here,” said Horikita.<span class=\"pg\">p.128<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Whatever my plans may be, I’ve no intention of telling you,” said Horikita.<span class=\"pg\">p.128<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s an interesting thing to say. Are you saying that you know who the VIP is?”<span class=\"pg\">p.128<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “No, I wouldn’t. You don’t have any support like Ichinose-san and Katsuragi-kun do. You only have enemies. I can’t imagine you have reliable information,” she countered.<span class=\"pg\">p.128<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I see. Anyone could think of that. But are they going to answer honestly? If the school has a rule that guarantees your anonymity, all they need to do is lie and gain 500,000 points, right?” Horikita countered.<span class=\"pg\">p.129<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Where someone can’t lie?”<span class=\"pg\">p.129<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Are you insane? The school doesn’t allow that. If you were discovered, you’d be expelled,” snapped Horikita.<span class=\"pg\">p.129<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yes. But you haven’t got the answer yet. If you had, you would’ve sent an email to the school immediately,” answered Horikita.<span class=\"pg\">p.129<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You don’t know when someone else is going to figure it out. You shouldn’t be so laid-back,” Horikita snapped.<span class=\"pg\">p.130<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ryuuen-kun. While you’re here, I’d like to ask you something. The test ended for the Monkey group yesterday. What do you think about that?” she asked.<span class=\"pg\">p.130<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/b> Probes Ryuuen on the Monkey-group early end; he waves it off as small fry.<span class=\"pg\">p.130<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I don’t know how much of what he said is true,” she said.<span class=\"pg\">p.130<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Spots the silent recording phone under Ryuuen’s chair; texts Ayanokōji the caution line.<span class=\"pg\">p.130<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> If that phone is his, we probably shouldn’t say anything careless. (chat message, p.130)<span class=\"pg\">p.130<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I have to wonder. I can’t say I’m 100% sure. But…there’s a possibility. I don’t think we can keep up this test much longer, though.”<span class=\"pg\">p.130<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’ve got a lot of work for you to do. I need you to find the group’s VIP as soon as possible,” said Horikita.<span class=\"pg\">p.131<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I won’t expect too much from you. I just want information about the Rabbit group.”<span class=\"pg\">p.131<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Reads Ryuuen’s phone plant as reason to keep talking carefully; still assigns Ayanokōji the Rabbit VIP hunt as cover.<span class=\"pg\">p.130-131<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4-p116-1\">← Before: Ch.3: one of the two assets<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4-p139-1\">→ After: Ch.4: the three-way deadlock<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4-p139-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"","w":"horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune ch 4  the three way deadlock named in the corridor wait   she s in the dragon group with katsuragi while ichinose wants in  ayanokoji  no  that s not it   horikita s in the same group as katsuragi  ichinose takes the news and waves hamaguchi off  he sends horikita an instant message he doesn t think she reads  ichinose calls her a star player in the class d line up  ichinose wants to wait with him for horikita san   her chances to speak with her are limited since katsuragi brushed her off  the wait ends  inside  horikita  kanzaki  and ryuuen sit slightly apart   a three way deadlock  ryuuen needles ayanokouji   first suzune  now ichinose   while horikita dismisses ryuuen s proposal as a waste of time  having already heard it  ryuuen reports suzune and kanzaki disagree with his crush class a plan  and that he told suzune he already knows the class c vip identities  ichinose  horikita san rejected ryuuen s proposal  so the plan is off to a bad start   ryuuen adds that even if suzune wanted to agree  a reason stops her  horikita says she might be overstepping but doubts he can pull it off  her speaking up surprises ayanokoji  who meant to observe silently  horikita  this will be tough  he s gunning for us   ichinose counters that ryuuen is naturally wary of class a and thinks b will side with d  ichinose asks horikita san and ayanokouji kun whether the test will create trust between classes  horikita answers they don t know how to make a d b alliance  ichinose  i understand what horikita san said earlier  but i think there s still room for cooperation  the narration  breaking the truce with horikita and exploiting class d would be nonsensical  adopting a strategy without the risk of exposure would fracture the truce with horikita   the safer path is the show","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4-p139-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.4: the three-way deadlock<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.139–153<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named in the corridor wait — she’s in the Dragon group with Katsuragi while Ichinose wants in.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>13 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Ayanokōji: no, that’s not it — Horikita’s in the same group as Katsuragi; Ichinose takes the news and waves Hamaguchi off.<span class=\"pg\">p.139<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> He sends Horikita an instant message he doesn’t think she reads; Ichinose calls her a star player in the Class D line-up.<span class=\"pg\">p.140<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Ichinose wants to wait with him for Horikita-san — her chances to speak with her are limited since Katsuragi brushed her off.<span class=\"pg\">p.143<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The wait ends: inside, Horikita, Kanzaki, and Ryuuen sit slightly apart — a three-way deadlock.<span class=\"pg\">p.144<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Ryuuen needles Ayanokouji — first Suzune, now Ichinose — while Horikita dismisses Ryuuen’s proposal as a waste of time, having already heard it.<span class=\"pg\">p.145<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Ryuuen reports Suzune and Kanzaki disagree with his crush-Class-A plan, and that he told Suzune he already knows the Class C VIP identities.<span class=\"pg\">p.146<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Ichinose: Horikita-san rejected Ryuuen’s proposal, so the plan is off to a bad start — Ryuuen adds that even if Suzune wanted to agree, a reason stops her.<span class=\"pg\">p.147<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Horikita says she might be overstepping but doubts he can pull it off; her speaking up surprises Ayanokōji, who meant to observe silently.<span class=\"pg\">p.148<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Horikita: this will be tough, he’s gunning for us — Ichinose counters that Ryuuen is naturally wary of Class A and thinks B will side with D.<span class=\"pg\">p.149<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Ichinose asks Horikita-san and Ayanokouji-kun whether the test will create trust between classes; Horikita answers they don’t know how to make a D–B alliance.<span class=\"pg\">p.150<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Ichinose: I understand what Horikita-san said earlier, but I think there’s still room for cooperation.<span class=\"pg\">p.151<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The narration: breaking the truce with Horikita and exploiting Class D would be nonsensical.<span class=\"pg\">p.152<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Adopting a strategy without the risk of exposure would fracture the truce with Horikita — the safer path is the show.<span class=\"pg\">p.153<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4-p125-1\">← Before: Ch.4 §4.0: the Karuizawa brief and the planted phone<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4-p170-1\">→ After: Ch.4: the bridge and the orders<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4-p170-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"","w":"horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune ch 4  the bridge and the orders named in the midnight vending machine talk as the reason hirata wanted the meeting  ayanokoji cites hirata s own wish to act as a bridge between horikita and the rest of the class  saying it is about that  hirata asks whether horikita san told him to talk to him  ayanokoji continues  once he heard about what happened with karuizawa  horikita told him to keep an eye on hirata too and to follow him   but hirata had said he wanted to act as a bridge for her  the read of hirata s game  he was using karuizawa to extract information as a tribute to horikita  ayanokoji s cover  he heard about it from horikita   she said karuizawa had her reasons for clinging to hirata and to others   and that he is only following her orders  on horikita s advice and detailed reports  hirata  even if ayanokouji is just following horikita san s orders  he is still the one talking to him   it isn t as though she gave him a list of prepared responses  hirata asks whether he and horikita san will keep this confidential  the answer is that if he promises not to get involved  horikita will stay silent  on karuizawa  her social pull makes her an even more valuable ally than horikita","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4-p170-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.4: the bridge and the orders<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.170–171, p.175, p.178–179, p.182, p.202<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named in the midnight vending-machine talk as the reason Hirata wanted the meeting.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>7 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Ayanokōji cites Hirata’s own wish to act as a bridge between Horikita and the rest of the class, saying it is about that; Hirata asks whether Horikita-san told him to talk to him.<span class=\"pg\">p.170<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Ayanokōji continues: once he heard about what happened with Karuizawa, Horikita told him to keep an eye on Hirata too and to follow him — but Hirata had said he wanted to act as a bridge for her.<span class=\"pg\">p.171<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The read of Hirata’s game: he was using Karuizawa to extract information as a tribute to Horikita.<span class=\"pg\">p.175<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Ayanokōji’s cover: he heard about it from Horikita — she said Karuizawa had her reasons for clinging to Hirata and to others — and that he is only following her orders, on Horikita’s advice and detailed reports.<span class=\"pg\">p.178<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Hirata: even if Ayanokouji is just following Horikita-san’s orders, he is still the one talking to him — it isn’t as though she gave him a list of prepared responses.<span class=\"pg\">p.179<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Hirata asks whether he and Horikita-san will keep this confidential; the answer is that if he promises not to get involved, Horikita will stay silent.<span class=\"pg\">p.182<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> On Karuizawa: her social pull makes her an even more valuable ally than Horikita.<span class=\"pg\">p.202<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4-p139-1\">← Before: Ch.4: the three-way deadlock<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4-p206-1\">→ After: Ch.5: the shared powerlessness<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4-p206-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"","w":"horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune ch 5  the shared powerlessness named in the post island humbling that hit everyone  in the two summer tests everyone had experienced the bitter sense of their own powerlessness  even horikita","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4-p206-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.5: the shared powerlessness<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.206<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named in the post-island humbling that hit everyone.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> In the two summer tests everyone had experienced the bitter sense of their own powerlessness, even Horikita.<span class=\"pg\">p.206<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4-p170-1\">← Before: Ch.4: the bridge and the orders<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4-p207-1\">→ After: Ch.5 §5.1: the night meet<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4-p207-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka hirata-yousuke ryuuen-kakeru horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune ch 5  5 1  the night meet last pre final meeting with ayanokoji in person  claims the win flatly  refuses detail on listener risk  and takes the hirata recruitment plan with gritted teeth   i ll win  she replied flatly   i m not sure who might be listening to us right now  so i won t go into detail  i ll just ask that you believe in me  everything will be fine  confidence despite the odds   ayanokoji already knows kushida is dragon vip and reads this as solid victory  person to person because chat leaves traces   make whatever moves you like  snaps at free shadow operation   did you want to consult with me  she asked   so what did you want to talk about  i thought we both agreed to avoid unnecessary contact   judging from how you phrased that  i m guessing you can do something about it   i don t particularly want that  she said   i don t really like how freely you re operating in the shadows  she answered   well  i suppose so  she sighed   okay  i really don t like this  i don t want you to just go ahead and recruit people as you see fit  she snapped   i have a general idea of what you re thinking  but  well  fine  at any rate  let s meet back here after the test is over  the cooperation she does not want    i don t particularly want that    ayanokoji will handle him alone   i wonder how many traitors will come forward in this test  said horikita   yes  i think so  too  horikita briefly averted her eyes  the sort of unconscious gesture people made when they were worried about something   nothing  it s just  well  something about this test doesn t make sense  but there shouldn t be any mistakes  i definitely shouldn t lose  she replied  anxiety finally leaking   the averted eyes  then the  doesn t make sense  line  he stays quiet because kind words would be refused  his pursuit is the fear she won t name under listener risk","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4-p207-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.5 §5.1: the night meet<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.207–209<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Last pre-final meeting with Ayanokóji in person; claims the win flatly, refuses detail on listener risk, and takes the Hirata/recruitment plan with gritted teeth.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> · <a href=\"ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“I’ll win,” she replied flatly.<span class=\"pg\">p.207<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I’m not sure who might be listening to us right now, so I won’t go into detail. I’ll just ask that you believe in me. Everything will be fine.”<span class=\"pg\">p.207<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Did you want to consult with me?” she asked.<span class=\"pg\">p.207<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>15 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Confidence despite the odds — Ayanokōji already knows Kushida is Dragon VIP and reads this as solid victory.<span class=\"pg\">p.207<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Person-to-person because chat leaves traces; “Make whatever moves you like”; snaps at free shadow operation.<span class=\"pg\">p.207-209<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “So what did you want to talk about? I thought we both agreed to avoid unnecessary contact.”<span class=\"pg\">p.207<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Judging from how you phrased that, I’m guessing you can do something about it?”<span class=\"pg\">p.207<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I don’t particularly want that,” she said.<span class=\"pg\">p.208<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I don’t really like how freely you’re operating in the shadows,” she answered.<span class=\"pg\">p.208<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, I suppose so,” she sighed.<span class=\"pg\">p.208<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Okay, I really don’t like this. I don’t want you to just go ahead and recruit people as you see fit,” she snapped.<span class=\"pg\">p.208<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I have a general idea of what you’re thinking, but… Well, fine. At any rate, let’s meet back here after the test is over.”<span class=\"pg\">p.208<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> The cooperation she does not want — “I don’t particularly want that” — Ayanokōji will handle him alone.<span class=\"pg\">p.208<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I wonder how many traitors will come forward in this test,” said Horikita.<span class=\"pg\">p.208<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yes, I think so, too.” Horikita briefly averted her eyes, the sort of unconscious gesture people made when they were worried about something.<span class=\"pg\">p.208<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Nothing. It’s just, well… Something about this test doesn’t make sense. But there shouldn’t be any mistakes. I definitely shouldn’t lose,” she replied.<span class=\"pg\">p.209<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Anxiety finally leaking — the averted eyes, then the “doesn’t make sense” line; he stays quiet because kind words would be refused.<span class=\"pg\">p.208-209<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> His pursuit is the fear she won’t name under listener risk.<span class=\"pg\">p.207<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4-p206-1\">← Before: Ch.5: the shared powerlessness<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4-p215-1\">→ After: Ch.5: the points, the discretion, the phone swap<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4-p215-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"","w":"horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune ch 5  the points  the discretion  the phone swap named in the class d finance talk   her effort against undeposited points  class d s financial situation is especially awful  even though horikita s trying her hardest  the island test points have yet to be deposited  and they might lose them in this test  the discretion check  even if the information were shared with horikita san  he wouldn t go blabbing to everyone after seeing her phone  the swap camouflage  if kushida and horikita switched phones  a spy would suspect horikita was the vip   and a traitor submitting her name would then be wrong","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4-p215-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.5: the points, the discretion, the phone swap<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.215–217<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named in the Class D finance talk — her effort against undeposited points.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Class D’s financial situation is especially awful: even though Horikita’s trying her hardest, the island-test points have yet to be deposited, and they might lose them in this test.<span class=\"pg\">p.215<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The discretion check: even if the information were shared with Horikita-san, he wouldn’t go blabbing to everyone after seeing her phone.<span class=\"pg\">p.216<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The swap camouflage: if Kushida and Horikita switched phones, a spy would suspect Horikita was the VIP — and a traitor submitting her name would then be wrong.<span class=\"pg\">p.217<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4-p207-1\">← Before: Ch.5 §5.1: the night meet<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4-p230-1\">→ After: Ch.5 §5.2–5.3: the plan’s author, then the café<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4-p230-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"spoken","w":"ichinose-honami sudou-ken yamauchi-haruki karuizawa-kei kouenji-rokusuke ryuuen-kakeru kushida-kikyou ayanokouji-kiyotaka horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune ch 5  5 2 5 3  the plan s author  then the cafe gets the credit line from ichinose    her plan was a huge success    then runs the cafe debrief with hirata  absorbs ryuuen s kushida reveal and the class c blowout  and talks ayanokoji out of his premonition  the relayed verdict on the phone swap  ayanokoji is told to say it was her plan   ahh  when i see you people  i can t help but sigh  muttered horikita   ignore him  think of him as a ghost that attached itself to my back  horikita said flatly  shuts him down repeatedly    you re in the way  get lost   sudou kun  be quiet    then lets him stay as chair grabbing baggage   you re in the way  get lost  she spat   in that case  do you believe you ll end up with good results   you re in the way  horikita grumbled   minami kun was the horse group vip  right  asked horikita   did one of us send an email for the other groups  asked horikita   ah  he s probably okay  yamauchi kun was in the rooster group  it seems he did try sending an email but agonized over it for too long  the test ended before he could actually send it  said horikita  the rooster who froze on the send button   her prediction he would have guessed wrong  accepts the girls side report flatly   no social pull of her own  so she takes what controllers say   this exam was all about testing our thinking  it s not like every single question would have an answer  said horikita   what i m worried about is that those four emails came in at almost the exact same time  the school said we had a timeframe of thirty minutes at the end of the test to betray someone  but all the emails came within one to two seconds of each other  she said  the automated timing deduction with hirata   four simultaneous betrayals   one class showing off   when kouenji kun sent the email to betray his group  the school responded without delay  if you think about how fast it was  it must have been automated  horikita began  his earlier betrayal email is the calibration point for the school s speed   yeah  and there s only one person i can imagine who d do such a thing  said horikita  the sixth guest she expected  the kushida reveal hits her confidence  the threat leaves her staring at the results without a comeback   yes  i chose this space because even an idiot like you would be able to find it quite easily  you should be grateful  answered horikita   i disliked your persistent harassment  i was talking to them about it  said horikita flatly   sudou kun  be quiet  horikita snapped   more or less  you look rather relaxed  horikita said   i m quite glad to hear that  i look forward to the results  she replied with confidence   i m sorry  but i m hearing the irritating whine of a loser  the test has already ended  and no one in the dragon group has turned traitor  that can only mean one thing  she answered  her certainty that ryuuen never got it   broken when he says the name   all right  tell me then  who is the dragon group vip  asked horikita   you re joking  right  if that s true  you would have turned traitor and sent an email  but the test didn t end like that  that must mean you realized that fact after the exam had ended  there s no other way  am i wrong  asked horikita   me  she asked  dumbfounded   stop with the jokes   that s  i m sure you could ve just heard it from someone else  horikita stammered   what  what did you do  asked horikita  class c  150 cl and  5 5 million pr    class c came out on top  stunned at the table   class c came out on top  muttered horikita  his trouble warning  her calm rebuttal that ryuuen s win does not guarantee future danger   by trouble  you mean ryuuen kun  it s true he did very well in this test  but there s no guarantee he ll be dangerous in the future  your group won their test  after all  didn t they  she asked  the composed front after the humiliation   she keeps him from spiraling into the premonition","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4-p230-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.5 §5.2–5.3: the plan’s author, then the café<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.230–243<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Gets the credit line from Ichinose — “her plan was a huge success” — then runs the café debrief with Hirata, absorbs Ryuuen’s Kushida reveal and the Class C blowout, and talks Ayanokōji out of his premonition.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a> · <a href=\"sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a> · <a href=\"yamauchi-haruki.html\">Yamauchi Haruki<\/a> · <a href=\"karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a> · <a href=\"kouenji-rokusuke.html\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/a> · <a href=\"ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> <span class=\"n\">+2 more<\/span><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Ahh. When I see you people, I can’t help but sigh,” muttered Horikita.<span class=\"pg\">p.235<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Ignore him. Think of him as a ghost that attached itself to my back,” Horikita said flatly.<span class=\"pg\">p.235<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“You’re in the way. Get lost,” she spat.<span class=\"pg\">p.235<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>34 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> The relayed verdict on the phone swap; Ayanokōji is told to say it was her plan.<span class=\"pg\">p.230<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> Shuts him down repeatedly — “You’re in the way. Get lost,” “Sudou-kun, be quiet” — then lets him stay as chair-grabbing baggage.<span class=\"pg\">p.235-241<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “In that case, do you believe you’ll end up with good results?”<span class=\"pg\">p.235<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You’re in the way,” Horikita grumbled.<span class=\"pg\">p.235<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Minami-kun was the Horse group VIP, right?” asked Horikita.<span class=\"pg\">p.236<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Did one of us send an email for the other groups?” asked Horikita.<span class=\"pg\">p.236<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ah, he’s probably okay. Yamauchi-kun was in the Rooster group. It seems he did try sending an email but agonized over it for too long. The test ended before he could actually send it,” said Horikita.<span class=\"pg\">p.236<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yamauchi Haruki<\/b> The Rooster who froze on the send button — her prediction he would have guessed wrong.<span class=\"pg\">p.236<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> Accepts the girls-side report flatly — no social pull of her own, so she takes what controllers say.<span class=\"pg\">p.236<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “This exam was all about testing our thinking. It’s not like every single question would have an answer,” said Horikita.<span class=\"pg\">p.237<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What I’m worried about is that those four emails came in at almost the exact same time. The school said we had a timeframe of thirty minutes at the end of the test to betray someone, but all the emails came within one to two seconds of each other,” she said.<span class=\"pg\">p.237<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> The automated-timing deduction with Hirata — four simultaneous betrayals = one class showing off.<span class=\"pg\">p.237<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “When Kouenji-kun sent the email to betray his group, the school responded without delay. If you think about how fast it was, it must have been automated,” Horikita began.<span class=\"pg\">p.237<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/b> His earlier betrayal email is the calibration point for the school’s speed.<span class=\"pg\">p.237<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yeah. And there’s only one person I can imagine who’d do such a thing.” said Horikita.<span class=\"pg\">p.237<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> The sixth guest she expected; the Kushida reveal hits her confidence; the threat leaves her staring at the results without a comeback.<span class=\"pg\">p.237-241<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yes. I chose this space because even an idiot like you would be able to find it quite easily. You should be grateful,” answered Horikita.<span class=\"pg\">p.238<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I disliked your persistent harassment. I was talking to them about it,” said Horikita flatly.<span class=\"pg\">p.238<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Sudou-kun, be quiet,” Horikita snapped.<span class=\"pg\">p.238<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “More or less. You look rather relaxed,” Horikita said.<span class=\"pg\">p.238<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m quite glad to hear that. I look forward to the results,” she replied with confidence.<span class=\"pg\">p.238<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m sorry, but I’m hearing the irritating whine of a loser. The test has already ended, and no one in the Dragon group has turned traitor. That can only mean one thing,” she answered.<span class=\"pg\">p.239<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> Her certainty that Ryuuen never got it — broken when he says the name.<span class=\"pg\">p.239<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “All right, tell me then. Who is the Dragon group VIP?” asked Horikita.<span class=\"pg\">p.239<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You’re joking, right? If that’s true, you would have turned traitor and sent an email. But the test didn’t end like that. That must mean you realized that fact after the exam had ended. There’s no other way. Am I wrong?” asked Horikita.<span class=\"pg\">p.239<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Me?” she asked, dumbfounded.<span class=\"pg\">p.240<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Stop with the jokes!”<span class=\"pg\">p.240<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s… I’m sure you could’ve just heard it from someone else,” Horikita stammered.<span class=\"pg\">p.240<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What? What did you do?” asked Horikita.<span class=\"pg\">p.240<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> Class C +150 cl and +5.5 Million pr — “Class C…came out on top,” stunned at the table.<span class=\"pg\">p.241<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Class C…came out on top,” muttered Horikita.<span class=\"pg\">p.241<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> His trouble-warning; her calm rebuttal that Ryuuen’s win does not guarantee future danger.<span class=\"pg\">p.243<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “By trouble, you mean Ryuuen-kun? It’s true he did very well in this test, but there’s no guarantee he’ll be dangerous in the future. Your group won their test, after all. Didn’t they?” she asked.<span class=\"pg\">p.243<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The composed front after the humiliation — she keeps him from spiraling into the premonition.<span class=\"pg\">p.243<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4-p215-1\">← Before: Ch.5: the points, the discretion, the phone swap<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4_5-p13-1","v":"y1v4.5","y":1,"o":5,"k":"","w":"horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune ch 2  passing mentions her name threads the fortune teller plans from the first phone call onward  sudou insists that ayanokoji invite suzune out as well  since his own chances with her would be slim  his insistence on inviting her is what gives the plan its shape  ibuki s questions and the label of horikita whisperer keep her the real subject of the talk  the queue conversation circles her from the uniformed girl s mission to who will finally invite her  ibuki is compared to her as another classmate who keeps to herself  a classmate like her is what would let ayanokoji coast by","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4_5-p13-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2: passing mentions<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4.5 · p.13, 19–21, 24, 31<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Her name threads the fortune-teller plans from the first phone call onward.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Sudou insists that Ayanokōji invite Suzune out as well, since his own chances with her would be slim.<span class=\"pg\">p.13<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> His insistence on inviting her is what gives the plan its shape.<span class=\"pg\">p.19<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Ibuki&#x27;s questions and the label of Horikita whisperer keep her the real subject of the talk.<span class=\"pg\">p.20<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The queue conversation circles her from the uniformed girl&#x27;s mission to who will finally invite her.<span class=\"pg\">p.21<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Ibuki is compared to her as another classmate who keeps to herself.<span class=\"pg\">p.24<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> A classmate like her is what would let Ayanokōji coast by.<span class=\"pg\">p.31<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4_5-p14-1\">→ After: Ch.2: the fortune-telling call<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4_5-p14-1","v":"y1v4.5","y":1,"o":5,"k":"action spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune ch 2  the fortune telling call ayanokoji calls out of nowhere to ask whether she likes fortune telling  she answers immediately and makes him pay for the answer   you open conversations in the strangest way  she answered  never had her fortune told   only the morning horoscopes   yet  it would be a lie to say i dislike fortune telling   however  the big difference between fortune tellers and psychics is that fortune tellers give readings based on a massive amount of past data  the rational account of the booth  fortune tellers interpret patterns to understand people   observation  not power   you re rather cheeky  but i guess you do know some things  she credits him with knowing the technique and tells him he should go   i refuse  she answered   sorry  but i ll pass  turns down the outing on the crowds   she will not enter a place with so many excited students","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4_5-p14-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2: the fortune-telling call<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4.5 · p.14–17<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Ayanokōji calls out of nowhere to ask whether she likes fortune-telling; she answers immediately and makes him pay for the answer.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“You open conversations in the strangest way,” she answered.<span class=\"pg\">p.15<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“However, the big difference between fortune-tellers and psychics is that fortune-tellers give readings based on a massive amount of past data.”<span class=\"pg\">p.16<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“You’re rather cheeky, but I guess you do know some things.”<span class=\"pg\">p.16<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Never had her fortune told — only the morning horoscopes — yet “it would be a lie to say I dislike fortune-telling.”<span class=\"pg\">p.15<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The rational account of the booth: fortune-tellers interpret patterns to understand people — observation, not power.<span class=\"pg\">p.16<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> She credits him with knowing the technique and tells him he should go.<span class=\"pg\">p.16<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I refuse,” she answered.<span class=\"pg\">p.17<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Sorry, but I’ll pass.”<span class=\"pg\">p.17<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Turns down the outing on the crowds — she will not enter a place with so many excited students.<span class=\"pg\">p.17<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4_5-p13-1\">← Before: Ch.2: passing mentions<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4_5-p23-1\">→ After: Ch.2: a passing mention in Ibuki’s question<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4_5-p23-1","v":"y1v4.5","y":1,"o":5,"k":"","w":"horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune ch 2  a passing mention in ibuki s question named in ibuki s memory of the island test   the class d leader she identified  the narration confirms it   she discovered that horikita was the leader  and she hadn t been wrong","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4_5-p23-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2: a passing mention in Ibuki’s question<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4.5 · p.23<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named in Ibuki’s memory of the island test — the Class D leader she identified.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The narration confirms it: “She discovered that Horikita was the leader, and she hadn’t been wrong.”<span class=\"pg\">p.23<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4_5-p14-1\">← Before: Ch.2: the fortune-telling call<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4_5-p28-1\">→ After: Ch.2: a passing mention in the partner list<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4_5-p28-1","v":"y1v4.5","y":1,"o":5,"k":"","w":"horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune ch 2  a passing mention in the partner list named once as the invite he does not even attempt  expected to decline before being asked   horikita would just turn me down if i asked","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4_5-p28-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2: a passing mention in the partner list<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4.5 · p.28<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named once as the invite he does not even attempt.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Expected to decline before being asked: “Horikita would just turn me down if I asked.”<span class=\"pg\">p.28<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4_5-p23-1\">← Before: Ch.2: a passing mention in Ibuki’s question<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4_5-p30-1\">→ After: Ch.2: a passing mention in the pair proposal<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4_5-p30-1","v":"y1v4.5","y":1,"o":5,"k":"","w":"horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune ch 2  a passing mention in the pair proposal named as the friend ayanokoji invokes to dismiss ibuki s worry about the island grudge  his line   even if horikita were here  she s only a friend    the grudge talk stops there","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4_5-p30-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2: a passing mention in the pair proposal<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4.5 · p.30<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named as the friend Ayanokōji invokes to dismiss Ibuki’s worry about the island grudge.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> His line: “Even if Horikita were here, she’s only a friend.” — the grudge talk stops there.<span class=\"pg\">p.30<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4_5-p28-1\">← Before: Ch.2: a passing mention in the partner list<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4_5-p41-1\">→ After: Ch.2: passing mentions in the elevator<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4_5-p41-1","v":"y1v4.5","y":1,"o":5,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune ch 2  passing mentions in the elevator named as the rescue call ibuki will not allow  and again as the rival ibuki measures herself against   maybe horikita  ibuki s veto   as long as it s not horikita  the combat memory   i heard you kept up with horikita    ayanokoji grants he could not defeat her in combat","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4_5-p41-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2: passing mentions in the elevator<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4.5 · p.41, 43<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named as the rescue call Ibuki will not allow, and again as the rival Ibuki measures herself against.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “Maybe Horikita?”<span class=\"pg\">p.41<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Ibuki’s veto: “As long as it’s not Horikita.”<span class=\"pg\">p.41<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The combat memory: “I heard you kept up with Horikita.” — Ayanokōji grants he could not defeat her in combat.<span class=\"pg\">p.43<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4_5-p30-1\">← Before: Ch.2: a passing mention in the pair proposal<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4_5-p51-1\">→ After: Ch.3: passing mentions<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4_5-p51-1","v":"y1v4.5","y":1,"o":5,"k":"spoken","w":"sudou-ken kushida-kikyou horikita-manabu katsuragi-kouhei horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune ch 3  passing mentions named in passing as half of the  horikita and kushida  schedules ak refuses to manage  otherwise absent from the chapter s scenes  the room speculates katsuragi s gift could be for her  sudou demands her birthday and gets february 15 from kushida   it s on february 15  her brother calls her a failure who belongs in class d  ak s cover story for the island test is rejected   she s a failure who belongs in class d  katsuragi asks if ak is close with her  ak attributes it to the seating partnership","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4_5-p51-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3: passing mentions<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4.5 · p.51, 62–63, 71, 77–78<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named in passing as half of the “Horikita and Kushida” schedules AK refuses to manage; otherwise absent from the chapter&#x27;s scenes.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a> · <a href=\"kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-manabu.html\">Horikita Manabu<\/a> · <a href=\"katsuragi-kouhei.html\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> “It’s on February 15.”<span class=\"pg\">p.63<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Manabu<\/b> “She’s a failure who belongs in Class D.”<span class=\"pg\">p.71<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> The room speculates Katsuragi&#x27;s gift could be for her; Sudou demands her birthday and gets February 15 from Kushida.<span class=\"pg\">p.62–63<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Manabu<\/b> Her brother calls her a failure who belongs in Class D; AK&#x27;s cover story for the island test is rejected.<span class=\"pg\">p.71<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> Katsuragi asks if AK is close with her; AK attributes it to the seating partnership.<span class=\"pg\">p.77<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4_5-p41-1\">← Before: Ch.2: passing mentions in the elevator<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4_5-p60-1\">→ After: Ch.3: passing mentions<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4_5-p60-1","v":"y1v4.5","y":1,"o":5,"k":"","w":"horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune ch 3  passing mentions her absence and her secrets run through the birthday hunt s margins  the gathering in ayanokoji s room would have been perfect with her there  kushida s social network is said to extend even to horikita s birthday  ayanokoji leaves the group and approaches her directly  katsuragi works out that she is the student council president s little sister","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4_5-p60-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3: passing mentions<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4.5 · p.60, 65, 84, 90<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Her absence and her secrets run through the birthday hunt&#x27;s margins.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The gathering in Ayanokōji&#x27;s room would have been perfect with her there.<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Kushida&#x27;s social network is said to extend even to Horikita&#x27;s birthday.<span class=\"pg\">p.65<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Ayanokōji leaves the group and approaches her directly.<span class=\"pg\">p.84<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Katsuragi works out that she is the student council president&#x27;s little sister.<span class=\"pg\">p.90<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4_5-p51-1\">← Before: Ch.3: passing mentions<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4_5-p86-1\">→ After: Ch.3: the bench conversation<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4_5-p86-1","v":"y1v4.5","y":1,"o":5,"k":"spoken","w":"ryuuen-kakeru ayanokouji-kiyotaka chabashira-sae horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune ch 3  the bench conversation reading outside  she accosts the shopping four about the ryuuen loss  ak sits down and reframes the semester   even after we suffered so much at ryuuen kun s hands  the class c loss under ryuuen is what still gnaws at her   look  we just finished the first semester of our first year   although you can t see what s directly beneath your feet  you re always looking far ahead   i think that it s preferable for you to fall until you hit rock bottom  she calls out the island contradiction in his order to things advice  he admits it without explaining chabashira   you say there s an order to things  but if that s true  why did you go to all that trouble back on the island  she has no clue about his dealings with chabashira  that stays hidden   none of your business   i refuse  she refuses to join the shopping trip  ak had known all along it would be her answer","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4_5-p86-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3: the bench conversation<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4.5 · p.86–87<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Reading outside, she accosts the shopping four about the Ryuuen loss; AK sits down and reframes the semester.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"chabashira-sae.html\">Chabashira Sae<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Even after we suffered so much at Ryuuen-kun’s hands?”<span class=\"pg\">p.86<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “Look, we just finished the first semester of our first year.”<span class=\"pg\">p.86<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “Although you can’t see what’s directly beneath your feet, you’re always looking far ahead.”<span class=\"pg\">p.86<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>8 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> The Class C loss under Ryuuen is what still gnaws at her.<span class=\"pg\">p.86<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I think that it’s preferable for you to fall until you hit rock bottom,”<span class=\"pg\">p.86<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Voice<\/span> She calls out the island contradiction in his order-to-things advice; he admits it without explaining Chabashira.<span class=\"pg\">p.87<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You say there’s an order to things, but if that’s true, why did you go to all that trouble back on the island?”<span class=\"pg\">p.87<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> She has no clue about his dealings with Chabashira; that stays hidden.<span class=\"pg\">p.87<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “None of your business.”<span class=\"pg\">p.87<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I refuse.”<span class=\"pg\">p.87<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> She refuses to join the shopping trip; AK had known all along it would be her answer.<span class=\"pg\">p.87<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4_5-p60-1\">← Before: Ch.3: passing mentions<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4_5-p108-1\">→ After: Ch.4: the water bottle<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4_5-p108-1","v":"y1v4.5","y":1,"o":5,"k":"action spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune ch 4  the water bottle  place dormitory  she calls ak twice during the water outage and then goes silent  starting the chapter s worry  missed calls  read receipts without replies  then no read receipt at all on his last text   sorry for calling a bunch of times   no  i wasn t   i m kind of in the middle of something right now  a metallic thunk sounds on the line and she ends the call abruptly   there s something i wanted to ask you   let s say that there was a turtle   this would have been easier if you d just assumed that turtles can t get up on their own and listened to me   in such a situation  what would you do   i was just talking about a turtle on its back   i just wanted to talk to you about a turtle that flipped over   if you say that you can t prevent wanting to help people  then perhaps i can t go to you for advice   i m just having a little trouble   that s not it   i ll tell you everything   could you come to my room   i understand  but to deal with this  you need to be here   i know  but i can t do this unless you re here  she hangs up without another word  leaving him to decide whether to come  she calls him past nine rather than anyone else on the floor   even if someone came in right now  i d conk them with my right hand   once you see  you ll understand  she turns to show her right hand completely stuck inside a small water bottle   don t be dumb   it wasn t funny because i was teasing you  right   this water bottle got stuck because i tried to wash my hand   let s get this over with quickly  exhausted from two hours of trying alone  she resigns herself to being stuck when the pull fails   did you forget that there s a water outage right now   pass   i m opposed to using any water they might have  she braces her right arm for a second pull  sweating through the pain   yes  even if it hurts","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4_5-p108-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.4: the water bottle<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4.5 · p.108–119<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">[place:dormitory] She calls AK twice during the water outage and then goes silent, starting the chapter&#x27;s worry.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “Sorry for calling a bunch of times.”<span class=\"pg\">p.111<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“No, I wasn’t.”<span class=\"pg\">p.111<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I’m kind of in the middle of something right now,”<span class=\"pg\">p.111<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>30 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Missed calls, read receipts without replies, then no read receipt at all on his last text.<span class=\"pg\">p.108–110<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> A metallic thunk sounds on the line and she ends the call abruptly.<span class=\"pg\">p.111<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “There’s something I wanted to ask you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.112<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Let’s say that there was a turtle,”<span class=\"pg\">p.112<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “This would have been easier if you’d just assumed that turtles can’t get up on their own and listened to me,”<span class=\"pg\">p.113<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “In such a situation, what would you do?”<span class=\"pg\">p.113<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I was just talking about a turtle on its back.”<span class=\"pg\">p.113<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I just…wanted to talk to you about a turtle that flipped over,”<span class=\"pg\">p.113<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If you say that you can’t prevent wanting to help people, then perhaps I can’t go to you for advice,”<span class=\"pg\">p.113<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m just having a little trouble.”<span class=\"pg\">p.113<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s not it.”<span class=\"pg\">p.114<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’ll tell you everything.”<span class=\"pg\">p.114<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Could you come to my room?”<span class=\"pg\">p.114<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I understand, but…to deal with this, you need to be here.”<span class=\"pg\">p.114<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I know, but I can’t do this unless you’re here,”<span class=\"pg\">p.114<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> She hangs up without another word, leaving him to decide whether to come.<span class=\"pg\">p.114<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> She calls him past nine rather than anyone else on the floor.<span class=\"pg\">p.114<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Even if someone came in right now, I’d conk them with my right hand,”<span class=\"pg\">p.115<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Once you see, you’ll understand.”<span class=\"pg\">p.115<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> She turns to show her right hand completely stuck inside a small water bottle.<span class=\"pg\">p.115<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Don’t be dumb.”<span class=\"pg\">p.116<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It wasn’t funny because I was teasing you, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.116<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “This water bottle got stuck because I tried to wash my hand.”<span class=\"pg\">p.116<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Let’s get this over with quickly,”<span class=\"pg\">p.116<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Exhausted from two hours of trying alone, she resigns herself to being stuck when the pull fails.<span class=\"pg\">p.116<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Did you forget that there’s a water outage right now?”<span class=\"pg\">p.118<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Pass,”<span class=\"pg\">p.119<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m opposed to using any water they might have.”<span class=\"pg\">p.119<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> She braces her right arm for a second pull, sweating through the pain.<span class=\"pg\">p.119<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yes. Even if it hurts,”<span class=\"pg\">p.119<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4_5-p86-1\">← Before: Ch.3: the bench conversation<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4_5-p120-1\">→ After: Ch.4: refused help and the way home<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4_5-p120-1","v":"y1v4.5","y":1,"o":5,"k":"action spoken","w":"kushida-kikyou horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune ch 4  refused help and the way home cornered by the outage  she refuses hirata s water to avoid a debt and vetoes kushida on sight   i wouldn t have any concerns about the quality of hirata s water  but i dislike the idea of owing him a debt   please ask sakura san   there s no reason for us to get along   she abandoned the idea of trying to win right from the start   kushida being our group s vip gave class d the advantage   therefore  i assume she s guilty   don t be absurd   you re talking about very complicated things   i accept the test results   honestly  today is just not my day   if i planned to wait  i wouldn t have called you   this is not my day   i really can t go outside like this   that was completely unnecessary   will a bath towel do   rejected   can t you think of anything better   i suppose so   i d rather take the stairs than let someone see me   that s maezono san s room   there s no need for us to linger   nothing s wrong  she refuses kushida s water without a word  pressing the bottle into ak s back  the water kushida offers is the one thing horikita wants most and will not take from her   at this rate  they re going to see us   we have no choice now but to use the elevator   since we know the camera s position  we should be able to do that   i ll just endure this bottle until the water comes back  kouenji boards at the fifth floor  she hides in the camera s blind spot behind ak   walking around outside is completely out of the question   however  please don t tell sakura san about me  she nearly swings the bottle at the commemorative photo joke   honestly  this day was a complete disaster   please don t speak a word of this to anyone   thank you   shut up","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4_5-p120-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.4: refused help and the way home<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4.5 · p.120–131<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Cornered by the outage, she refuses Hirata&#x27;s water to avoid a debt and vetoes Kushida on sight.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“I wouldn’t have any concerns about the quality of Hirata’s water, but…I dislike the idea of owing him a debt,”<span class=\"pg\">p.120<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Please ask Sakura-san,”<span class=\"pg\">p.120<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“There’s no reason for us to get along.”<span class=\"pg\">p.120<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>33 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “She abandoned the idea of trying to win right from the start.”<span class=\"pg\">p.120<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Kushida being our group’s VIP gave Class D the advantage.”<span class=\"pg\">p.121<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Therefore, I assume she’s guilty.”<span class=\"pg\">p.121<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Don’t be absurd.”<span class=\"pg\">p.121<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You’re talking about very complicated things,”<span class=\"pg\">p.122<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I accept the test results.”<span class=\"pg\">p.122<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Honestly, today is just not my day,”<span class=\"pg\">p.122<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If I planned to wait, I wouldn’t have called you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.122<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “This is not my day,”<span class=\"pg\">p.123<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I really can’t go outside like this,”<span class=\"pg\">p.123<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That was completely unnecessary,”<span class=\"pg\">p.123<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Will a bath towel do?”<span class=\"pg\">p.123<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Rejected.”<span class=\"pg\">p.124<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Can’t you think of anything better?”<span class=\"pg\">p.124<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I suppose so.”<span class=\"pg\">p.124<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’d rather take the stairs than let someone see me,”<span class=\"pg\">p.125<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s Maezono-san’s room.”<span class=\"pg\">p.125<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “There’s no need for us to linger,”<span class=\"pg\">p.126<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Nothing’s wrong!”<span class=\"pg\">p.126<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> She refuses Kushida&#x27;s water without a word, pressing the bottle into AK&#x27;s back.<span class=\"pg\">p.127<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> The water Kushida offers is the one thing Horikita wants most and will not take from her.<span class=\"pg\">p.127<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “At this rate, they’re going to see us,”<span class=\"pg\">p.128<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “We have no choice now but to use the elevator!”<span class=\"pg\">p.128<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Since we know the camera’s position, we should be able to do that,”<span class=\"pg\">p.128<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’ll just endure this bottle until the water comes back,”<span class=\"pg\">p.129<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Kouenji boards at the fifth floor; she hides in the camera&#x27;s blind spot behind AK.<span class=\"pg\">p.129<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Walking around outside is completely out of the question,”<span class=\"pg\">p.130<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “However, please don’t tell Sakura-san about me,”<span class=\"pg\">p.130<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> She nearly swings the bottle at the commemorative-photo joke.<span class=\"pg\">p.130<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Honestly, this day was a complete disaster,”<span class=\"pg\">p.131<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Please don’t speak a word of this to anyone.”<span class=\"pg\">p.131<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Thank you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.131<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Shut up,”<span class=\"pg\">p.131<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4_5-p108-1\">← Before: Ch.4: the water bottle<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4_5-p132-1\">→ After: Ch.5: a passing mention<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4_5-p132-1","v":"y1v4.5","y":1,"o":5,"k":"","w":"yamauchi-haruki sakura-airi horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune ch 5  a passing mention yamauchi s old phone number bargain damaged his perceived market value in her eyes  that embarrassment is why ak judges he owes yamauchi one  sakura s first worry on receiving the letter is whether horikita will be angry  she never appears on the page  her would be reaction is ak s guess of an exasperated sigh","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4_5-p132-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.5: a passing mention<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4.5 · p.132, 141<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Yamauchi&#x27;s old phone-number bargain damaged his perceived market value in her eyes.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"yamauchi-haruki.html\">Yamauchi Haruki<\/a> · <a href=\"sakura-airi.html\">Sakura Airi<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yamauchi Haruki<\/b> That embarrassment is why AK judges he owes Yamauchi one.<span class=\"pg\">p.132<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> Sakura&#x27;s first worry on receiving the letter is whether Horikita will be angry.<span class=\"pg\">p.141<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> She never appears on the page; her would-be reaction is AK&#x27;s guess of an exasperated sigh.<span class=\"pg\">p.141<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4_5-p120-1\">← Before: Ch.4: refused help and the way home<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4_5-p160-1\">→ After: Ch.6: passing mentions<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4_5-p160-1","v":"y1v4.5","y":1,"o":5,"k":"","w":"horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune ch 6  passing mentions her name runs through the outing plans  the pool pairings  and the sunset walk  the four guy outing is announced alongside her name in the plans  and the combination is called bizarre  a line urges asking her directly  on the grounds that ayanokoji is close to her  karuizawa measures herself against her through the rest area argument  the pairing talk sends sudou with her  and sudou asks whether she will come  ike worries aloud about the others seeing suzune sad or defenseless  she is named among the girls who assemble at the pool","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4_5-p160-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6: passing mentions<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4.5 · p.160–163, 170, 175<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Her name runs through the outing plans, the pool pairings, and the sunset walk.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The four-guy outing is announced alongside her name in the plans, and the combination is called bizarre.<span class=\"pg\">p.160<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> A line urges asking her directly, on the grounds that Ayanokōji is close to her.<span class=\"pg\">p.161<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Karuizawa measures herself against her through the rest-area argument.<span class=\"pg\">p.162<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The pairing talk sends Sudou with her, and Sudou asks whether she will come.<span class=\"pg\">p.163<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Ike worries aloud about the others seeing Suzune sad or defenseless.<span class=\"pg\">p.170<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> She is named among the girls who assemble at the pool.<span class=\"pg\">p.175<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4_5-p132-1\">← Before: Ch.5: a passing mention<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4_5-p164-1\">→ After: Ch.6: coerced to the pool<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4_5-p164-1","v":"y1v4.5","y":1,"o":5,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune ch 6  coerced to the pool ak s water bottle leverage turns her refusal into an 8 30 lobby attendance   what do you want   i refuse   you have a very unpleasant phone manner   okay  what do you need me to do tomorrow  and at what time   understood  but i won t forgive you if you ever try this again  she reads the water bottle line as cashing in a favor and complies to protect her reputation   you just barely made it  huh   the elevator s really swamped  right   he probably overslept   did something happen to him   don t tell me that   don t you think this is a little strange   did something occur to you  sudou kun   i can t help but think they have ulterior motives   even though they shouldn t have brought anything with them except towels and swimsuits  that bag looks really heavy   just look at the bag   i see  i suppose that s credible   you gained points through personal activities   the day when you contribute more significantly to the class might be near","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4_5-p164-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6: coerced to the pool<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4.5 · p.164–169<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">AK&#x27;s water-bottle leverage turns her refusal into an 8:30 lobby attendance.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“What do you want?”<span class=\"pg\">p.164<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I refuse,”<span class=\"pg\">p.164<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“You have a very unpleasant phone manner.”<span class=\"pg\">p.164<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>16 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Okay. What do you need me to do tomorrow, and at what time?”<span class=\"pg\">p.165<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Understood. But I won’t forgive you if you ever try this again,”<span class=\"pg\">p.165<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> She reads the water-bottle line as cashing in a favor and complies to protect her reputation.<span class=\"pg\">p.165<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You just barely made it, huh?”<span class=\"pg\">p.166<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “The elevator’s really swamped, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.166<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “He probably overslept,”<span class=\"pg\">p.166<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Did something happen to him?”<span class=\"pg\">p.167<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Don’t tell me that,”<span class=\"pg\">p.168<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Don’t you think this is a little strange?”<span class=\"pg\">p.168<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Did something occur to you, Sudou-kun?”<span class=\"pg\">p.168<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I can’t help but think they have ulterior motives,”<span class=\"pg\">p.168<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Even though they shouldn’t have brought anything with them except towels and swimsuits, that bag looks really heavy.”<span class=\"pg\">p.168<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Just look at the bag,”<span class=\"pg\">p.168<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I see. I suppose that’s credible,”<span class=\"pg\">p.169<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You gained points through personal activities?”<span class=\"pg\">p.169<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “The day when you contribute more significantly to the class might be near,”<span class=\"pg\">p.169<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4_5-p160-1\">← Before: Ch.6: passing mentions<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4_5-p179-1\">→ After: Ch.6: her brother&#x27;s shadow and the sunset walk<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4_5-p179-1","v":"y1v4.5","y":1,"o":5,"k":"spoken","w":"nagumo-miyabi ichinose-honami ayanokouji-kiyotaka horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune ch 6  her brother s shadow and the sunset walk horikita stiffens at the student council talk  argues ichinose over class placement  plays to win the volleyball bet  and stays behind for a sunset walk with ayanokoji  the vice president s name tightens her shoulders  and she praises the president in front of others without revealing he is her brother   i m sure the student council president would easily surpass him in any activity   you re quite well informed  aren t you  replied horikita   he had a delayed start  she spat   isn t it obvious  horikita said without hesitation   so  you re saying there s a problem with me overall   i can t believe that  said horikita in a low voice   those are separate issues   it s not  running away  when it s just a simple game  snapped horikita   fine  let s do it  said horikita   since we re doing this  we re going to win  said horikita   to buy lunch for this many people  you might have to spend up to 10 000 points  she trades barbs with ichinose over class sorting and accepts the lunch at stakes bet as if it were a special test   you re not really bad at sports  are you  she observed   you re not going to show your hand yet  then   that s because he has a face like a doll   surprisingly  i had fun today   that s a secret  she does not take the elevator  invites him for a walk  and hints at a secret about what she was able to do during vacation","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4_5-p179-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6: her brother&#x27;s shadow and the sunset walk<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4.5 · p.179–204<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Horikita stiffens at the student council talk, argues Ichinose over class placement, plays to win the volleyball bet, and stays behind for a sunset walk with Ayanokōji.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"nagumo-miyabi.html\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/a> · <a href=\"ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a> · <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“I&#x27;m sure the student council president would easily surpass him in any activity.”<span class=\"pg\">p.179<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“You&#x27;re quite well-informed, aren&#x27;t you?” replied Horikita.<span class=\"pg\">p.180<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“He had a delayed start,” she spat.<span class=\"pg\">p.181<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>16 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/b> The vice president&#x27;s name tightens her shoulders, and she praises the president in front of others without revealing he is her brother.<span class=\"pg\">p.179<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Isn&#x27;t it obvious?” Horikita said without hesitation.<span class=\"pg\">p.181<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “So, you&#x27;re saying there&#x27;s a problem with me overall?”<span class=\"pg\">p.181<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I can&#x27;t believe that,” said Horikita in a low voice.<span class=\"pg\">p.181<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Those are separate issues.”<span class=\"pg\">p.181<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It&#x27;s not &#x27;running away&#x27; when it&#x27;s just a simple game,” snapped Horikita.<span class=\"pg\">p.182<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Fine. Let&#x27;s do it,” said Horikita.<span class=\"pg\">p.183<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Since we&#x27;re doing this, we&#x27;re going to win,” said Horikita.<span class=\"pg\">p.183<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “To buy lunch for this many people, you might have to spend up to 10,000 points.”<span class=\"pg\">p.183<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> She trades barbs with Ichinose over class sorting and accepts the lunch-at-stakes bet as if it were a special test.<span class=\"pg\">p.181–183<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You&#x27;re not really bad at sports, are you?” she observed.<span class=\"pg\">p.190<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You&#x27;re not going to show your hand yet, then.”<span class=\"pg\">p.190<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That&#x27;s because he has a face like a doll.”<span class=\"pg\">p.201<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Surprisingly, I had fun today.”<span class=\"pg\">p.204<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That&#x27;s a secret.”<span class=\"pg\">p.204<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> She does not take the elevator, invites him for a walk, and hints at a secret about what she was able to do during vacation.<span class=\"pg\">p.203–204<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4_5-p164-1\">← Before: Ch.6: coerced to the pool<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4_5-p206-1\">→ After: Ch.7: passing mentions<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4_5-p206-1","v":"y1v4.5","y":1,"o":5,"k":"","w":"horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune ch 7  passing mentions the victory talk  the monitor  and the locker room keep her name in the foreground  sudou credits the island win to her  and another line counts having her on their side toward class c  through the poor quality feed  she and the others are visible  at the lockers she speaks to no one in particular and only glances at kushida  the scene closes with a wish to see her naked body","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4_5-p206-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.7: passing mentions<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4.5 · p.206, 213, 220, 222<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">The victory talk, the monitor, and the locker room keep her name in the foreground.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Sudou credits the island win to her, and another line counts having her on their side toward Class C.<span class=\"pg\">p.206<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Through the poor-quality feed, she and the others are visible.<span class=\"pg\">p.213<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> At the lockers she speaks to no one in particular and only glances at Kushida.<span class=\"pg\">p.220<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The scene closes with a wish to see her naked body.<span class=\"pg\">p.222<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4_5-p179-1\">← Before: Ch.6: her brother&#x27;s shadow and the sunset walk<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4_5-p215-1\">→ After: Ch.7: the recorded changing room<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4_5-p215-1","v":"y1v4.5","y":1,"o":5,"k":"spoken","w":"ichinose-honami horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune ch 7  the recorded changing room she appears in the recorded footage changing with the others and cannot explain to anyone why she came along   ichinose san  could you please not stare at me  said horikita   i m not here because i like this kind of thing  she will not tell anyone how ayanokoji called in a favor   the water bottle humiliation goes to her grave   why don t you try changing without talking to me  she retorted   when did you get those breasts   that must be why you don t know what to do with them  she watches ichinose s graceless undressing for a moment despite herself   she s like a human typhoon  isn t she  said horikita","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4_5-p215-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.7: the recorded changing room<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4.5 · p.215–219<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">She appears in the recorded footage changing with the others and cannot explain to anyone why she came along.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Ichinose-san, could you please not stare at me?” said Horikita.<span class=\"pg\">p.215<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I’m not here because I like this kind of thing.”<span class=\"pg\">p.215<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Why don’t you try changing without talking to me?” she retorted.<span class=\"pg\">p.218<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> She will not tell anyone how Ayanokōji called in a favor — the water-bottle humiliation goes to her grave.<span class=\"pg\">p.218<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “When did you get those breasts?”<span class=\"pg\">p.219<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That must be why you don’t know what to do with them.”<span class=\"pg\">p.219<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> She watches Ichinose’s graceless undressing for a moment despite herself.<span class=\"pg\">p.219<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “She’s like a human typhoon, isn’t she?” said Horikita.<span class=\"pg\">p.219<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v4_5-p206-1\">← Before: Ch.7: passing mentions<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v5-p13-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"spoken","w":"karuizawa-kei horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune ch 2  the zodiac debrief at pallet at pallet with hirata  karuizawa and ayanokoji  she walks the rabbit group through the alphabetical vip rule and the cruise ship exam s logic   if you put the names of the students in the rabbit group in alphabetical order  it would be ayanokouji kun  ichinose san  ibuki san  and then karuizawa san  confirms karuizawa s dragon group deduction   kushida fifth   and explains why the pattern was hard to see mid exam   though it appears that ryuuen kun rules class c alone  perhaps that isn t actually true   a rebellious student must ve tossed out the wrong answer in direct defiance of ryuuen kun   that said  you evaded ryuuen kun s clutches quite well    aims it at karuizawa   unnecessary    refuses hirata s proposal to rope kushida in   i won t deny the fact that she has certain skills  but we can do anything she can on our own   those who claim that they have no presence usually cast long shadows   do you take me for a fool    stung by ayanokoji s no presence bait  not joking","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v5-p13-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2: the zodiac debrief at Pallet<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.13–15<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">At Pallet with Hirata, Karuizawa and Ayanokōji, she walks the rabbit group through the alphabetical VIP rule and the cruise-ship exam’s logic.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“If you put the names of the students in the rabbit group in alphabetical order, it would be Ayanokouji-kun, Ichinose-san, Ibuki-san, and then Karuizawa-san,”<span class=\"pg\">p.13<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Though it appears that Ryuuen-kun rules Class C alone, perhaps that isn’t actually true.”<span class=\"pg\">p.14<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“A rebellious student must’ve tossed out the wrong answer in direct defiance of Ryuuen-kun.”<span class=\"pg\">p.14<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> Confirms Karuizawa’s dragon-group deduction — Kushida fifth — and explains why the pattern was hard to see mid-exam.<span class=\"pg\">p.13<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That said, you evaded Ryuuen-kun’s clutches quite well.” — aims it at Karuizawa.<span class=\"pg\">p.14<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Unnecessary,” — refuses Hirata’s proposal to rope Kushida in.<span class=\"pg\">p.15<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I won’t deny the fact that she has certain skills, but we can do anything she can on our own.”<span class=\"pg\">p.15<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Those who claim that they have no presence usually cast long shadows,”<span class=\"pg\">p.15<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Do you take me for a fool?” — stung by Ayanokōji’s no-presence bait; not joking.<span class=\"pg\">p.15<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v5-p16-1\">→ After: Ch.2 §2.1: the briefing and the huddle<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v5-p16-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"action spoken","w":"horikita-manabu horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune ch 2  2 1  the briefing and the huddle in homeroom she spots the testing method on the handout before most of the class and calls ayanokoji over  at the mention that class a   her brother s year   rides the same red team  she mutters at ayanokoji to drop it   don t talk about that here  after hirata s practical questions she raises her own  what happens on the day if someone is absent from a group competition   well  how many points are needed to assign a substitute  sudou  ike and yamauchi corner her in the free homeroom period to argue the festival strategy   why do only guys like these come to me   that s not a valid opinion    shuts down ike s fun and win line at once   within our class  you stand out as someone with superior athletic skill    concedes sudou s claim on the recommended events   stamina isn t an unlimited resource    her counter to entering sudou in everything   we re not coming to any decisions right now    ends the huddle without a decision","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v5-p16-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2 §2.1: the briefing and the huddle<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.16–25<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">In homeroom she spots the testing method on the handout before most of the class and calls Ayanokōji over. Sudou, Ike and Yamauchi corner her in the free homeroom period to argue the festival strategy.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-manabu.html\">Horikita Manabu<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Don’t talk about that here,”<span class=\"pg\">p.17<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Well, how many points are needed to assign a substitute?”<span class=\"pg\">p.23<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Why do only guys like these come to me?”<span class=\"pg\">p.23<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Manabu<\/b> At the mention that Class A — her brother’s year — rides the same Red Team, she mutters at Ayanokōji to drop it.<span class=\"pg\">p.17<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> After Hirata’s practical questions she raises her own: what happens on the day if someone is absent from a group competition?<span class=\"pg\">p.22<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s not a valid opinion.” — shuts down Ike’s fun-and-win line at once.<span class=\"pg\">p.24<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Within our class, you stand out as someone with superior athletic skill.” — concedes Sudou’s claim on the recommended events.<span class=\"pg\">p.24<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Stamina isn’t an unlimited resource.” — her counter to entering Sudou in everything.<span class=\"pg\">p.24<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “We’re not coming to any decisions right now.” — ends the huddle without a decision.<span class=\"pg\">p.25<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v5-p13-1\">← Before: Ch.2: the zodiac debrief at Pallet<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v5-p26-1\">→ After: Ch.2 §2.2: the assembly and the coin<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v5-p26-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-manabu katsuragi-kouhei ayanokouji-kiyotaka ryuuen-kakeru ichinose-honami horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune ch 2  2 2  the assembly and the coin in gymnasium 1 she scans restlessly for her brother  he never takes red team command  and fujimaki does instead  has never gone to meet him first   he always initiates contact   and cannot spot him in the crowd of four hundred  gets his warning about ryuuen and answers with a pointed question about personal experience  he leaves it at  i ve warned you  pulls him into the strategy question   what factor besides athleticism decides the festival   and gets  mere luck  for her trouble   i m not talking about random chance  though    wants a definite method  not luck  carries shame over her island mistakes  the narration reads her as even more obsessed with victory   different  i think it s the same kind of special exam    against ayanokoji s distinction   i definitely want class d to win    retort when he says she wants loopholes  not preparation   so  you re saying that we need to fight clean and fight hard to win   wait  are you saying that classes b and c are working together behind the scenes   but if that s true  it s crazy    can t believe ryuuen could have a plan already   fine  do enlighten me    swallows the rudeness and asks to be set straight  defends her b and c reading against his push  she thinks a behind the scenes deal is unlikely  suggests ichinose might set aside her feelings and cooperate with ryuuen for victory   ayanokoji calls the view too small","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v5-p26-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2 §2.2: the assembly and the coin<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.26–34<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">In Gymnasium 1 she scans restlessly for her brother; he never takes Red Team command, and Fujimaki does instead.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-manabu.html\">Horikita Manabu<\/a> · <a href=\"katsuragi-kouhei.html\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/a> · <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“I’m not talking about random chance, though,” — wants a definite method, not luck.<span class=\"pg\">p.32<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Different? I think it’s the same kind of special exam.” — against Ayanokōji’s distinction.<span class=\"pg\">p.32<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I definitely want Class D to win,” — retort when he says she wants loopholes, not preparation.<span class=\"pg\">p.33<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>10 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Manabu<\/b> Has never gone to meet him first — he always initiates contact — and cannot spot him in the crowd of four hundred.<span class=\"pg\">p.26<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> Gets his warning about Ryuuen and answers with a pointed question about personal experience; he leaves it at “I’ve warned you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.28<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Pulls him into the strategy question — what factor besides athleticism decides the festival — and gets “Mere luck?” for her trouble.<span class=\"pg\">p.31<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Carries shame over her island mistakes; the narration reads her as even more obsessed with victory.<span class=\"pg\">p.32<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “So, you’re saying that we need to fight clean and fight hard to win?”<span class=\"pg\">p.33<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Wait. Are you saying that Classes B and C are working together behind the scenes?”<span class=\"pg\">p.34<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “But if that’s true, it’s crazy.” — can’t believe Ryuuen could have a plan already.<span class=\"pg\">p.34<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Fine, do enlighten me.” — swallows the rudeness and asks to be set straight.<span class=\"pg\">p.34<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Defends her B-and-C reading against his push; she thinks a behind-the-scenes deal is unlikely.<span class=\"pg\">p.34<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> Suggests Ichinose might set aside her feelings and cooperate with Ryuuen for victory — Ayanokōji calls the view too small.<span class=\"pg\">p.34<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v5-p16-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.1: the briefing and the huddle<\/button><\/div><\/article>"}];
